{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason","id":1040029,"title":"Was Earth FLAT before the Order of Reason?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T09:17:29-08:00","id":1040029,"title":"Was Earth FLAT before the Order of Reason?","content":"Many people and cultures believed that Earth was flat. And, since Consensus shape reality.. <br /> <br /> And what if one civilization believed in a round Earth, and another in a flat one?<br /> <br /> Is it possible that the Americas weren't just a new Continent on Earth... But another MATERIAL REALM, and that the Atlantic's &quot;edges&quot; were actually a spiritual division between different worlds... Separate &quot;reality bubbles&quot;... And when the Void Explorers &quot;discovered&quot; the Americas, they ACTUALLY travelled across an Umbral Sea and reached another New, Brave World? And after managing to spread Consensus upon the, literally OLD world and this NEW world, they've managed to bind both realities toghether in the same Realm?<br /> <br /> And don't know if that possibility could have any ground on the scenario, but it is an interesting possibility","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:53:51-08:00","id":1040058,"title":"","content":"That is my thinking on the history of Mage. It is far from universal though. A lot of people prefer the idea of a baseline reality that the Consensus only shifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:58:19-08:00","id":1040063,"title":"","content":"The Earth existed in a state of quantum flux in which it was flat, round, spherical, an oblate spheroid, cube-shaped, stacked on the back of a turtle, or floating in a blob of god-sperm simultaneously/none of the above until an observer believed in it hard enough and collapsed the quantum wave state for the duration of the observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:01:27-08:00","id":1040067,"title":"","content":"No, Pythagoras proved that the Earth was spherical in the 6th century BC and everyone with a shred of education from the British Isles to the Japanese Isles knew the world was round after the 3rd century BC due to the spread of information along the ancient trade networks. Before him, the Lapita culture of Polynesia knew that the Earth was spherical due to their exploration of the Pacific. In addition, the people of the Americas were not Ephemera, which is what would have been the case had America been another Material Realm (just like the 'inhabitants' of the Deep Umbra colonies of the Technocracy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:09:21-08:00","id":1040074,"title":"","content":"For once I agree with Aya on how things happened in reality. However, in Mage if the majority believed that the Earth was flat the the Earth was flat and it would be impossible for Pythagoras to come to a conclusion that the Earth is actually spherical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:17:30-08:00","id":1040079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040067#post1040067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Pythagoras proved...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Proved.&quot; By using the word prove, you're making assumptions that reality conforms to the scientific worldview (knowledge is obtained by proof rather than divine revelation, pure logical deduction, or what I saw when I tripped out on mushrooms, for instance) and that the baseline state of nature isn't subject to change and that the trigonometric data can best reasonably be explained by a spherical earth. And that it wasn't flat BEFORE he made his observations and didn't revert to being flat AFTER he made them. And also that it can't be both flat AND an oblate spheroid at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-29-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:32:17-08:00","id":1040084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040074#post1040074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For once I agree with Aya on how things happened in reality. However, in Mage if the majority believed that the Earth was flat the the Earth was flat and it would be impossible for Pythagoras to come to a conclusion that the Earth is actually spherical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Earth was flat for many people, but round for Pythagoras and the poliniseans.<br /> <br /> Those that believed Earth was flat, would drop from its edge, directly to some Umbra (into the Low Umbra perhaps?). Pythagoras and the poliniseans, would travel across the Atlantic, and instead of seeing the Edge of the world, would see the other &quot;side&quot; of Earth, on the Pacific, and would apear in the &quot;other end&quot; of the world's &quot;disc&quot;. Space is an illusion, after all.<br /> <br /> Andd those believing in giant turtles and eelephants, would see a turtle with the size of J\u00fapiter with 3 elephants on top of each the size of Uranus holding a flat Earth on their backs, as they fell in the primordial Umbral Sea...<br /> <br /> How would Pythagoras disappear from the Atlanttic and reach the Pac\u00edfic? Space connections between those seas, only acesdible by those that believe it so.<br /> <br /> About the Americas, it wouldn't be an EPHEMERAL world in the Umbra... Hell, the separation between matter and spirit is a recent event. At that time, its higly possible that &quot;other Earths&quot; existed... Actually, at least each continent were, in fact, A DIFFERENT world. Why didn't no one &quot;discovered&quot; the Australia before? Probably, because it were a separeted world. In such scenarios, the explorations of the VE made a lot more sense. And, it's even possible that some other worlds were left behind by our Earth... Maybe the Hollow Earth co","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:52:44-08:00","id":1040091,"title":"","content":"The separation of spirit and matter is an ancient event, predating the Imperium and the first War of Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:10:15-08:00","id":1040129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040091#post1040091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The separation of spirit and matter is an ancient event, predating the Imperium and the first War of Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>When are we talking here? 1000 BCE or 10,000 BCE?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:41:11-08:00","id":1040151,"title":"","content":"The Earth was never flat, because no significant body of people ever actually believed it. &quot;Flat Earth&quot; is, in the real world, a piece of propaganda that was invented to discredit specific groups (such as the Catholic Church) by trying to paint them as believing in ridiculous in things you can easily see are false.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the strongest &quot;evidence&quot; for there being historical flat earth believers is... that people drew maps of the world as flat discs. It's like saying that using a rectangular map of the world means you believe the world is a flat rectangle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Flat Earth&quot; myths in Mage only make sense as being exactly what they are in the real world: propaganda. Tools of the Order or Reason to attack mystics and eventually the religious elements of their own membership.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:43:24-08:00","id":1040154,"title":"","content":"I won't copy there my posts about the Earthly Foundations and baseline reality from the other topic.<br /> <br /> If you like the notion of a World, which is totally the product and on the whim of the beliefs of people and the Consensus, by all means, go for it! But that's not how the Setting is written.<br /> <br /> And even after that, as Heavy wrote, large swaths of people never really believed that the Earth was flat. That is one of the misconceptions of later people about earlier ones and civilizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-29-2017, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:14:26-08:00","id":1040168,"title":"","content":"The fact that the earth was flat didn't stopped Vampires,Mages and Fera reaching the new world many centuries before people in the western world accepted its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way I can't understand why so many seem to have problem grasping the concept of earthly foundations.<br /> <br /> Page 612<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Earthly Foundations: <b>Certain laws of Earth\u2019s reality<br /> physics are more or less fixed.</b> You can go against them,<br /> but no matter who you are or what you do, those efforts<br /> will almost certainly count as vulgar magick.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Technocratic Reality: Here, the laws of scientific<br /> technology dictate what is and is not acceptable within<br /> the zone.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Localized Reality: In certain flexible areas, reality<br /> depends more upon specific local beliefs than on a rigid<br /> set of rules.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Primal Reality: Technology holds little influence in<br /> Primal Reality places. The laws of mystic Old Ways still<br /> dominate what is and is not possible.<br /> In game terms, a given zone either accepts or rejects a<br /> mage\u2019s activities. The more she can play within the rules of a<br /> zone, the more successful she will be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some things are almost always vulgar, no matter who\u2019s doing them, where they\u2019re doing them, or how they\u2019re being done. I<b>n game terms, acts that violate these Earthly Foundations<br /> contradict the <span style=\"font-size:18px\">baseline reality</span> for Earth.</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 Sudden Large Alterations of Physical and Metaphysical Mass or Space: Stacking places on top of one another, disintegrating large structures, changing large masses of physical matter into large emissions of energy (i.e., explosions), radical transformations of one physical form into another (that is, people into stone or vampires into lawn chairs)\u2026 such things disrupt Reality on a<br /> fundamental level. Even when performed by technology, such large-scale alterations are never truly safe. The horrific consequences of nuclear detonation could be seen as manifestations of the Paradox Effect; so could environmental pollution, climate change, organ rejection, electromagnetic pulses, cancer, and other aftershocks of technological disruption. The bigger the Effect, the larger the consequences\u2026 and no matter who you are or how you work your magicks, no mage acts without consequences.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Obvious violations of normal physical laws:</b> Water running uphill, people flying around, free-floating molecules abruptly manifesting as solid mass, turtles suddenly moving at cheetah speed\u2026 such gross alterations of Earth\u2019s primary physical laws tend to incur Paradox. Certain long-term projects \u2013 like airplanes, flying ointments, and martial arts \u2013 might be able to bend those principles a bit, but the act of investing that much time, energy, and devotion to a task still recognizes that those principles exist. <b>Simply ignoring them \u2013 say, by jumping off a roof while believing you can fly \u2013 is a good way to get your ass kicked, either by Paradox (if you do fly) or by physics (if you don\u2019t).</b> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round Earth is part of the baseline reality of Earth, just as gravity: It's not like before Isaac Newton people could jump from the roof, because gravity was always there.<br /> <br /> Consensus doesn't shape everything, the base structure of the world is already in place, determined long before the Consensus.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:22:56-08:00","id":1040174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040151#post1040151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Earth was never flat, because no significant body of people ever actually believed it. &quot;Flat Earth&quot; is, in the real world, a piece of propaganda that was invented to discredit specific groups (such as the Catholic Church) by trying to paint them as believing in ridiculous in things you can easily see are false.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the strongest &quot;evidence&quot; for there being historical flat earth believers is... that people drew maps of the world as flat discs. It's like saying that using a rectangular map of the world means you believe the world is a flat rectangle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Flat Earth&quot; myths in Mage only make sense as being exactly what they are in the real world: propaganda. Tools of the Order or Reason to attack mystics and eventually the religious elements of their own membership.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I will agree with. Given the nature of belief is is far more likely that it had no shape and no set distance (or even relationship) between civilizations and landmasses.<br /> <br /> You know it is entirely possible there were civilizations and landmasses that were never incorporated into Earth, and instead formed connected worlds of their own. Food for thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040168#post1040168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the earth was flat didn't stopped Vampires,Mages and Fera reaching the new world many centuries before people in the western world accepted its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way I can't understand why so many seem to have problem grasping the concept of earthly foundations.<br /> <br /> Page 612<br /> [/B]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Round Earth is part of the baseline reality of Earth, just as gravity: It's not like before Isaac Newton people could jump from the roof, because gravity was always there.<br /> <br /> Consensus doesn't shape everything, the base structure of the world is already in place, determined long before the Consensus.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But what counts as an Earthly Foundation is up for debate. As is what Earthly Foundations actually are and if they are truly static. They are certainly a way out for players and STs who don't want to deal with a shapechanging earth, but the mere fact that M20 talks about them in no way indicates that the world was always the way it is now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:38:47-08:00","id":1040183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040168#post1040168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way I can't understand why so many seem to have problem grasping the concept of earthly foundations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect it's just they had a picture about the setting in their head about how it works and they like the idea of &quot;consensus shapes everything&quot; for various reasons. It's okay, nothing stops you to play in your personal version of the setting, but the official setting isn't that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:39:25-08:00","id":1040184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040183#post1040183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect it's just they had a picture about the setting in their head about how it works and they like the idea of &quot;consensus shapes everything&quot; for various reasons. It's okay, nothing stops you to play in your personal version of the setting, but the official setting isn't that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can say the exact same thing to you, just switching out 'static reality' for 'consensus shapes everything'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:46:56-08:00","id":1040190,"title":"","content":"Cool, we've reached a deadlock.<br /> <br /> Let's go home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:50:41-08:00","id":1040194,"title":"","content":"Cite any parts from the books that confirms that the entire world is the product of consensus and that there aren't universally working rules as a baseline.<br /> <br /> As for M20, if the Earthly Foundations aren't independent from humanity and consensus, there weren't a reason to emphasize them. Yes, the book doesn't explicitly say that they were just like now since forever, but it also doesn't say that they're malleable. The fact that they are got highlighted in the book and works everywhere, regardless of reality zones indicates that they are universal.<br /> <br /> As for what are they exactly, I think the book is fairly clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:11:27-08:00","id":1040265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040194#post1040194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cite any parts from the books that confirms that the entire world is the product of consensus and that there aren't universally working rules as a baseline.<br /> <br /> As for M20, if the Earthly Foundations aren't independent from humanity and consensus, there weren't a reason to emphasize them. Yes, the book doesn't explicitly say that they were just like now since forever, but it also doesn't say that they're malleable. The fact that they are got highlighted in the book and works everywhere, regardless of reality zones indicates that they are universal.<br /> <br /> As for what are they exactly, I think the book is fairly clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. I'm not getting into this with yet another person who thinks they've found the one true way of playing Mage. Your way is absolutely consistent with Mage as written, but so is an Earth that is entirely mutable. That's why exactly what classifies as an Earthly Foundation and how strong they are is deliberately vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:01:40-08:00","id":1040295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040265#post1040265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, no. I'm not getting into this with yet another person who thinks they've found the one true way of playing Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mistaken. I never said that my interpretation, or the writers intention is the only true way to play mage. I explicitly said here, on on the other topic, that an entirely malleable reality is a perfectly good way to play the game, if one wants. It's a game, you do as you and your party see fit.<br /> <br /> However, when people are claiming statements about the setting, or the game in general, like why the Union is absolutely necessary and good, or why the game is incompatible with other lines and making those claims based not on the setting and game as written, but on their personal interpretations and headcanons, well, that's how you get misinformation and misconceptions. Basicaly, I frequently feel that people are not arguing with me, they are arguing with the authors. That's okay, you could love and play the game, while not agreeing with the authors', or a specific author's vision of it, but you should say clearly where you differ from the official material.<br /> <br /> When I'm writing on a public forum, I'm usually trying to stick to the setting as written, because that's the common ground, since we both read the same books presumably. But that's it, that doesn't mean, that's the only way to play the game. It just means, that when we're speaking about how such and such thing is, at first, we should base the conversation on the books as written. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your way is absolutely consistent with Mage as written, but so is an Earth that is entirely mutable. </div> </div> </div>Still waiting for proof, if you insist that it is in-line with the setting as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why exactly what classifies as an Earthly Foundation and how strong they are is deliberately vague. </div> </div> </div>Debatable. I think the book is fairly clear that the natural laws are basically the Foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:50:22-08:00","id":1040319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040295#post1040295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're mistaken. I never said that my interpretation, or the writers intention is the only true way to play mage. I explicitly said here, on on the other topic, that an entirely malleable reality is a perfectly good way to play the game, if one wants. It's a game, you do as you and your party see fit.<br /> <br /> However, when people are claiming statements about the setting, or the game in general, like why the Union is absolutely necessary and good, or why the game is incompatible with other lines and making those claims based not on the setting and game as written, but on their personal interpretations and headcanons, well, that's how you get misinformation and misconceptions. Basicaly, I frequently feel that people are not arguing with me, they are arguing with the authors. That's okay, you could love and play the game, while not agreeing with the authors', or a specific author's vision of it, but you should say clearly where you differ from the official material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is the thing a lot of people have problems with. Mage isn't consistent. There are multiple interpretations to large chunks of it. That's why we have the HAP/HOP divide and endless other discussions about the rules, setting, etc. Not even the writers are all on the same page, even when there is only one of them. So this isn't an issue where you can be right because there literally isn't a one true Mage the Ascension. There are multiple ways of looking at the game that do not differ from the official material (which is to say they ALL do, but within acceptable parameters).<br /> <br /> If you absolutely need a citation, though, I'll give you the only one I've seen that matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, pg 617</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change the Game and Change Your World<br /> The choice between those options belongs to each individual group and Storyteller. Mage, however, has always been dedicated to the idea of transformation. The very first tagline for Mage \u2013 one that was never actually published and which appeared only on the in-house drafts created by the original authors \u2013 was \u201cA Storytelling game of changing reality.\u201d And although that sentiment lacks the immediacy of Mage\u2019s other taglines, the idea that you CAN change the world is an essential element of the game.<br /> As Uncle Al said, do what you Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:12:51-08:00","id":1040337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040319#post1040319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is the thing a lot of people have problems with. Mage isn't consistent. There are multiple interpretations to large chunks of it. That's why we have the HAP/HOP divide and endless other discussions about the rules, setting, etc. Not even the writers are all on the same page, even when there is only one of them. So this isn't an issue where you can be right because there literally isn't a one true Mage the Ascension. There are multiple ways of looking at the game that do not differ from the official material (which is to say they ALL do, but within acceptable parameters).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's not 100% consistent, but I might say, it's fairly consistent. It's an organically evolved rpg setting, with a lot of authors, but certain things, like &quot;Was the World flat before the Consensus&quot; and the handling of such questions are reasonably consistent. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you absolutely need a citation, though, I'll give you the only one I've seen that matters. </div> </div> </div>Oh, but that doesn't prove that the default setting is the entirely malleable reality, it just say you could do with your personal game as you want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And again nothing's ban with that. You could love the idea of Mage, but with tweaks of your choice. Differing from the canon material is okay.<br /> <br /> However, when the argument goes:<br /> <br /> - Why the Union is the good guys?<br /> - Because without them and the Consensus there wouldn't be science or even gravity and we'd live in small bubbles of reality!<br /> - No, that's not true.<br /> - Yes it is.<br /> <br /> and so on, then, the best we could do is looking up what is the official default setting of the game as written and not personal versions of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:47:49-08:00","id":1040351,"title":"","content":"I just get an image in my mind that some people think that everything was in the Flux Realm before the Technocracy nailed everything down. As if we would not have written evidence from China, India, Europe, etc that nature did not work before 1200 AD. I think natural philosophers would have noted if 1 out of 10 people fell up into the sky when they were doing jumping exercises or the wood had an annoying habit of turning into butter when left-handed girls sneezed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:48:36-08:00","id":1040380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040351#post1040351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just get an image in my mind that some people think that everything was in the Flux Realm before the Technocracy nailed everything down. As if we would not have written evidence from China, India, Europe, etc that nature did not work before 1200 AD. I think natural philosophers would have noted if 1 out of 10 people fell up into the sky when they were doing jumping exercises or the wood had an annoying habit of turning into butter when left-handed girls sneezed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires came from the land of Nod. Right?<br /> <br /> Where is that place ON EARTH?<br /> <br /> Second, there were a great flood in the VAMPIRE WORLD.<br /> <br /> All those tales, do indeed support the idea of reality bubbles floating around on etherspace (or perhaps, ethersea and etheratmosphere, at that time).<br /> <br /> I mean, in the mythical ages, if you physicaly flew up, you would see angels hiding in the clouds (you would reach the High Umbra, just as much that you'll reach the Deep Umbra TODAY if you physically travel in the space).<br /> <br /> Also, where is Atl\u00e2ntida?<br /> <br /> The idea of &quot;reality bubbles&quot; actually makes ALL gamelines more fitting.<br /> <br /> So, the world of vampires truly were DESTROYED by a great flood... The lands of Nod, a kind of alternate Earth.<br /> <br /> Probably connected to the other Earths by the primal ethersea... That idea of an &quot;ethersea&quot;, also goes well with many myths of a primal, vastless Sea, upon which the world floated.<br /> <br /> So, for example, the Midgard Earth - the Earth of the Nords. It is possible, indeed, that this Earth were created by Odin and his brothers using the body of the primal Titan Ymir, the original Frost Giant. Egypt, however, were created for Ra.<br /> <br /> Now, like it happens on many Umbral realms, those parallel Earths have points of connection, and sometimes, overlapping. In the primitive Earth, when you crossed, physically, on foot, between Finland, Norway, etc, and reached South, you would enter the overlapping areas were Midgard have a connection with &quot;Olympus&quot; realm, during Roman time. At south, the &quot;realm of Olympus&quot; have overlaping with the &quot;reality&quot; of Babilonia and Egypt. Just as physically crossing the skies will send you to Umbral realms TODAY, crossing the Mediterranean would send you to a parallel Earth, one which had that quantic connection.<br /> <br /> In our REAL world, the gods of a Roman... Were in Rome. He praised Mercury for a safe travel... But, once in Egypt... It's no longer the land of the Roman Gods. A roman in Egypt would praise Isis and Horus. As would an egyption praise Jupiter in Rome.<br /> <br /> In the WoD, reality bubbles, or parallel earths, would account for ALL myths.<br /> <br /> And the land of Nod were a real place. And were destroyed by a great flood.<br /> <br /> And Atl\u00e2ntida were one of perhaps many earths lost in the past.<br /> <br /> Hell, crossing from one civilization to another WERE crossing to another &quot;world&quot;; they would have different critters, different spirits... We have Fae on ALL those Earths, however, Sidhe are mostly Europeans. While djins are EXCLUSIVE to the Middle East.<br /> <br /> What about Kuei Jins? That kind of thing didn't even existed in the West until VERY recently!!!<br /> <br /> If you go to the East, EVERYTHING changes... Their spirits are TOTALLY different. The critters are different. Why is the kuei jin phenomenon exclusive for for the East?<br /> <br /> Its almost as if... It were another reality... Another version of Earth...<br /> <br /> Why the Low Umbra in Africa have WILD ANIMALS? No animal turn into wraiths anywhere... Except in Africa.<br /> <br /> So, where is your &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; when you have mummy-like vampires in only ONE part of the world? Or maybe do you think that whole &quot;vampires are part of reality&quot; is bullshit? Do you think, by that logic, that Kuei Jin or the animal wraiths in Africa are one of those &quot;Earthly Foundation&quot;? If so... Why there are &quot;primal, unchangeable&quot;constants... Oh, but only for this piece of land over here... Or, perhaps, kuei jins are just a flimpsy trick of the Eastern Consensus? Because they don't seem to suffer from Paradox like Bygones anymore than the kindred do...<br /> <br /> So, the Earth were created by Odin, by Ra, by the Titans, by Tiamat, by Bhrama, and the land of Nod destroyed by Adonai, the God of the armies (the god of the hebrews). All true, at once.<br /> <br /> Until the Order of Reason kicked in, turning the metaphysical overlappings on the parsllel Earths into one single realm.<br /> <br /> Some alternate Earths were lost behind perhaps? Maybe, now there is still an Atl\u00e2ntida... But the techies forever cut the acces to it, with the Consensus on how the modern Earth is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:53:01-08:00","id":1040381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040337#post1040337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, but that doesn't prove that the default setting is the entirely malleable reality, it just say you could do with your personal game as you want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And again nothing's ban with that. You could love the idea of Mage, but with tweaks of your choice. Differing from the canon material is okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever, I've been on Mage forums long enough to see when someone is trying to start an argument, and calling classic interpretations non-canon is a dead giveaway. As is this atrociously bad strawman:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, when the argument goes:<br /> <br /> - Why the Union is the good guys?<br /> - Because without them and the Consensus there wouldn't be science or even gravity and we'd live in small bubbles of reality!<br /> - No, that's not true.<br /> - Yes it is.<br /> <br /> and so on, then, the best we could do is looking up what is the official default setting of the game as written and not personal versions of it. </div> </div> </div>Seriously, you are spending far too much time trying to write other people's arguments for them. There are much more productive ways of talking about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:06:18-08:00","id":1040382,"title":"","content":"I could just as easily say that &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; is just a &quot;unrefined&quot; Consensus. Its not like THERE WAS NO CONSENSUS, it just wasn't so ecstatic as today. <br /> <br /> Maybe, on &quot;parallel Earths&quot; were people INDEED felt into the sky... Those weird &quot;local Consensus&quot; were too far removed from the &quot;Olympian Earth&quot;, or the &quot;Midgard Earth&quot;, or the &quot;Middle Kingdom Earth&quot; (China) and all the others that make our Earth, to have connections.<br /> <br /> Hell, that could even explain why Atlantida, for example, disappeared without a trace... Maybe the atlanteans started having too weird ideas to remain connected to the other Earths... And so, their parallel spinned farther away in the etherspace, vanishing for us (but they may well still exist, in another quantum frequency... With weird physical laws to us).<br /> <br /> Hey, in the Demon game, wasn't Lucifer plotting to use humans faith to cut off the Abyss from the Tellurian or something like that? Or you wouldn't count THE ABYSS as one of those foundations?<br /> <br /> <br /> There is another thing: this &quot;Consensus&quot; that make reality, it may not be the solo work of humans. Before human kind, that could've been kept by the spirits. So, humans make the changes upon the spirits blueprints.<br /> <br /> That view would also support seing the Umbra on terms of &quot;up and down&quot;. Low Umbra, High Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:13:09-08:00","id":1040384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040337#post1040337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's not 100% consistent, but I might say, it's fairly consistent. It's an organically evolved rpg setting, with a lot of authors, but certain things, like &amp;quot;Was the World flat before the Consensus&amp;quot; and the handling of such questions are reasonably consistent. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, but that doesn't prove that the default setting is the entirely malleable reality, it just say you could do with your personal game as you want. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And again nothing's ban with that. You could love the idea of Mage, but with tweaks of your choice. Differing from the canon material is okay.<br /> <br /> However, when the argument goes:<br /> <br /> - Why the Union is the good guys?<br /> - Because without them and the Consensus there wouldn't be science or even gravity and we'd live in small bubbles of reality!<br /> - No, that's not true.<br /> - Yes it is.<br /> <br /> and so on, then, the best we could do is looking up what is the official default setting of the game as written and not personal versions of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying that the Union are the good guys for binding toghether all the former reality bubbles that floated in the ether. It is NOT a judgment of the Union, just an analizes of the settings of the world.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Parallel Earths would do better staying apart. I don't know, and don't care, that's not what is being discuss\u00f5es.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:44:34-08:00","id":1040392,"title":"","content":"What Parallel Earths? What book and page do you draw your assumptions that there were multiple parallel Earths that the OoR threaded together? Is there anything other than fluff or is this just fluff and headcannon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:46:15-08:00","id":1040393,"title":"","content":"I was tempted to go on about how vampire <b>mythology</b> is not absolute fact in VtM, so it has no place in this discussion of mage history.<br /> <br /> Then I realized that there's an argument that Nod is a physical place... which is hilarious. To live in the land of Nod means to live a nomadic life style, which was part of Cain's punishment because Cain was a farmer, and you can't farm as a nomad. It's why VtM's mythology dooms Caine (and his children) to never be able to maintain a civilization; he's cursed to wonder, and building a city to live in is avoiding his curse, so such cities are doomed. Even trying to just settle down with Lilith was painted as an effort that could never succeed.<br /> <br /> Anyway again:<br /> <br /> The official Mage books do not demonstrate that the world was split up into Reality Zones. All the different mythologies of the world exist in Mage for the same reasons the exist in reality: people tried to explain the world around them. The only difference is that in the WoD some of those myths are more empirically informed (because various supernatural forces do exist) than in the real world.<br /> <br /> If Mage's history started with some multiverse/etc. phenomenon, there is no explanation in any of the books about how in the Dark Ages a consistent reality formed, and then in the Renaissance Reality Zones had distinct metaphysical impact on magical practice from place to place. Meanwhile the Reality Zones the Order of Reason created so they could then merge them into the Consensus they wanted explains just fine why there's evidence of all these alternate mythologies (because the local Reality Zones created them) without the multiverse approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T20:53:28-08:00","id":1040397,"title":"","content":"And the Umbra of the Fera and the Dreaming of the Changelings pretty much explains any inconsistencies (Odin? Which Odin? We have one in each of the Near Umbra, one in the Deep Umbra, a dozen in the Deep Dreaming, and one hunting Garou in Scandinavia).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:10:52-08:00","id":1040401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040393#post1040393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was tempted to go on about how vampire <b>mythology</b> is not absolute fact in VtM, so it has no place in this discussion of mage history.<br /> <br /> Then I realized that there's an argument that Nod is a physical place... which is hilarious. To live in the land of Nod means to live a nomadic life style, which was part of Cain's punishment because Cain was a farmer, and you can't farm as a nomad. It's why VtM's mythology dooms Caine (and his children) to never be able to maintain a civilization; he's cursed to wonder, and building a city to live in is avoiding his curse, so such cities are doomed. Even trying to just settle down with Lilith was painted as an effort that could never succeed.<br /> <br /> Anyway again:<br /> <br /> The official Mage books do not demonstrate that the world was split up into Reality Zones. All the different mythologies of the world exist in Mage for the same reasons the exist in reality: people tried to explain the world around them. The only difference is that in the WoD some of those myths are more empirically informed (because various supernatural forces do exist) than in the real world.<br /> <br /> If Mage's history started with some multiverse/etc. phenomenon, there is no explanation in any of the books about how in the Dark Ages a consistent reality formed, and then in the Renaissance Reality Zones had distinct metaphysical impact on magical practice from place to place. Meanwhile the Reality Zones the Order of Reason created so they could then merge them into the Consensus they wanted explains just fine why there's evidence of all these alternate mythologies (because the local Reality Zones created them) without the multiverse approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consistent reality? Like the one that creates Kuei Jin ONLY amongst Easterners? Or the one that creates djinns (fae or spirit, who knows) only in middle east? Or the one that creates animal wraiths only on Africa? Or the one were ALL ananasi in the East are of the Wyrm? Or &quot;Les Invisibles&quot; only on the Caribbe? That doesn't seem &quot;consistent&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> About Cain, it was just an analogy. I said <i>it could be</i>. But just as much, it could be just myth (we know the 3rd generation is real, even if they keep saying &quot;no one knows&quot; in the setting, every player knows. But Cain... Well, Cain shows off at the end of the world, so... Yeah, whatever).<br /> <br /> About reality zones: Consensus weren't so rigid back in the day, to get to the point of creating &quot;reality zones&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, in the VtM, I've heard some people talking about &quot;how the antidiluvians survived the flood&quot;. So, it seems that the great flood is cannonical in VtM, which is really hard to fit with the other game if that's the case, but perhaps others could answer that with more bases than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-30-2017, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:20:18-08:00","id":1040405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040397#post1040397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Umbra of the Fera and the Dreaming of the Changelings pretty much explains any inconsistencies (Odin? Which Odin? We have one in each of the Near Umbra, one in the Deep Umbra, a dozen in the Deep Dreaming, and one hunting Garou in Scandinavia).</div> </div> </div> </div>ALL of them could've created the Midgard Earth.<br /> <br /> Or none of them. Who knows. That's just speculation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:42:29-08:00","id":1040416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040381#post1040381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever, I've been on Mage forums long enough to see when someone is trying to start an argument, and calling classic interpretations non-canon is a dead giveaway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still waiting for the exact proof from the books for those classic interpretations. I might add, proof, as: setting information written by the authors-as-authors, not legends from the mouth of in-world characters, but passages, where writers objectively described the fully malleable reality as the baseline of the setting.<br /> <br /> By the way, that some interpretations of the setting are classic doesn't make them official. Official setting is what it is. Oh, and I'm still not attacking personal headcanons and interpretations. Those are all good, but when we're speaking about the default setting, on the common ground of official material, I think it is better to stick with exactly that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As is this atrociously bad strawman:<br /> Seriously, you are spending far too much time trying to write other people's arguments for them. There are much more productive ways of talking about this. </div> </div> </div>With the intention of staying polite, sorry, but that was the (admittedly intentionally very rough) simplification of where to the argument boiled down and what ultimately brought up the whole discussion over the nature of reality. I skipped parts, yes and there were other arguments on the Union's side, but that was one of them and the one that completely derailed the conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, about mythologies and other stuff: what Heavy and Aya said.<br /> <br /> I might add that why should not different critters and spirits exist on different parts of the World? Lemures are living only on Madagascar. South-America doesn't have polar bears. Nature is diverse, why the supernatural landscape should be absolutely unified across the planet, without breaking the Foundations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:10:01-08:00","id":1040521,"title":"","content":"Because IRL, the differences in the species over the regions, is due to GEOGRAPHIC ISOLATION, caused by GEOGRAPHICAL BARRIERS (like mountains, or seas)<br /> <br /> Good for you to mention that. It just reinforce my point. Because, to have all those differences, you'll need SUPERNATURAL ISOLATION caused by SUPERNATURAL BARRIERS.<br /> <br /> EDIT: you can't have a set of laws written on stone... But them you have the &quot;exceptions&quot;. If you try to use biology in your argument, you'll do bad. For example, the water enviroment doesn't allow for creatures that aren't &quot;fish-like&quot;, eg hidrodynamics. Thats a Law set in Stone, no exceptions. That's why dolphins and sharks are so similar, despite one being a fish and the other a mammal. And in the air, you'll need wings. No matter if in the Amazonic rainforest, the Congo rainforest or in Australia. THAT is a nature's Law in our real world.<br /> <br /> Now, if all people that day stay dead or in the Low Umbra... Except in the China were they can come back as a different breed of Vampire... Well, that's not a Natural Law... That's not a &quot;Foundation&quot; upon which reality anchors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-30-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:20:59-08:00","id":1040526,"title":"","content":"And one other thing you're not taking in account: <b>Marauders</b>.<br /> <br /> Those guys say &quot;Fuck your Earthly Foundations!&quot;, and so they get fucked.<br /> <br /> Indeed, Marauders DO exist in their own personal Bubbles of reality. A bubble that distorts the CONSENSUAL reality around him. And, when he gets too alien, he literally SPIN AWAY ON THE ETHERSPACE, exactly like I said it could had happened to an hypotetical Atlantida, for example.<br /> <br /> You could try to say that to Marauders is just the work of their avatars, but it wouldn't be true; if it were, any and all bizarr effects he causes would cause pararox, and they would be ejected from reality almost immediatly, cuz their paradox would skyrocket. Also, their Avatars would need to do SEVERAL magiks at the same time, breaking one of the core rules of magik. Therefore, Marauders REALLY change reality... Even of what you could call &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot;<br /> <br /> keep insisting that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:31:33-08:00","id":1040556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040521#post1040521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because IRL, the differences in the species over the regions, is due to GEOGRAPHIC ISOLATION, caused by GEOGRAPHICAL BARRIERS (like mountains, or seas)</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't true. Species - in modern synthesis evolutionary biology - arise due to a number of factors. Isolation can be a factor, but is not always a factor or the sole factor. The key to a new species evolving is the way current species in a habitat respond to a change in the available ecological niches. Geographic isolation is a common source of new species because it correlates strongly to changes in the niche the common ancestor species inhabited previously. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good for you to mention that. It just reinforce my point. Because, to have all those differences, you'll need SUPERNATURAL ISOLATION caused by SUPERNATURAL BARRIERS. </div> </div> </div>Um, no. Not only does this make no sense, it completely misses the point.<br /> <br /> The point being made is that the Giant Panda only existing in Asia does not mean reality is inconsistent. Localized phenomena that arise out of the interaction of universal consistent rules means reality is consistent. The existence of localized supernatural creatures is not evidence of an inconsistent reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: you can't have a set of laws written on stone... But them you have the &quot;exceptions&quot;. </div> </div> </div>So... I take it you haven't studied much biology then. Life absolutely abhors attempts to set simple laws, and the laws of biology are riddled with exceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, the water enviroment doesn't allow for creatures that aren't &quot;fish-like&quot;, eg hidrodynamics. </div> </div> </div>I think squid, crabs, jellyfish, shrimp, sea slugs, coral, tunicates, sponges, urchins, kelp, water bears, sea otters, barnacles, a host of worms, and so on would all like a word with you about your assumptions about the diversity of life in aquatic environments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thats a Law set in Stone, no exceptions. That's why dolphins and sharks are so similar, despite one being a fish and the other a mammal. </div> </div> </div>Besides similar exterior shapes, sharks and cetaceans have incredibly different internal biology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in the air, you'll need wings. </div> </div> </div>You'd think so....but ballooning spiders don't have wings, or even adapt a body part to function as a wing (like many &quot;flying&quot; glider animals do). As their name suggests, they use their silk to float around in the air. Researchers in Antarctica sometimes find them because they can travel that far from their normal habitats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, if all people that day stay dead or in the Low Umbra... Except in the China were they can come back as a different breed of Vampire... Well, that's not a Natural Law... That's not a &quot;Foundation&quot; upon which reality anchors </div> </div> </div>Coming back from the dead happens across the world. Risen, Mummies, etc. are all similar phenomena to Kuei-jin. Kuei-jin are just called vampires because they are energy parasites instead of the other kind of dead-things-that-came-back. Kind of like how a &quot;daddy long legs&quot; is a name that refers to three completely different animals. Humans just named them all that because of a specific feature that stands out to us (they have really long legs in relation to their body compared to similar animals). The Kuei-jin are called vampires (so are Psychic Vampires!) despite having very little in common with Cainites besides being parasites on normal humans.<br /> <br /> As well, the Earthly Foundations are supposed to be things more on the scale of gravity. Essential basic laws that make the world function well enough for the Antrophic Principle to take hold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040526#post1040526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those guys say &quot;Fuck your Earthly Foundations!&quot;, and so they get fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. And you're just talking about actualized Marauders in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could try to say that to Marauders is just the work of their avatars, but it wouldn't be true; if it were, any and all bizarr effects he causes would cause pararox,... </div> </div> </div>And here's your problem. Marauders do cause Paradox. One of the things that makes them dangerous though, is that they tend to shunt their Paradox on other people instead of getting hit themselves.<br /> <br /> The rules for how lots of Paradox inducing effects brought on by the Marauder Quiet, and when that pushes them out of reality, is detailed in the books. So no, this point really doesn't go your way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:04:09-08:00","id":1040566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040067#post1040067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Pythagoras proved that the Earth was spherical in the 6th century BC and everyone with a shred of education from the British Isles to the Japanese Isles knew the world was round after the 3rd century BC due to the spread of information along the ancient trade networks. Before him, the Lapita culture of Polynesia knew that the Earth was spherical due to their exploration of the Pacific. In addition, the people of the Americas were not Ephemera, which is what would have been the case had America been another Material Realm (just like the 'inhabitants' of the Deep Umbra colonies of the Technocracy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree 100% on the first part. About the Americas, I believe Sorcerer's Crusade allowed room for the Horizon to exist in earth's geography (I.e. across the atlantic) and physical Earth to exist on both sides but Umbral weirdness in-between... iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-30-2017, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:41:35-08:00","id":1040587,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040416#post1040416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the intention of staying polite, sorry, but that was the (admittedly intentionally very rough) simplification of where to the argument boiled down and what ultimately brought up the whole discussion over the nature of reality. I skipped parts, yes and there were other arguments on the Union's side, but that was one of them and the one that completely derailed the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's surprising to see a highly subjective reality used to bolster the Technocracy. Usually it's used to show how much good work they stopped.<br /> <br /> I understand your frustration, though. These kind of arguments have been derailing threads since the 90s and they can be really annoying. In all that time, though, no one has managed to stop them with a quote war. That kind of thing only fans the flames precisely because two people can look at the same line and see very different things based on, if you'll forgive the term, the paradigm they are coming from. They can argue forever, all the time wondering why the other person keeps making strange interpretations when the real meaning is <i>so obvious</i>. Except it's not. It is based on our implicit assumptions.<br /> <br /> Already in this thread you've said several things that seem reasonable to you but scream subjective opinion (dare I say, headcanon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) to me. It's obvious you think the same thing about me, you've said as much. That cannot be solved with a citation battle; we're already looking at the same book. <br /> <br /> In my experience it is far more productive to discuss the assumptions we are making, why they appeal to us, and what they bring to Mage. We're not likely to convince each other, but we'll probably help other people in the process.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:08:23-08:00","id":1040832,"title":"","content":"Again, what Heavy wrote, I don't feel the need to repeat it, it basically covered all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040587#post1040587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's surprising to see a highly subjective reality used to bolster the Technocracy. Usually it's used to show how much good work they stopped.<br /> <br /> I understand your frustration, though. These kind of arguments have been derailing threads since the 90s and they can be really annoying. In all that time, though, no one has managed to stop them with a quote war. That kind of thing only fans the flames precisely because two people can look at the same line and see very different things based on, if you'll forgive the term, the paradigm they are coming from. They can argue forever, all the time wondering why the other person keeps making strange interpretations when the real meaning is <i>so obvious</i>. Except it's not. It is based on our implicit assumptions.<br /> <br /> Already in this thread you've said several things that seem reasonable to you but scream subjective opinion (dare I say, headcanon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) to me. It's obvious you think the same thing about me, you've said as much. That cannot be solved with a citation battle; we're already looking at the same book.<br /> <br /> In my experience it is far more productive to discuss the assumptions we are making, why they appeal to us, and what they bring to Mage. We're not likely to convince each other, but we'll probably help other people in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all that. We certainly wouldn't convince each other, so at this point let's just say that everyone's interpretation is perfectly valid for their own games and parts of the official setting aren't as well-defined, as they could be, probably intentionally. However, I'm on the opinion that they're not as ambiguous either, but that's indeed just my opinion.<br /> <br /> Individuals could decide on a case-by-case basis, which interpretation they feel closer to what is in the books and they don't even have to agree with the books if they don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:55:19-08:00","id":1040957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040832#post1040832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with all that. We certainly wouldn't convince each other, so at this point let's just say that everyone's interpretation is perfectly valid for their own games and parts of the official setting aren't as well-defined, as they could be, probably intentionally. However, I'm on the opinion that they're not as ambiguous either, but that's indeed just my opinion.<br /> <br /> Individuals could decide on a case-by-case basis, which interpretation they feel closer to what is in the books and they don't even have to agree with the books if they don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We can still get into the reasons why we think and prefer each side, by the way. Nothing is stopping us there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T16:03:25-08:00","id":1040960,"title":"","content":"It was flat back when the glowy dudes with the big gold swords were running around...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:39:58-08:00","id":1040993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't true. Species - in modern synthesis evolutionary biology - arise due to a number of factors. Isolation can be a factor, but is not always a factor or the sole factor. The key to a new species evolving is the way current species in a habitat respond to a change in the available ecological niches. Geographic isolation is a common source of new species because it correlates strongly to changes in the niche the common ancestor species inhabited previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, isolation creates new species because of genetic drift; after the isolation happens, the two populations that were only one, now will randomly have new mutations being added to the genetic pool, but those won't mix with one another. It's NOT about the new niche. Speciation (rise of new species) can happen in the same area, but it is far more uncommon, because to have that phenomenon, you need to halt the genetic mixing somehow between two groups (for example, in some specie of spiders with red and yellow females, all males brown, a mutation occurs that gives rise to a blue male; lets say the blue males only like yellow females (and vice versa) and the browns prefere the red (and vice versa). In time, a new species will rise).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, no. Not only does this make no sense, it completely misses the point.<br /> <br /> The point being made is that the Giant Panda only existing in Asia does not mean reality is inconsistent. Localized phenomena that arise out of the interaction of universal consistent rules means reality is consistent. The existence of localized supernatural creatures is not evidence of an inconsistent reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giant Panda only existing in Asia means that the BIOLOGICAL REALITY of Asia ONLY EXISTS IN ASIA.<br /> Put a Giant Panda in Antartica and see what happens.<br /> <br /> Of course, the real Umbra does not have Umbras to keep things afar, and the landmasses on our world are not parallel words connected by an umbral or etherial Sea.<br /> <br /> But, the Saara is a VERY different reality than the Amazon rainforest. Different weather, different humidit, diferent species, different soil. They ARE different worlds.<br /> <br /> And, althouth both have gravity, in both the oxigen oxidates things and in both the hot air goes up, and the Cold air goes down, there are an extensive number of different &quot;reality laws&quot;, if you wanna call them that. If you think not, you should know that you can take things like the dynamic of populations (the number of individuals, the area of dispersion of them, of any given species), and you can make them into MATHEMATICAL PATTERS. There is a mathematical f\u00f3rmula for all that. And the patterns that the species on the Saara have will be NOTHiNG like the pattern of the species on the Amazonia. But you can take completely different species from Amazonia, and they'll show similar patterns.<br /> <br /> Not only that: you can even turn the rate that new species arise in maths. And again, while ALL the species of Saara of a same close group (mammals, for example, or insects, or angiospermae) have THE SAME rate of time upon new species are formed, and the same can be said to the amazonic rainforest (so yes, new species of rats will arise in the same time frame of new species of whales), that pattern IS NOT the same for both Saara and Amazonia<br /> <br /> All that infers that different habitats have DIFFERENT ECOLOGICAL DYNAMISM<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it you haven't studied much biology then. Life absolutely abhors attempts to set simple laws, and the laws of biology are riddled with exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, it looks like you have absolutely no knowledge of biology AT ALL.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think squid, crabs, jellyfish, shrimp, sea slugs, coral, tunicates, sponges, urchins, kelp, water bears, sea otters, barnacles, a host of worms, and so on would all like a word with you about your assumptions about the diversity of life in aquatic environments.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, I was thinking only about vertabrates. I haven't been clear in that one because I didn't think I would need to, since I was clearly comparing sharks and dolphins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides similar exterior shapes, sharks and cetaceans have incredibly different internal biology.</div> </div> </div> </div>And?<br /> <br /> I was clearly talking about the hydrodynamics. You can make the strawman you like, just don't claim victory over it.<br /> <br /> To live on Sea, mammals had to look more like sharks. Pleissiosaurs and Ichtyossaurs, both families of &quot;reptiles&quot;, also had the same &quot;fish-like&quot; anatomy. Which shows the convenience of that form in the aquatic enviroment. What does their very different biochmestries have to do with any of it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd think so....but ballooning spiders don't have wings, or even adapt a body part to function as a wing (like many &amp;quot;flying&amp;quot; glider animals do). As their name suggests, they use their silk to float around in the air. Researchers in Antarctica sometimes find them because they can travel that far from their normal habitats.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? Once again, your point is? Well, perhaps you just like to make strawman<br /> <br /> Tell me, how many whales have you ever saw flying?<br /> <br /> You can't fly without specific adaptation. That's the central point of the argument - once again, &quot;strawman it&quot; if you will, but don't call it a &quot;win&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming back from the dead happens across the world. Risen, Mummies, etc. are all similar phenomena to Kuei-jin. Kuei-jin are just called vampires because they are energy parasites instead of the other kind of dead-things-that-came-back. Kind of like how a &amp;quot;daddy long legs&amp;quot; is a name that refers to three completely different animals. Humans just named them all that because of a specific feature that stands out to us (they have really long legs in relation to their body compared to similar animals). The Kuei-jin are called vampires (so are Psychic Vampires!) despite having very little in common with Cainites besides being parasites on normal humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>And... Surprise surprise! More strawman!!!<br /> <br /> Yep, risen and mummies happens everywhere. And? Your point is?<br /> <br /> First of all... What is the matter the taxonomic supernatural group that Kuei Jin occupy to the points <u>you're trying to disprove</u>?<br /> <br /> Second: are <u>Kuei Jins</u> a natural occurence worldwide like risen?<br /> I rest my case.<br /> <br /> And, since you love strawman so much, two can play this game: mummies are NOT a natural occurence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, the Earthly Foundations are supposed to be things more on the scale of gravity. Essential basic laws that make the world function well enough for the Antrophic Principle to take hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, an airplane would burn in Paradox in the 18th century.<br /> <br /> Unless you wanna tell me that airplanes can fly because of the aerodynamics of their wings.<br /> <br /> But then, you'd have to agree on the scientific Paradigm (a dangerous assumption in the WoD). But if you do that, you would have to take away from the Mythical Ages a HUGE set of bygones - gryphs, Pegasus, dragons, none of those would be able to fly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040556#post1040556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. And you're just talking about actualized Marauders in this case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And here's your problem. Marauders do cause Paradox. One of the things that makes them dangerous though, is that they tend to shunt their Paradox on other people instead of getting hit themselves.<br /> <br /> The rules for how lots of Paradox inducing effects brought on by the Marauder Quiet, and when that pushes them out of reality, is detailed in the books. So no, this point really doesn't go your way.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, when I thought the strawman session was over...<br /> <br /> Marauders incur in Paradox the same way as Mages: by doing <u><b><i>vulgar effects</i></b></u>. However, LIKE I SAID, the crazy reality distortions that their mere presence causes ARE NOT EFFECTS AND CAUSE HIM NO PARADOX. So, when reality around a Marauder makes Stones turn into butter... It's the <u>reality that changes</u>, it's not the Marauder <u>changing the reality</u><br /> <br /> <br /> When you wanna start debating my ARGUMENTS we may try to discuss more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:45:02-08:00","id":1041039,"title":"","content":"Reality does not change because everything returns back to normal when the Marauder leaves. The Quiet of the Marauder is superimposed over Reality, but Reality returns to normal like a rubber band that has been stretched. It is probably best to think of the Quiet as a bubble of the Dreaming that is being temporarily superimposed over Reality and, when the Marauder leaves, the Dreaming withdraws as Reality imposes itself. And we are still waiting for a book and page number for your claims about parallel Earths being woven together by the Order of Reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-30-2017, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T21:24:44-08:00","id":1041094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040993#post1040993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, isolation creates new species because of genetic drift;</div> </div> </div> </div>Genetic drift happens without isolation, and doesn't inherently lead to speciation. If it did, we wouldn't consider there to only be one species of humans on Earth, as genetic drift, founder effect, and isolation have combined in various ways to create genetically distinct groups of humans with observable morphological, genetic, and physiological differences. <i>Canis lupus</i> has groups that have been isolated from each other for thousands of years (Eurasian vs. American) without qualifying for being different species, and even for all their differences dogs have been reclassified as <i>Canis lupus familiaris</i> as a subspecies rather than a full species despite isolation from wolves.<br /> <br /> And even when isolation is a factor in speciation, it is not isolation itself that causes it. Isolation just provides are fertile ground for speciation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's NOT about the new niche. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;new&quot; I said &quot;altered.&quot; This matters significantly towards balancing the different schools of definition species and if you claimed to know this as well as you are saying, I shouldn't need to explain this. And I really don't want to start explaining N-th dimensional hypercubes for this tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Giant Panda only existing in Asia means that the BIOLOGICAL REALITY of Asia ONLY EXISTS IN ASIA. </div> </div> </div>Stop. You are misusing the word &quot;reality&quot; by a significant degree. I'm going to treat this as just a language barrier issue for now, but I doubt that this is the case. You're conflating the use of the word &quot;reality&quot; to describe the actualized expression of the natural laws of the universe, with the use of the word to describe the specifics of a given situation. When someone says, &quot;the political reality is that we can't get this law passed&quot; they are not talking about the natural laws of the universe.<br /> <br /> The unique circumstances that lead to a species only existing in one location is not &quot;local biological reality.&quot; It is the interaction of a number of natural forces. That combine in a specific way in a specific location and time. Kind of like how DNA can express so many different species depending on how it comes together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Put a Giant Panda in Antartica and see what happens. </div> </div> </div>It dies (baring a highly specialized and expensive artificial habitat), because reality is consistent. The natural laws that govern the world allow Giant Pandas to live only in specific circumstances. Antarctica lacks those circumstances. How this goes back to the original point is that consistency in reality does not require ubiquity of the expression of the rules of reality. Antarctica is consistent with Asia despite being different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you think not, you should know that you can take things like the dynamic of populations (the number of individuals, the area of dispersion of them, of any given species), and you can make them into MATHEMATICAL PATTERS. </div> </div> </div>Considering I did this for a few years...<br /> <br /> No. You can <b>model</b> them with mathematical equations. You cannot make them into mathematical patterns. You can <b>estimate</b> them with mathematical patterns. These models are always approximations. They're always &quot;best guesses.&quot; The scientific goal is to refine them so that the models are close enough to reality that the model is useful to substitute for reality for experimental, technological, or policy-based applications to be valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the patterns that the species on the Saara have will be NOTHiNG like the pattern of the species on the Amazonia. But you can take completely different species from Amazonia, and they'll show similar patterns. </div> </div> </div>Depends what we're modelling. Though any model that's not specific to the environmental factors involved is unlikely to follow this. Comparing K-type reproduction models to R-type reproduction models is going to show commonalities between species from all environments, because those models work across all biomes. If we're modelling behaviors to disperse excess heat, then we'll see greater similarities between unrelated sandy desert species than to more genetically closely related tropical rain forest species.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My mistake, I was thinking only about vertabrates. I haven't been clear in that one because I didn't think I would need to, since I was clearly comparing sharks and dolphins. </div> </div> </div>I mentioned another aquatic vertebrate in my list. Why don't sea otters look like sharks exactly?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And?<br /> <br /> I was clearly talking about the hydrodynamics. </div> </div> </div>If you don't understand how the internal biology of species impacts hydrodynamics... you need to bone up on your marine biology. How an air breathing mammal handles internal buoyancy and air compression in their lungs has major impacts on their hydrodynamic efficiency, which works entirely differently than a fish's swim bladder or a shark's lipid storage distributions.<br /> <br /> Or we can look at how sharks and dolphins have radically different surface textures to deal with drag if internal biology isn't something you want to get into.<br /> <br /> Of course, sharks have a huge variety of body shapes many of which look nothing like a silky shark or a dolphin; like say angel sharks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can make the strawman you like,... </div> </div> </div>I don't think you know what that term actually means. Please include your justification for using it in response to anything I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To live on Sea, mammals had to look more like sharks. </div> </div> </div>No. To fulfill similar niches different species will experience pressures that lead to convergent evolution. Basking sharks and gray whale have similar traits because they occupy a similar niche as large krill eating pelagic predators. While silky sharks and bottlenose dolphins have a lot of similarities as they consume similar food sources as their primary diets (both tend towards large number of smaller fish rather than hunting large prey like great whites or orcas)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile sea otters don't look like sharks at all, because they don't occupy a similar niche as any shark and have had no pressure to evolve in that direction.<br /> <br /> Many other mammals, like manatees/dugongs, or the seal family, are more in the mid-ground of some more fish like features, and some distinctly mammalian features.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And? Once again, your point is? </div> </div> </div>You're stating something objectively false. I'm pointing that out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tell me, how many whales have you ever saw flying? </div> </div> </div>See, this is a strawman.<br /> <br /> You argued to live an aerial lifestyle, a creature needs wings. I offered a fact that disproves this rule: an animal that lives an aerial lifestyle without wings.<br /> <br /> My point does not rely on all animals being capable of flying, just that animals without wings can fly. So the whale thing is a strawman. It's an argument you're making up that I didn't say, so you can beat on it instead of what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't fly without specific adaptation. </div> </div> </div>Life can't do anything without specific adaptions. What's the point of this? How is this a central argument to anything? What does this prove about Reality Zones in Mage? Or the history of the physical state of Earth in Mage? Animals have adaptations to suit their niche... is meaningless as a central point to any of that. It doesn't even disprove the biology analogy that started all this (it actually supports it by acknowledging that the rules of biology are consistent even if their is great diversity in the animal kingdom).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep, risen and mummies happens everywhere. And? Your point is? </div> </div> </div>Coming back from the dead in a culturally specific fashion isn't unique to the Kuei-jin as you were attempting to assert.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all... What is the matter the taxonomic supernatural group that Kuei Jin occupy to the points <u>you're trying to disprove</u>? </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to &quot;disprove&quot; anything. I'm pointing out that the word &quot;vampire&quot; like many names for creatures is not a strict taxonomic thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second: are <u>Kuei Jins</u> a natural occurence worldwide like risen? </div> </div> </div>Possibly. But not in the now of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I rest my case. </div> </div> </div>Asking two questions doesn't actually make a case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet, an airplane would burn in Paradox in the 18th century. </div> </div> </div>Why? Humans had flying technology in the 18th century. Humans already had methods to stay in the air, and understood the idea of wings. The idea of a winged flying machine had already entered the imagination of the general public as something that might be possible. Go back a bit earlier... probably but then you're in Sorcerer's Crusade territory where Reality Zones are in full effect and if you go back father than that paradox didn't happen and airplanes would be no more dangerous than flying carpets (aka Dark Ages and before).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, LIKE I SAID, the crazy reality distortions that their mere presence causes ARE NOT EFFECTS AND CAUSE HIM NO PARADOX. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the books phrase this as something that is caused by their Avatars. Now, you can argue it's the Avatar acting on its own, and the books support the idea that Avatars might be capable of things the mage they're connected to cannot do yet, but this is still an awakened dynamic effect in application. The Avatar is the &quot;translator&quot; between the Marauder's Quiet and baseline reality around them. Reality doesn't change, the Marauder changes it (either directly and subconsciously, or indirectly through the effects of Quiet on their Avatar).<br /> <br /> And this all might go better is you stopped being quite so antagonistic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:02:15-08:00","id":1041234,"title":"","content":"@Karlgust:<br /> <br /> Question. If you already have an established headcanon about how earth was previous to the OoR, and you don't want to deviate from it (in spite of how the books may be interpreted, or what common sense combined with historical knowledge can say about it). Then why do you ask? . <br /> <br /> For the record, I don't think that earth was flat before OoR, that's not how I, personaly, interpret Mage cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:31:53-08:00","id":1041246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041234#post1041234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Karlgust:<br /> <br /> Question. If you already have an established headcanon about how earth was previous to the OoR, and you don't want to deviate from it (in spite of how the books may be interpreted, or what common sense combined with historical knowledge can say about it). Then why do you ask? .<br /> <br /> For the record, I don't think that earth was flat before OoR, that's not how I, personaly, interpret Mage cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the original question was about if the idea was possible, not certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:01:31-08:00","id":1041255,"title":"","content":"Well, the author seems to believe that it was a certainity from the evidence of their posts. If they want possibilities, they should look to the Dreaming or the Umbra, there are probably Realms of Flat Earths there. The problem with the idea of the Earth being possibly flat before the OoR is that it conflicts with historical evidence (horizons always existed and are mentioned in some of the earliest records) and the canon evidence (the Fera have always known that the Earth was spherical because they have existed for 250 million years and have explored the entire surface many, many times). <br /> <br /> If they just want to play in an alternate cWoD though where the Earth was flat before the OoR, they should feel free. It does conflict with canon though, so they have to change canon so it can fit, but it would have been better to have titled the thread as 'Creating a Flat Earth Alternative Earth'. At least that would have allowed for a potentially more productive discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:24:27-08:00","id":1041277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041255#post1041255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the author seems to believe that it was a certainity from the evidence of their posts. If they want possibilities, they should look to the Dreaming or the Umbra, there are probably Realms of Flat Earths there. The problem with the idea of the Earth being possibly flat before the OoR is that it conflicts with historical evidence (horizons always existed and are mentioned in some of the earliest records) and the canon evidence (the Fera have always known that the Earth was spherical because they have existed for 250 million years and have explored the entire surface many, many times).<br /> <br /> If they just want to play in an alternate cWoD though where the Earth was flat before the OoR, they should feel free. It does conflict with canon though, so they have to change canon so it can fit, but it would have been better to have titled the thread as 'Creating a Flat Earth Alternative Earth'. At least that would have allowed for a potentially more productive discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go back and look at the original proposal, though. The title may say flat earth, but the original post says multiple worlds with different rules separated by umbral reaches. It's not hard to see how horizons would exist in that scenario.<br /> <br /> Also, as a substitute for just saying that this is Mage, not Werewolf, didn't the gauntlet used to be nonexistent? That's not just a WtF thing right? (Edit: Ah yes, I see you already answered this earlier this thread, thanks for that.) Because in any scenario where the barrier between worlds is thin to nonexistent it would be impossible to judge distance in any real sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-31-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:43:14-08:00","id":1041313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the original question was about if the idea was possible, not certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you start that line of thought believing firmly that a flat earth it's, indeed, possible, and are going to argument to the death against anyone that thinks other way. If you already &quot;know&quot; that &quot;the idea it's possible&quot;, and no amount of flying whales or cosmological constants are going to change your mind. Then it's a fake question, because you are certain that the idea it's, indeed, possible.<br /> <br /> If anything, this shouldn't be a question about the possibility of the idea, but a statement taking the idea as an axiom and elaborating from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-31-2017, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:40:49-08:00","id":1041368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041313#post1041313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you start that line of thought believing firmly that a flat earth it's, indeed, possible, and are going to argument to the death against anyone that thinks other way. If you already &quot;know&quot; that &quot;the idea it's possible&quot;, and no amount of flying whales or cosmological constants are going to change your mind. Then it's a fake question, because you are certain that the idea it's, indeed, possible.<br /> <br /> If anything, this shouldn't be a question about the possibility of the idea, but a statement taking the idea as an axiom and elaborating from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I test an idea I often have reason to think it is going to work, but I run it by other people to see what I haven't thought of and what permutations come out of it. Even if the Earth is mutable enough, there could be other reasons why history couldn't happen that way. <br /> <br /> Plus the forums are not united on the issue of how mutable consensual reality is. I daresay the thread would have gone completely differently if they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:55:58-08:00","id":1041374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041313#post1041313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you start that line of thought believing firmly that a flat earth it's, indeed, possible, and are going to argument to the death against anyone that thinks other way. If you already &amp;quot;know&amp;quot; that &amp;quot;the idea it's possible&amp;quot;, and no amount of flying whales or cosmological constants are going to change your mind. Then it's a fake question, because you are certain that the idea it's, indeed, possible.<br /> <br /> If anything, this shouldn't be a question about the possibility of the idea, but a statement taking the idea as an axiom and elaborating from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it impossible?<br /> <br /> I'm only been rude in my answers with Heavy Arms for his condescending tone; now he asks for less &quot;antagonism&quot; in my arguments, the typical victimization after being a total jerk, and I'm only being a jerk to him in response. If a person wants respects, it must learn basic education.<br /> <br /> I know I do say the wrong things in a wrong way, sadly I can't change that, no matter how much I try, but it's not in purpose - except when it is, like now, where I was defending myself from his free insults.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm not stating anything. If anyone convinces me otherwise, I'll change my opinion. I just haven't been convinced yet, and I simply state the reasons of my logic. Show my logic to be false, and it's all well and good.<br /> <br /> Tell me now, when the Void Seekers during the Sorcerors Cruzade crossed the Atlantic, wasn't there an Umbral component in their jorney? They didn't just crossed geeographycal space.<br /> <br /> About &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot;, everywhere in the WoD claim that everything was the &quot;work&quot; of spirits (please, it's an analogy, don't use strawmen here). So, water is wet, because that how the water spirits &quot;made&quot; it. It's kind of a reflex that cuts both ways. Well, before human kind, spirit and matter where united (WtA is also like that). And spirits are sentient beings, if not all, at least the bosses of the mindless ones are. They've shaped the world. Its a hard abstract concept, but it's a kind of &quot;Spiritual Consensus&quot;. The Umbras work in this way; a kind of chicken and egg situation (what came first, the material water or the spirit of water? Is the spirit of water &quot; wet&quot; because he was born from water, or is water wet because that's how the first water spirit &quot;imagined&quot; it?)<br /> <br /> You may say &quot;Umbra has no Consensus&quot;, but that's not necessarily true. For example, what happens when a legion of banes invade a Gaian realm? That real is turned into a corrupted place. It will change - in very significant ways. How? Didn't that realm had several &quot;eternal laws&quot; set on stone? Lets look at the Low Umbra for example. The Tempest was a calm Sea. But, as corruption spread on Earth, and the Angst of the dead raised, it became an infernal tempest, riddled with specters. Hum, interesting... It's almost as if the raising numbers of Spectres were <i>shaping it</i>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that's what happens on all places on Umbra: it's spiritual residents are the ones that shape the place they live.<br /> <br /> About Fera travel around the Earth: shifters see an OBJECTIVE point of view of spiritual. Humans do not. My theory is that is because of the dual material/spiritual nature of Fera.<br /> <br /> For example: a Mage (or sleeper) seing a spirit of Love, could see Romeo and Juliette, could see Venus, or could see Helen of Troy. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Fine. But a spirit of Jealousy, would not perceive an spirit of love in a subjective way. He could perceive it as a trickester demon, as a spider that wants to ambush it's prey... Whatever. But ALL JEALOUSY SPIRITS WOULD PERCEIVE IT THE SAME WAY. That's because they are Bond on their roles; for a Jealousy spirit, everything in the world is disgusting. For ALL of the same kind. Just as much, for ALL love spirits (of the same kind), the world is beautiful, colorful, warm.<br /> <br /> Probably, spirits don't see subjectivity in the world because <i>they are subjective themselves </i>. They perceive the tellurian with different lenses.<br /> <br /> It's like an any climbing on a person; her perspective doesn't allow her to realize that it's a titanic being that it is climbing, and not just a mountain.<br /> <br /> The Fera probably have the same problem, being half spirits themselves. They are bound on their roles, so, they perceive things with those lenses.<br /> <br /> So, when Fera crossed the ancient world, they would have a magnificent quantum view of reality; while humans would only see what they wanted, Fera would see ALL the possibilities. But... They too wouldn't understand that which they were seeing. <br /> <br /> For example<br /> <br /> Caveman A believes Earth to be flat. He travels to the middle of Atlantic. He falls from the Edge of the world (into the Low Umbra? Into the Deep Umbra? Another Umbra? Whatever)<br /> <br /> Caveman B believe earth to be round. He travels to the Atlantic, and reaches &quot;the other side&quot; of the world.<br /> <br /> Fera is half spirit, and perceive reality in an objective way, because he is bound to his role. Fera travels to the Atlantic. In the middle of the ocean, he finds out a &quot;quantum singularity&quot;, or, as he would call it, &quot;a natural opening to the Low Umbra/Deep Umbra/Whatever. He can now choose to go ahead or t\u00f4 enter that &quot;natural portal&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Fera can't realize that he is watching The umbral cat both dead AND alive at the same time, as his spiritual connection don't trigger the observer effect, collapsing one of the possibilities. The Fera will interpret that in an objective way - the Gauntlet is open at this point.<br /> <br /> And he will see some humans entering the breach, and some don't. That's it. That's the perspective of the Fera... Because they can't perceive it in another way.<br /> <br /> It's not so nonsense that.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is headcannon. But, here is the catch: this explanation of why Fera see the Umbra in an objetive way and Mages in a subjective way, are no where to be found. There is no explanation. But, it is said that they are half spirits. It is said that Mages perceive things according to their expectations. So, this explanation have logical consistency, it's not just insane. <br /> <br /> Be it as it may, it is not impossible. So, I think you can't simply say &quot;it's not cannon&quot;, because there is no were saying explicit that. To say &quot;oh, the game doesn't allow that as written&quot; isn't true. It also doesn't state that; it's left for players to tell. But it is a valid view","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:56:28-08:00","id":1041375,"title":"","content":"Paradoxically, I think the pro-Technocracy crowd is saying that there is only Consensual Reality while the pro-Tradition crowd is saying that Consensual Reality is superimposed over Fundamental Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:26:29-08:00","id":1041400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be it as it may, it is not impossible. So, I think you can't simply say &quot;it's not cannon&quot;, because there is no were saying explicit that. To say &quot;oh, the game doesn't allow that as written&quot; isn't true. It also doesn't state that; it's left for players to tell. But it is a valid view</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't need, nor want, to &quot;proove&quot; that your headcanon it's false.<br /> <br /> You know as well as I that these things are purposely left in the air so you can adjust the setting as you see fit, there's no canon answer.<br /> <br /> The same rule of three explains why you have failed to disproove the arguments of Heavy Arms (or those that come before them). The books can be interpreted, easily, in ways that allow earth to have been round from day 1. This interpretation it's jut that, a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> The whole point that you seem to miss, and that Saikou already complained about in another thread it's the folowing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou, in other thread </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, it's cool. It just irks me when I see posts that are like:<br /> A: Hey, how does X work?<br /> B: X works like this.<br /> A: Wrong! X actually works like this!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you get it? . The problem it's that you don't seem to accept that the books can be interpreted in other ways. Thus, why should I bother presenting MY headcanon? I'm not going to defend my understanding of canon cosmology until the armaggedon, much less if I have to justify obscure crossover happenings, real life science, and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-31-2017, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:46:24-08:00","id":1041415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041375#post1041375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradoxically, I think the pro-Technocracy crowd is saying that there is only Consensual Reality while the pro-Tradition crowd is saying that Consensual Reality is superimposed over Fundamental Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol<br /> <br /> That's some crazy shit huh?<br /> <br /> EDIT: that's because we, members of Control, know the lies we spread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-31-2017, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:57:20-08:00","id":1041422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041400#post1041400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't need, nor want, to &amp;quot;proove&amp;quot; that your headcanon it's false.<br /> <br /> You know as well as I that these things are purposely left in the air so you can adjust the setting as you see fit, there's no canon answer.<br /> <br /> The same rule of three explains why you have failed to disproove the arguments of Heavy Arms (or those that come before them). The books can be interpreted, easily, in ways that allow earth to have been round from day 1. This interpretation it's jut that, a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> The whole point that you seem to miss, and that Saikou already complained about in another thread it's the folowing:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you get it? . The problem it's that you don't seem to accept that the books can be interpreted in other ways. Thus, why should I bother presenting MY headcanon? I'm not going to defend my understanding of canon cosmology until the armaggedon, much less if I have to justify obscure crossover happenings, real life science, and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok. But I'm NOT the one doing this. I asked &quot;Could Earth be round before the OoR?'<br /> <br /> And people went crazy.<br /> <br /> Everybody said it's impossible; it's non canon. It's not a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> Hey, Earthly Foundations is a valid concept? Yes it is! If you want it, go for it! No problem at all. It's also NOT a good explanation as any. Somethings ARE set in stone; that's fine.<br /> <br /> But, just don't say that OTHERS views are absolutely invalid, because they aren't. It is not stated in the books &quot;gravity is inviolable&quot;.<br /> <br /> I know I give that impression when I talk, but Im a creature of glamour and have a tendency of being... Passionate in debates.<br /> <br /> However, my idea were met with an absolut negative by those that do not share this view, not with &quot;it could be, but that's not how I do it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:15:48-08:00","id":1041436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041422#post1041422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's ok. But I'm NOT the one doing this. I asked &quot;Could Earth be round before the OoR?'<br /> <br /> And people went crazy.<br /> <br /> Everybody said it's impossible; it's non canon. It's not a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> Hey, Earthly Foundations is a valid concept? Yes it is! If you want it, go for it! No problem at all. It's also NOT a good explanation as any. Somethings ARE set in stone; that's fine.<br /> <br /> But, just don't say that OTHERS views are absolutely invalid, because they aren't. It is not stated in the books &quot;gravity is inviolable&quot;.<br /> <br /> I know I give that impression when I talk, but Im a creature of glamour and have a tendency of being... Passionate in debates.<br /> <br /> However, my idea were met with an absolut negative by those that do not share this view, not with &quot;it could be, but that's not how I do it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same token, you could make the argument that the world we see around us doesn't actually exist, and is just an elaborate bubble within the Dreaming in the mind of a sleeping child, and in reality Mages do not exist. It is just this child's power fantasy for a way to combat a world run by Vampires, where Werewolves hunt for all they deem threats, and where there is no heaven or hell, but only Oblivion to greet them.<br /> <br /> It's not canon, it's never stated as such that Mage works like this, but could it be a possible? Sure, as much anything can be.<br /> But what good does it do to try and go through all the books explaining why this interpretation is <i>actually</i> more valid than other interpretations might be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:41:31-08:00","id":1041449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041436#post1041436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the same token, you could make the argument that the world we see around us doesn't actually exist, and is just an elaborate bubble within the Dreaming in the mind of a sleeping child, and in reality Mages do not exist. It is just this child's power fantasy for a way to combat a world run by Vampires, where Werewolves hunt for all they deem threats, and where there is no heaven or hell, but only Oblivion to greet them.<br /> <br /> It's not canon, it's never stated as such that Mage works like this, but could it be a possible? Sure, as much anything can be.<br /> But what good does it do to try and go through all the books explaining why this interpretation is <i>actually</i> more valid than other interpretations might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. Ok, like I said, I'm passionate on discussions. I like the mental exercise. And I like to give attention to the details; that's why I like to throw the ideas and see how they are opposed. And I try to counterpose them. So, kuei jins being a singular event, gives plausable argument to the idea? Good. It fits. Animal wraiths in Africa too? Ok, good it. All points fit toghether, the logic is consistent. That's enriching for the concept.<br /> <br /> If one of the books said &quot;mages are lunatics, Fera are right and the Umbra and reality is objective&quot;. Well, that would be a final deal breaker for that interpretation. But, since it's not, the possibility is up. So, I may be looking like I'm doing my best to show it's the <i>interpretation</i>, but I'm only trying to make it more <i>solid</i>. Not unique.<br /> <br /> For example: &quot;sorcerors powers doesn't fit the scenario&quot;. Because of reasons. If those reasons are solid enough... Good, my interpretation is valid. <u>It doesn't mean others aren't, or that they are worse</u>. It only means that my idea have solid foundations. And in fact, in this case, which is in another topic, I was showed that I was wrong, the reasons for my idea weren't solid. And I could understand why, and change my interpretation.<br /> <br /> But, until I was convinced of it, I held my ground with the same passion as in this topic. If there is a deal breaker for that notion of &quot;absolutely subjetivity&quot;, I'll abandon the concept.<br /> <br /> And if you ask me, I dare saying that the WoD were all vampires and werewolves and Mages and fae and wraiths live and perish, is just an RPG, were some people from another dimension play with the fates of these poor beings, for their amusement only. That's cruel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:50:54-08:00","id":1041457,"title":"","content":"Basically, I like some logic consistency for my scenarios. For example, if I say &quot;I want a world were the Technocracy is indeed all powerful and all knowing. They watch all the 7.5 billion people on Earth with correspondence and a mega mind to process all the information. They also watch all the reality deviants in the same way. Besides, they can kill Cain or a Neverborn with a blink&quot;. Ok, that's a scenario. But it's absolutely illogical in such a scenario to have ANY deviants AT ALL.<br /> <br /> So, I place all my reasons on the table, so that they may be faced with opposed ideas, and any logic hole that I haven't previously noticed can be fine tuned.<br /> <br /> And again, I wasnt saying other options were invalid. But many said that mine was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:08:09-08:00","id":1041471,"title":"","content":"Especially since the Union has extreme difficulty perceiving the creatures of the Dreaming because of their Banality. An Elder Dragon from the Deep Dreaming could do a number on the Technocrats because it could be constructed with 500 Creation Points and could possess 50 Glamour, and that it not even the worst thing that the Deep Dreaming can spit out (the Old Ones and their minions sleep within the Deep Dreaming).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:10:45-08:00","id":1041506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041375#post1041375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradoxically, I think the pro-Technocracy crowd is saying that there is only Consensual Reality while the pro-Tradition crowd is saying that Consensual Reality is superimposed over Fundamental Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? Usually it is the other way around. When did this start happening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:26:02-08:00","id":1041517,"title":"","content":"The Traditions have a diversity of worldviews, so they have to depend on a Fundamental Reality that their worldview can exist within. The Union supposedly has one worldview that it wants to replace the Fundamental Reality with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:38:00-08:00","id":1041525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041517#post1041517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions have a diversity of worldviews, so they have to depend on a Fundamental Reality that their worldview can exist within. The Union supposedly has one worldview that it wants to replace the Fundamental Reality with.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I see it the opposite way. Consensual reality is what makes the claim that their ways are better actually valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:45:59-08:00","id":1041529,"title":"","content":"I do not agree. Consensual Reality does not work when you have nine different belief systems, otherwise you have constant flux within the Horizon Realms. It is better to come to an agreement on the Fundamental Reality within the Horizon Realms and leave enough flexibility for everyone to be content even if they are not happy. That philosophy of compromise extends to their view of the Earth. The Traditions do not let the perfect be the enemy of the good while the Technocracy is willing to kill the good to have one chance in a million at the perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:56:47-08:00","id":1041539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041529#post1041529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree. Consensual Reality does not work when you have nine different belief systems, otherwise you have constant flux within the Horizon Realms. It is better to come to an agreement on the Fundamental Reality within the Horizon Realms and leave enough flexibility for everyone to be content even if they are not happy. That philosophy of compromise extends to their view of the Earth. The Traditions do not let the perfect be the enemy of the good while the Technocracy is willing to kill the good to have one chance in a million at the perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Traditions goal is exactly that. They want a world where people are free to choose what works for them. Yeah, it's a crazy goal and almost certainly impossible, but it is their ideal.<br /> <br /> They compromise so that one day that compromise is unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:31:48-08:00","id":1041561,"title":"","content":"Not really, not at least as I understand their positions at least. They want a world where magic is free to exist alongside the mundane, not a world where one Paradigm is dominant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:41:50-08:00","id":1041589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041561#post1041561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, not at least as I understand their positions at least. They want a world where magic is free to exist alongside the mundane, not a world where one Paradigm is dominant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. No one paradigm reigns supreme, but all magic works alongside the mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T00:07:54-08:00","id":1041721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1041374#post1041374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it impossible?<br /> <br /> I'm only been rude in my answers with Heavy Arms for his condescending tone; now he asks for less &quot;antagonism&quot; in my arguments, the typical victimization after being a total jerk, and I'm only being a jerk to him in response. If a person wants respects, it must learn basic education.<br /> <br /> I know I do say the wrong things in a wrong way, sadly I can't change that, no matter how much I try, but it's not in purpose - except when it is, like now, where I was defending myself from his free insults.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is your last warning from a moderator, next offense is a suspension. Read the forum rules, you are not allowed to respond to a perceived offense by being intentionally rude or disruptive. If you feel someone is breaking the rules or have any other issue with something someone else posts then you use the &quot;flag&quot; option located on the lower right hand side of the post to report it, then you ignore it and move on. Do not reply to this post.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:12:10-08:00","id":1041783,"title":"","content":"One of the other commonly stated interpretations (because there used to be a few people who were <i>very</i> vocal about it) is that everything is true. The world is always flat, and round, and goes around the sun, and is surrounded by crystal spheres. One may dominate, but the others are true. Part of the revelations Mages have when they awaken is that just because one thing is present doesn't limit what else is.<br /> <br /> At the time I wasn't the biggest fan of the theory on the grounds that 'everything is true' and 'nothing is true' are indistinguishable from each other. I've changed my mind on that over the years, and think it works all right provided it is paired with the corollary: Nothing is as simple as it seems. In that form I tend to use it as the Tradition's explanation for why their magic can work together. I don't usually think it is necessary to decide if they are right or not.<br /> <br /> It's not that different from the way Demon describes the world, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:03:59-08:00","id":1042288,"title":"","content":"One question: Marauders get ejected from reality for being too insane, too unfitt.<br /> <br /> What happens if an entire CIVILIZATION starts having the weirdest ideas?<br /> <br /> Lets say for example that Atl\u00e2ntida was a real place in the long lost past of WoD. <br /> <br /> What would happen if their entire civilization became Quiet-like (believing for example they could breath under the water, and many many more), creating a kind of Consensus of their own? Would they also be ejected as a WHOLE?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:41:47-08:00","id":1042310,"title":"","content":"Entire civilizations do not benefit from Quiet because they are not Awakened (enough of them drown that they rest stop trying to breath underwater before Consensual Reality could ever kick in). The Dreaming is the release valve for the group in that case, as the Dreaming consumes the most extreme cases before they can change Consensual Reality for the group. The most dangerously insane mortals to a group start suffering from such low levels of Banality that they slip into the Near Dreaming and are imprisoned in the Near Dreaming by their own Chinera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:06:40-08:00","id":1042364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1042310#post1042310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entire civilizations do not benefit from Quiet because they are not Awakened (enough of them drown that they rest stop trying to breath underwater before Consensual Reality could ever kick in). The Dreaming is the release valve for the group in that case, as the Dreaming consumes the most extreme cases before they can change Consensual Reality for the group. The most dangerously insane mortals to a group start suffering from such low levels of Banality that they slip into the Near Dreaming and are imprisoned in the Near Dreaming by their own Chinera.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a good mechanism for explaining why the Earthly Foundations are hard to change. I mean, I wouldn't consider air breathing to be a natural law, but I think a lot of people would put it on that level. But if societies with beliefs that visibly different get whisked into the Dreaming, or the Umbra, or even just get separated to the point that they can't interact with each other, it would explain why certain things don't seem to shift.<br /> <br /> Moving to a different topic for a moment. One of the reasons I like the hazy Earth model is that it actually matches the maps that we have. The Romans and Greeks had a few maps that were generally reliable, but for the most part accurate maps weren't available until the Renaissance and the Age of Exploration. Now it could be that, like the real world, distances were always the same and only got measured later. However, in a world where most people never go more than a few miles from hope and going off the beaten path can get you hopelessly lost, it actually makes sense that maps and directions don't always lead you to the same place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:21:43-08:00","id":1042374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargust</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question: Marauders get ejected from reality for being too insane, too unfitt.<br /> <br /> What happens if an entire CIVILIZATION starts having the weirdest ideas?<br /> <br /> Lets say for example that Atl\u00e2ntida was a real place in the long lost past of WoD.<br /> <br /> What would happen if their entire civilization became Quiet-like (believing for example they could breath under the water, and many many more), creating a kind of Consensus of their own? Would they also be ejected as a WHOLE?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Aya it's saying it's true. There's another problem, Quiet it's usually individual. When two Marauders get rejected by Reality, they go each to their own individual Realms.<br /> <br /> There could be an exeption to these (hard as stone) rules. There are a few Marauders who get to share a Quiet, and can sumerge other Mages, and sleepers, into this mindseting. One of these contagious Marauders may get the Mages in the area to share the same Quiet, and thus they would end in the same Realm, when they reach 5. This doesn't means that sleepers are going to be instantly transported there, but I guess that, in his insanity, the Marauder's Avatar could be able to magickally transport the normal people to the Realm (if they're actors in his madness).<br /> <br /> The most common way for a magical landmass that defies Reality to be transported into the Umbra, however, it's through Paradox. It's what happens to a Sanctum if you try to make Archmagic work coincidentally there. If Atlantis existed and was full of mages, they could have caused a strong enough Backlash as to send the entire Island to the Umbra (trough a Paradox Storm that probably killed almost everyone)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Moving to a different topic for a moment. One of the reasons I like the hazy Earth model is that it actually matches the maps that we have. The Romans and Greeks had a few maps that were generally reliable, but for the most part accurate maps weren't available until the Renaissance and the Age of Exploration. Now it could be that, like the real world, distances were always the same and only got measured later. However, in a world where most people never go more than a few miles from hope and going off the beaten path can get you hopelessly lost, it actually makes sense that maps and directions don't always lead you to the same place.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This was a thing. In DA even sleepers can travel to places like the land of the giants, that aren't present in nowdays geography because they were send to the Umbra by the forces of the Consensus. In the Crusade, this phenomenon start getting rarer, and only happens to Mages. In modern days you need Spirit 3<br /> <br /> A theory says that these magical places existed because the Gauntlet was thinner before, and the Umbra and the Earth get yuxtaposed with ease. These places were never part of &quot;The Realm&quot; but rather other realms that yuxtaposed with it, and were thus accessible by everyone (regardless of Arete or personal Paradigm).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-02-2017, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:42:23-08:00","id":1042410,"title":"","content":"In addition, the Dreaming was more open to mortals, so mortal could travel into the Near Dreaming by accident (as well as occasionally having to deal with the stronger Chimera in the Real World). Depending on the region, I imagine that any mortal without a cold iron token to anchor them could have accidentally shifted into the Near Dreaming if they went off a familiar path or road during while traveling at night (cold iron token would have also repulsed most Chimera).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:15:04-08:00","id":1042495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1042374#post1042374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Aya it's saying it's true. There's another problem, Quiet it's usually individual. When two Marauders get rejected by Reality, they go each to their own individual Realms.<br /> <br /> There could be an exeption to these (hard as stone) rules. There are a few Marauders who get to share a Quiet, and can sumerge other Mages, and sleepers, into this mindseting. One of these contagious Marauders may get the Mages in the area to share the same Quiet, and thus they would end in the same Realm, when they reach 5. This doesn't means that sleepers are going to be instantly transported there, but I guess that, in his insanity, the Marauder's Avatar could be able to magickally transport the normal people to the Realm (if they're actors in his madness).<br /> <br /> The most common way for a magical landmass that defies Reality to be transported into the Umbra, however, it's through Paradox. It's what happens to a Sanctum if you try to make Archmagic work coincidentally there. If Atlantis existed and was full of mages, they could have caused a strong enough Backlash as to send the entire Island to the Umbra (trough a Paradox Storm that probably killed almost everyone)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This was a thing. In DA even sleepers can travel to places like the land of the giants, that aren't present in nowdays geography because they were send to the Umbra by the forces of the Consensus. In the Crusade, this phenomenon start getting rarer, and only happens to Mages. In modern days you need Spirit 3<br /> <br /> A theory says that these magical places existed because the Gauntlet was thinner before, and the Umbra and the Earth get yuxtaposed with ease. These places were never part of &amp;quot;The Realm&amp;quot; but rather other realms that yuxtaposed with it, and were thus accessible by everyone (regardless of Arete or personal Paradigm).</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anybody here ever played the Super Nintendo game Chrono Trigger?<br /> <br /> For those who haven't, it's a great RPG game with a wounderful history involving a lot of time travel. One of the places you visit is Atlantida, 12.000 years ago, a land so advanced that you simply couldn't tell the difference between magic and technology.<br /> <br /> And in several views of mythical Atl\u00e2ntida, it's a very similar view, like the versions of Atlantis of both the DC and Marvel comics<br /> <br /> Oh yes, the idea of Atl\u00e2ntida for the game Scion (also from White Wolf), is a land with technologies mixed with magic way beyond anything we could imagine (until the gods of the other Pantheons destroyed them for allegedly becoming cultists of the titans).<br /> <br /> Now, of course there isn't a line about Atl\u00e2ntida on WoD (unlike the CoD), but just in a hypotetical scenario, our modern world with computers, air planes and atomic bomba wasn't created over night... So, it is possible that the technocrats got it figured out, without their Time Table they would break the world.<br /> <br /> And, following this hypotetical super advanced Atl\u00e2ntida, it is quite possible that they would reach that status of high-tech/high-magic over a long course of time, giving reality enough time to &quot;sink in&quot;, just like the Technocracy did. So, couldn't be possible that such a highly advanced land, with it's very particular laws that are different from the rest of the world, couldn't they become too much alien to be able to remain in the same parallel? (Perhaps Atl\u00e2ntida could coexiste with modern world, but not with the animistic cavemen on the rest of the world)<br /> <br /> That idea of Realms or pieces of Realms who were &quot;ejected&quot; from Earth is interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:18:29-08:00","id":1042499,"title":"","content":"Why don't malkavians mess things up with the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> And, why aren't Marauders kicked to the Far Dream instead of the Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:20:45-08:00","id":1042525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, following this hypotetical super advanced Atl\u00e2ntida, it is quite possible that they would reach that status of high-tech/high-magic over a long course of time, giving reality enough time to &quot;sink in&quot;, just like the Technocracy did. So, couldn't be possible that such a highly advanced land, with it's very particular laws that are different from the rest of the world, couldn't they become too much alien to be able to remain in the same parallel? (Perhaps Atl\u00e2ntida could coexiste with modern world, but not with the animistic cavemen on the rest of the world)<br /> <br /> That idea of Realms or pieces of Realms who were &quot;ejected&quot; from Earth is interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was more able to coexist with the modern world than with the animistic cavemen of old, then how it's that it was part of Earth in that age, and not nowadays?.<br /> <br /> My interpretation of the matter, if Atlantis existed as part of Earth and was rejected (much like Lemuria, which it's in DA: Mage), it's that Atlantis did had &quot;magick/science above it's time&quot;, but that in the old Mythic Age the Consensus/Reality/Gauntlet (as these are related) wasn't hard enough for that to be a problem. Latter, the Consensus solidified and Atlantis was kicked of Reality.<br /> However, I like more the idea that it was a Backlash because it has that &quot;disaster&quot; vive arround it. Which coincide with the idea that the gods sunked the island as a punishment for Hubris. If there's a legendary place that it's made for a historical Paradox Storm it's Atlantis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why don't malkavians mess things up with the Dreaming? </div> </div> </div>Who says they don't?. In crossover, everything it's possible...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, why aren't Marauders kicked to the Far Dream instead of the Umbra? </div> </div> </div>Becuase the Dreaming isn't a thing in Mage. Mage has the Umbra for all places that don't correspond with Earth, from dreams (the Dream Zone/Maya) to fantasy (a lot of places in the Astral Umbra), and the Deep Umbra for those places that are beyond human understanding (the maddest of the mad go there).<br /> <br /> You could ask yourself why Demesnes aren't in the Dreaming, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-02-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:17:02-08:00","id":1042549,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming is part of cWoD, so it is part of Mage, even if Mages would like to ignore any area beyond their control. Malkavians are not dangerously insane to society, so they do not end up in the Far Dreaming (though they can occasionally end up in the Near Dreaming). Marauders are too dangerously insane for the Dreaming because their Quiet interferes with the Dreaming (it literally tears up the Near Dreaming), so they are kicked to the nearest equivalent of the Umbra. The Dreaming does not particularly like Mages, though it is willing to tolerate low Banality Mages who obey its rules, but Marauders only obey their own rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:54:12-08:00","id":1042585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1042525#post1042525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it was more able to coexist with the modern world than with the animistic cavemen of old, then how it's that it was part of Earth in that age, and not nowadays?.<br /> <br /> My interpretation of the matter, if Atlantis existed as part of Earth and was rejected (much like Lemuria, which it's in DA: Mage), it's that Atlantis did had &quot;magick/science above it's time&quot;, but that in the old Mythic Age the Consensus/Reality/Gauntlet (as these are related) wasn't hard enough for that to be a problem. Latter, the Consensus solidified and Atlantis was kicked of Reality.<br /> However, I like more the idea that it was a Backlash because it has that &quot;disaster&quot; vive arround it. Which coincide with the idea that the gods sunked the island as a punishment for Hubris. If there's a legendary place that it's made for a historical Paradox Storm it's Atlantis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if we go with a hazy Earth, it might not have been rejected so much as not incorporated. If there were only a few ways of getting to it (and Zeal, as it was called in my copy, was on floating continents so that is likely) those ways could just stop working. Who knows how many kingdoms and peoples never quite fit in and are no longer accessible (except possibly through the tiny little cracks that exist in the modern world).<br /> <br /> I suspect that any civilization that reached its power through centuries of progress rather than overnight paradoxical beliefs is safe from being outright shunted somewhere. The slow march of ideas means that at every point the people's beliefs are not at odds with the reality they are seeing. At least not too much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:42:40-08:00","id":1042611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1042585#post1042585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if we go with a hazy Earth, it might not have been rejected so much as not incorporated. If there were only a few ways of getting to it (and Zeal, as it was called in my copy, was on floating continents so that is likely) those ways could just stop working. Who knows how many kingdoms and peoples never quite fit in and are no longer accessible (except possibly through the tiny little cracks that exist in the modern world).<br /> <br /> I suspect that any civilization that reached its power through centuries of progress rather than overnight paradoxical beliefs is safe from being outright shunted somewhere. The slow march of ideas means that at every point the people's beliefs are not at odds with the reality they are seeing. At least not too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good ideas. All good scenarios. A horrible backlash, sure, that's a good one for such a myth as Atl\u00e2ntida; that one would fit the &quot;Eartlhy Foundations&quot; of Earth. The idea of been ejected is good for &quot;Consensus is all&quot;, and the idea of &quot;Never Incorporated&quot; is great for my idea of &quot;Reality Bubbles&quot; where only the realities close enough get toghether, in a kind of multiverse of infinite possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:09:14-08:00","id":1042982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dreaming is part of cWoD, so it is part of Mage, even if Mages would like to ignore any area beyond their control. Malkavians are not dangerously insane to society, so they do not end up in the Far Dreaming (though they can occasionally end up in the Near Dreaming). Marauders are too dangerously insane for the Dreaming because their Quiet interferes with the Dreaming (it literally tears up the Near Dreaming), so they are kicked to the nearest equivalent of the Umbra. The Dreaming does not particularly like Mages, though it is willing to tolerate low Banality Mages who obey its rules, but Marauders only obey their own rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>cWoD it's not unified in a single, coherent, world. Crossover it's not canon anymore.<br /> <br /> When Crossover was Canon, the Dreaming WAS the Dream Zone (Book of Worlds clarifies that the Dreaming it's how faes see Maya), and mages had no problem entering and traveling within the Zone.<br /> <br /> Currenly, the &quot;Dreaming does not particularly like Mages&quot; because cWoD does not particularly like crossover (you can see a similar trend among all gamelines, true crossover it's harder now. Long gone are the tolerant relations between Gangrel and Garou). The books only mantain a skeleton support for crossover, but you ain't going to see Mages intereacting with the Dreaming anymore. The reason of why Marauders aren't related with the Dreaming it's that Marauders are Mage antagonists, and the rules for the Dreaming aren't supported in Mage books anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-03-2017, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:23:38-08:00","id":1043020,"title":"","content":"How are crossovers not canon anymore? Are there no Garou or Kindred in M20 because there are Mages and Garou in V20 and there are Kindred and Mages in W20. By the way, The Book of Worlds was superseded by The Infinite Tapestry in Mage (Revised). Maya was effectively transformed into the Dream Zone and is unrelated to the Dreaming,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:59:21-08:00","id":1043039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How are crossovers not canon anymore? </div> </div> </div>It just isn't. As per the authors. Crossover isn't supported, do it at your own risk it's the current politic about crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there no Garou or Kindred in M20 because there are Mages and Garou in V20 and there are Kindred and Mages in W20. </div> </div> </div>You mean those Mages with Disciplines? That's not true crossover. True crossover has to take in count the supernatural powers of the other splats, explain the interactions between their societies, etc. There's very little of that in 20 aniversary editions, at least if we compare with the days of the Book of Lost Dreams/Book of Worlds (just a few lines vs whole books).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there no Garou or Kindred in M20 because there are Mages and Garou in V20 and there are Kindred and Mages in W20. Maya was effectively transformed into the Dream Zone and is unrelated to the Dreaming, </div> </div> </div>Maya was always the Dream Zone. It was just another name for the same place. It's unrelated to the Dreaming because, otherwise, the authors would have had to adress Crossover beyond a few lines, and they don't want to. So now we have two spiritual places for dream stuff, when in the old days there was only one.<br /> <br /> Regardless of that, Marauders weren't terribly related to the Dreaming in the age of Book of Worlds either (appart from disrupting it with their pressence), so I was wrong. The reason you suggested for them not being related to the Dreaming stands as a good theory, albeit it can also be because Marauder madness has more to do with warping reality in alien ways than with dream stuff (they don't go to the Dream Zone either, after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-03-2017, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:15:04-08:00","id":1043054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1043039#post1043039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean those Mages with Disciplines? That's not true crossover. True crossover has to take in count the supernatural powers of the other splats, explain the interactions between their societies, etc. There's very little of that in 20 aniversary editions, at least if we compare with the days of the Book of Lost Dreams/Book of Worlds (just a few lines vs whole books).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the rules per V20 Core present Mages literally as People with Disciplines and Paradox. Only Guide to the Black Hand introduces Archaic True Blood Mage Pillar Magik, and even that is somewhat distinct from M20 Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:12:16-08:00","id":1043179,"title":"","content":"Crossovers are canon to their own primary game, and each line is skewed to present its own concerns as the first and foremost gameplay and story elements - as it should be. It's fairer to say that crossover in a 'every line is true' sense isn't canonical, even if it's how a lot of people like to read the setting. What appears about mages in Vampire is canon for how mages roll in Vampire, but not in Mage, and vice versa, except where you get true crossover books ala Blood Treachery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:40:18-08:00","id":1043199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1043039#post1043039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just isn't. As per the authors. Crossover isn't supported, do it at your own risk it's the current politic about crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did the authors stated that, unifically? Or Onyx Path?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1043179#post1043179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossovers are canon to their own primary game, and each line is skewed to present its own concerns as the first and foremost gameplay and story elements - as it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but I wouldn't say that it equals with &quot;crossover isn't canon&quot;. As long as the games acknowledge each other and mention other critters in the books, crossover IS canon in my eyes.<br /> <br /> That the rules don't align and that the critters in the NPC section aren't using their actual splat-specific things? Oh, come on, we all know it's because of ease of play, because this way you don't need to learn a different game, either rules or fluff-wise just to bring in some vampires to a Mage game. It was always like that, always.<br /> <br /> Yes, some authors like(d) the idea of crossover and some don't. It was always that way too, so this part always left hazy. However, I wouldn't say &quot;crossover isn't canon&quot; as long as every game has the same WoD stamp on it and every game's corebook mentions the other critters and mentioning them again and again in nearly every book and having (albeit usually short) write-ups about the interactions with other splats. That's true even for the 20ths. That they don't have full crossover books? Well, they don't have an awful lot of things either. However, for example M20 mentions other critters a LOT and even have crossover rules for them.<br /> <br /> WoD always existed in a strange dichotomy, where crossover is part of the game and world but not really fully supported, because of, as above, ease of play and author preferences. With WWP's One WoD that'll likely change and hopefully we'd get full support for crossover, finally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-03-2017, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:51:16-08:00","id":1043203,"title":"","content":"I think it is as well, but I've mentioned my 'rule of primacy' to you before. For everyone else, that's a house rule I have that, when it comes to the oWoD, each game line gets priority in its own games. If something conflicts between Mage and Vampire, when I'm running Vampire, Vampire wins. Everything else I tend to treat personally as existing except where by implication it would cause a major conflict, and in my experience and opinion, the rule of primacy is the best and easiest way to handle the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:04:50-08:00","id":1043214,"title":"","content":"I agree that might be the best way to handle &quot;cameos&quot; in a game that focuses on one splat in every aspect, even if those cameos are frequent and important, or regular parts of the story.<br /> <br /> Naturally, full-on crossovers work differently, there you need to work out how the things work together and affects each-other. I suspect not so many people are doing that, because it's a lot of work, but I also think it's worth it, if you like that kind of games.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I think that's the reason a lot of people (and authors too) approaches crossover with the &quot;non-canon&quot; attitude. Because they don't want rule/lore arguments at the table, or because they want to focus on one splat. I suspect the authors had the same arguments and ultimately settled into the &quot;half-canon&quot; way as a compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:03:43-08:00","id":1043304,"title":"","content":"I agree. When you are playing a true crossover, where players are running characters of different splats, you have to give equal weight to each system. My rules of thumb for crossover campaigns are 1) the most recent book wins when there are conflicts between non-crossover books and 2) crossover books always win over non-crossover books when there are conflicts. For example, the Book of World was published in 1996, but the Book of Lost Dreams was published in 1997, so the Book of Lost Dreams wins for the rules of a crossover campaign on both accounts (it is the more recent book and it is a crossover book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:05:39-08:00","id":1043306,"title":"","content":"For rules, obviously you use the full rules. But what about for setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:06:08-08:00","id":1043307,"title":"","content":"Well, you could play with a table were you'd have a Mage, a Vampire, a Werewolf, a Changelling and a Wraith... But it would be absolutely unbalanced... And a total mess. What, would they have to worry about technocrats, sabbats, banes, autumm people and specters? Too much weirdness to handle, too many Umbras that half the table can't go, too many groups that they won't be able to deal with, too much trouble","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:37:43-08:00","id":1043376,"title":"","content":"You can generally run a mixed game with Fera, Mystical Traditions, and Seelie Changelings. Vampires and Wraiths tend to not work for crossovers in my opinion. As for settings in a crossover game, the best thing is to choose the core for your game and add on as needed. In the crossover game with Changelings, Fera, and Mages, I use the Fera setting as the core and add on the Dreaming from Changeling and expand on the Umbra to include the High and Low Umbra of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T01:20:07-08:00","id":1043414,"title":"","content":"Well, my rule for crossovers is &quot;what makes sense&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:48:53-08:00","id":1043616,"title":"","content":"I think crossovers with all the game lines would require the players be limited to certain compatible choices. For example, a Mage in a game with Werewolves and Wraiths should be required to have spirit 3.<br /> <br /> Similarly, depending on the factions, you might say only a certain archetype from each splat could be chosen. Perhaps a &quot;technophile&quot; game where you can only chose characters like Glasswalkers, artificiers, Etherites, Knockers, etc.<br /> <br /> Then you could make a threat that they would all have some stake in. Perhaps there is a group of Void Engineers which has discovered the Pattern Web, and is doing some strange experiments to it in order to test its parameters, unknowingly creating ripples in the stability of the telurian, causing all sorts of weird physics loopholes to appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:58:00-08:00","id":1043620,"title":"","content":"The total opposite direction can work as well. When you throw people from complete opposite ends of the spectrum together into a team it can be pretty hilarious. When you get a Slayer from Demon chatting with ghosts while the paranoid trigger-happy Iterator stands nearby, throwing things at the space in front of the Slayer because he doesn't see what the Slayer is talking to and doesn't believe in ghosts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T18:59:59-08:00","id":1043801,"title":"","content":"I really do not think that the Technocracy would allow a Demon to survive longer than it takes to pull the trigger. Demons are among to worst type of supernaturals to the Union, they are literally body snatchers from Outer Space from the perspective of the Technocracy, so I imagine that the only think that the Union will be doing relating to them will be sending in a squad of HitMarks with a dozen Specialists for support. Remember, the Technocracy Executes or Mindwipes any of its members that it finds dealing with Demons (and I doubt that they would terribly care if the Demon called itself a fallen angel).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-04-2017, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T00:30:34-08:00","id":1043882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1043801#post1043801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not think that the Technocracy would allow a Demon to survive longer than it takes to pull the trigger. Demons are among to worst type of supernaturals to the Union, they are literally body snatchers from Outer Space from the perspective of the Technocracy, so I imagine that the only think that the Union will be doing relating to them will be sending in a squad of HitMarks with a dozen Specialists for support. Remember, the Technocracy Executes or Mindwipes any of its members that it finds dealing with Demons (and I doubt that they would terribly care if the Demon called itself a fallen angel).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy doesn't acknowledge that Demons exist, the only standing orders on them are 'Make sure the pubic doesn't believe in them'. They're no more concerned with demonic possession than they are with any OTHER brand of EDE. Which is to say, they generally don't give a damn.<br /> <br /> Also this is the SAME union that conscripts vampires as shocktroopers. They're pretty flexible when it comes to taking weird life forms and putting them to use. As long as those life forms don't try to sell the people magic.<br /> <br /> And no, it wouldn't change a thing. Both are ridiculous names from the superstitious past. They're just another brand of EDE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:02:10-08:00","id":1044011,"title":"","content":"Actually, according to the Book of Madness Revised (pp. 78-80), the Technocrats have specific and extremely violent responses to Demons (which they consider to be among the worst EDEs). Kindred are one thing, they are an established phenomena with quantifiable weakness. Demons are another thing because, quite frankly, the Demons are extradimentional body snatchers who stated goals are to establish their own dominion on Earth, which is antithetical to the plans of the Union.<br /> <br /> I know that there are Demon fans that believe that Demons are not given their rightful due, but I really do believe that every major supernatural faction in cWoD believes Demons=Enemy. Whether you are Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, or Mages, you tend to be considered enemy number one when you make a deal with Demons. The only thing worse than an Infernalist is an actual Demon, which is exterminated with extreme prejudice because they are Evil with a capital E to most splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:34:37-08:00","id":1044497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044011#post1044011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, according to the Book of Madness Revised (pp. 78-80), the Technocrats have specific and extremely violent responses to Demons (which they consider to be among the worst EDEs). Kindred are one thing, they are an established phenomena with quantifiable weakness. Demons are another thing because, quite frankly, the Demons are extradimentional body snatchers who stated goals are to establish their own dominion on Earth, which is antithetical to the plans of the Union.<br /> <br /> I know that there are Demon fans that believe that Demons are not given their rightful due, but I really do believe that every major supernatural faction in cWoD believes Demons=Enemy. Whether you are Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, or Mages, you tend to be considered enemy number one when you make a deal with Demons. The only thing worse than an Infernalist is an actual Demon, which is exterminated with extreme prejudice because they are Evil with a capital E to most splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my hopes of organizing a Demon: The Fallen/Mage crossover game die an unmourned death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:54:31-08:00","id":1044508,"title":"","content":"They could try to explain:<br /> <br /> &quot;You know, we are not Earthbounds, and to tell you the truth, we fought for humanity... Yeah, we are demons but, you know, it's not just like that... Oh yeah, we have to snatch a mortal body to flee from the abyss but&quot;<br /> <br /> Multiple blasters lights from several technocrats and lightning bolts from several traditionalists cross the room, a result of their fragile alliance against something perceived as a bigger danger, and the demon stay on Earth gets a little shorter than predicted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:47:25-08:00","id":1044536,"title":"","content":"A demonic invasion is one of the events on the 'Ally with X' list of just about any supernatural faction. If you want a crossover game of Changelings, Garou, Kindred, KJ, Technocracy, Traditions, etc, that is one of the events that will cause it. All you need is ten thousand Demons crossing over during the same night...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:22:53-08:00","id":1044559,"title":"","content":"It's also a justification for working with a demon who is trying to stop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:13:48-08:00","id":1044588,"title":"","content":"Well, believing or helping a self proclaimed demon isn't likely, but if the Demons have low Torment, the mages don't need to know its a demon. Traditionalist make deals with angels from several layers of the Umbra. They may belive the creature it's another angelic manifestation, of a kind they never seen before. After all, True Demons were rare before the Week of Nightmares, mages may not know much about them. Most mages aren't going to like the body snatching part, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:51:13-08:00","id":1044617,"title":"","content":"Man following this thread is weird.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Mage is actually one of the few games where dealing with demons can be possible without the default hyper-wrath most other splats default to. This is because Mages (esp. Hermetics and Batini) generally understand that there are a lot of different kinds of demons out there in the WoD. The Astral Realms can have demons in them that are no more inherently evil than their angelic Umbrood counterparts. A skilled enough demonologist (at least non-Technocrat) mage is going to quickly figure out that &quot;demon&quot; is a very loose term in the WoD, and that the PC demons of DtF might deserve a shot as allies against the far more obviously bad demons out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:51:22-08:00","id":1044618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044588#post1044588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most mages aren't going to like the body snatching part, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be acceptable if the body and memories were snatched from a person who was dying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:58:34-08:00","id":1044621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044617#post1044617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man following this thread is weird.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Mage is actually one of the few games where dealing with demons can be possible without the default hyper-wrath most other splats default to. This is because Mages (esp. Hermetics and Batini) generally understand that there are a lot of different kinds of demons out there in the WoD. The Astral Realms can have demons in them that are no more inherently evil than their angelic Umbrood counterparts. A skilled enough demonologist (at least non-Technocrat) mage is going to quickly figure out that &quot;demon&quot; is a very loose term in the WoD, and that the PC demons of DtF might deserve a shot as allies against the far more obviously bad demons out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of an observation I saw once:<br /> <br /> Is selling your soul to a demon a bad idea in Mage? It depends a great deal on what the demon is. If, say, the Demon is the manifestation of your Avatar it could work out quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T11:11:40-08:00","id":1044629,"title":"","content":"It also depends on what the consequences of the deal are. From what I read of the Dark Ages Mage, there dealing with demons is described with the consequences happening after death. The 2nd <i>Book of Madness</i> and KotE's <i>A Thousand Hells</i> present the harsh option in which you can lose your free will with one badly negotiated deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:59:01-08:00","id":1044681,"title":"","content":"No, I disagree, both the Technocracy and the Traditions have fairly strict rules about dealing with Demons (Book of Madness Revised, pp. 74-83). Even summoning a demon for information is enough to get most Mages ostracized or re-educated. Actually making deals with Demons are an executable offense within both the Traditions and the Technocracy even if you do not engage in Soul Pacts. Actually engaging in Soul Pacts is one of the few things that the Traditions will Gilgul you for and the Technocracy will Mindwipe you for because you have thrown in your lot with the Nephandi, even if you are not officially part of their team yet.<br /> <br /> In addition to the legal consequences, the fact that your Avatar starts separating from your soul after (Avatar plus Arete) years and becomes the property of your Demon Lord within (Avatar) years is a bad thing for Mages. For Sorcerers, however, it is probably a sweet deal, because they can negotiate for Spheres without having to Awaken (getting a Demonic Avatar equal to their highest Sphere in the process). With a combination of luck and skill, Sorcerers can instantly become Masters in multiple Spheres without having to bother with any effort (or, with some bad luck, will end up becoming a demonic chew toy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T13:32:24-08:00","id":1044694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044681#post1044681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree, both the Technocracy and the Traditions have fairly strict rules about dealing with Demons (Book of Madness Revised, pp. 74-83). Even summoning a demon for information is enough to get most Mages ostracized or re-educated. Actually making deals with Demons are an executable offense within both the Traditions and the Technocracy even if you do not engage in Soul Pacts. Actually engaging in Soul Pacts is one of the few things that the Traditions will Gilgul you for and the Technocracy will Mindwipe you for because you have thrown in your lot with the Nephandi, even if you are not officially part of their team yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you didn't read that quite precise as in the book. Summoning a demon is frowned upon. Only actually making deals typically leads to being ostracized and branding (possibly death). Soul trade is death. Subjugation of the entire soul is gilgul. And even further, it mentions several times, 'this is fairly common, the traditions have divided means of enforcement, and rare is the master who hasn't done it before.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:23:08-08:00","id":1044745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044681#post1044681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree, both the Technocracy and the Traditions have fairly strict rules about dealing with Demons (Book of Madness Revised, pp. 74-83). Even summoning a demon for information is enough to get most Mages ostracized or re-educated. Actually making deals with Demons are an executable offense within both the Traditions and the Technocracy even if you do not engage in Soul Pacts. Actually engaging in Soul Pacts is one of the few things that the Traditions will Gilgul you for and the Technocracy will Mindwipe you for because you have thrown in your lot with the Nephandi, even if you are not officially part of their team yet.<br /> <br /> In addition to the legal consequences, the fact that your Avatar starts separating from your soul after (Avatar plus Arete) years and becomes the property of your Demon Lord within (Avatar) years is a bad thing for Mages. For Sorcerers, however, it is probably a sweet deal, because they can negotiate for Spheres without having to Awaken (getting a Demonic Avatar equal to their highest Sphere in the process). With a combination of luck and skill, Sorcerers can instantly become Masters in multiple Spheres without having to bother with any effort (or, with some bad luck, will end up becoming a demonic chew toy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the problem with that is you're conflating Demons, AKA The Entropic Umbrood Spirits, with Demons, The Fallen.<br /> <br /> Two entirely different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T17:09:11-08:00","id":1044778,"title":"","content":"I really doubt that the average Mage cares. The Demons of DtF resemble the most powerful of the Devil-Eaten. I think that the average Mage is going to kill it with fire and not bother to ask questions later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T17:53:02-08:00","id":1044790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044778#post1044778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really doubt that the average Mage cares. The Demons of DtF resemble the most powerful of the Devil-Eaten. I think that the average Mage is going to kill it with fire and not bother to ask questions later.</div> </div> </div> </div>EVERY Umbrood looks alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:33:50-08:00","id":1044806,"title":"","content":"Considering this actually happened in one of my games...<br /> <br /> Not every mage agrees on the same definition of what a demon is. On character (a Hermetic of House Xaos) has Eris as his Avatar, and when trying to explain who Eris is ran into a lot of trouble with a good number of the local mage community because he screwed up explaining it in a way that didn't make it should like his Avatar was of a goddess of evil (Aka a demon, aka he was a barabbi) and almost died before the miscommunication got sorted out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:49:56-08:00","id":1044812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044790#post1044790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EVERY Umbrood looks alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every Umbrood is a body snatching parasite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:09:56-08:00","id":1044998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044812#post1044812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not every Umbrood is a body snatching parasite.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existence of Fomori Kami Gorgons and Drones seems to contradict that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:37:14-08:00","id":1045002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044998#post1044998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The existence of Fomori Kami Gorgons and Drones seems to contradict that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So because there are examples of parasitic Umbrood, all Umbrood are parasitic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:41:30-08:00","id":1045005,"title":"","content":"Rather, when most Umbrood show capacity for parasitic acts, it's reasonable to assume all have the capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:01:10-08:00","id":1045009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1044778#post1044778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really doubt that the average Mage cares. The Demons of DtF resemble the most powerful of the Devil-Eaten. I think that the average Mage is going to kill it with fire and not bother to ask questions later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends entirely on the mage. There isn't really an 'average' mage, especially with the distinctions between paradigms. While interacting with demons is frowned up, how they react is very situational on both how the Demon is presented and the Mage's outlook/morality/etc. Most probably won't <i>like</i> something that might seemingly be infernal, but that doesn't mean fire and doom ASAP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045005#post1045005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, when most Umbrood show capacity for parasitic acts, it's reasonable to assume all have the capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do all spirits really have the possession charm? That seems like a bold claim to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:11:57-08:00","id":1045013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045005#post1045005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, when most Umbrood show capacity for parasitic acts, it's reasonable to assume all have the capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... are you including Duck? Can Unicorn's Duck possess you? Can any of Unicorn's brood possess you? These creatures which are specifically known for being spirits of peace, some of whom are taboo to directly intervene with things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:27:33-08:00","id":1045021,"title":"","content":"Oh hey. Here are these specific examples of exception to a general rule. Keep in mind most mages know very little about spirits. Possession is not uncommon, and is therefore not specifically a strike against the fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:10:23-08:00","id":1045041,"title":"","content":"Possession it's nearly always present in Banes, but it isn't so common among other Spirits. Gaian spirits rarely have it (Kami are rare), Weaver spirits also don't tend to have it (Drones are created by &quot;hearing the One Song&quot;, which isn't something tied to a singular spirit making a possesion). Kaos spirits don't tend to have it (Gorgons are rare, and happen randomly) In the Low Umbra Wraiths with high levels of Puppetry can do something similar, but I wouldn't say it's commonplace. High Umbra spirits usually don't have it, and those who have it are almost always astral demons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-07-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:17:13-08:00","id":1045044,"title":"","content":"Kami are not technically Possessed per se, no Gain spirit fuses with them. It is more of an alterative form of Awakening, where the Spirit rather than the Avatar becomes Awakened. In effect, the Spirit is transformed into a Gaian Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T03:36:17-08:00","id":1045670,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all, I doubt a Demon, aka, one of the fallen that took residence in the Abyss, I doubt it will go around in the streets telling everybody about how he rebelled against god and have thus became a body snatching spiritual parasitic demon. That's a first thing.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I doubt most of any splats will be able to tell this thing apart from... Some other thing. It's not like you could tell a fallen just by looking at it.<br /> <br /> Third: it could be hard to make a distinction between a true fallen and some kind of Umbrood. The fallen could use that in his favor to pose as something... Less abhorent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T03:48:41-08:00","id":1045671,"title":"","content":"Here's how I understand it from my limited reading.<br /> <br /> The Consensus is made up of a few things. Basic Reality as determined by the laws of nature. Then you can add to that the viewpoints of Sleepers to get a more local consensus.<br /> <br /> The Earth IS round. However, if everyone in the world believed it was flat, and every Mage worked together to try and make it flat, that could work. Never happened however.<br /> <br /> The viewpoints of sleepers don't shape the world or &quot;cast&quot; magic. They are effectively like counter-magic for the big constants. Sleepers know that the moon doesn't just fall out of the sky, the sea doesn't boil with a click of your fingers, and so their views shape how a Mage can alter reality. They don't, however, shape reality.<br /> <br /> For example, around the time the theory of the 4 Humours was abandoned and modern medical science was becoming more and more accepted, the bile, pus and blood in every human in the relevant Reality Zones didn't transmute into something else. Gay people existed in times where the consensus was that they didn't, as another example.<br /> <br /> Simply put, you have a basal reality which can be explained multiple ways. Maybe it's all code, maybe it's all one big machine, maybe it's all one big Spiritual Entity or a creation of Allah/The Seven Heavens/God/Your Pantheon. Maybe none of that matters. But at the end of the day what goes up must come down, basic Newtonian Physics, celestial bodies etc. etc. are not up for debate. A Mage can play with these things (using Forces to stop Newtonian Physics, with some excuse about magnets or some made-up-effect (a surname followed by Effect or Law usually works)) but they cannot rewrite these things. Sleepers can be wrong about these things (and their being wrong can help a Mage; people with a sloppy grasp of physics can help a Forces user to remain Coincidental) but they cannot change these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T05:18:33-08:00","id":1045691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045671#post1045671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, around the time the theory of the 4 Humours was abandoned and modern medical science was becoming more and more accepted, the bile, pus and blood in every human in the relevant Reality Zones didn't transmute into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny you should bring that up, because that is one of my go to examples of more recent world changing. It touches upon so much: it's a change pushed by Mages, it's a dramatic shift in the world, it leaves everything looking almost <i>exactly</i> the same, and how we choose to handle it has a profound effect on what Mage actually is. If it did change we have to contend with what was there before and how life worked before there was a definition for it. If it didn't we have to contend with how many modern principles we unintentionally said were hardcoded into reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T05:31:46-08:00","id":1045697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045691#post1045691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny you should bring that up, because that is one of my go to examples of more recent world changing. It touches upon so much: it's a change pushed by Mages, it's a dramatic shift in the world, it leaves everything looking almost <i>exactly</i> the same, and how we choose to handle it has a profound effect on what Mage actually is. If it did change we have to contend with what was there before and how life worked before there was a definition for it. If it didn't we have to contend with how many modern principles we unintentionally said were hardcoded into reality.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I go with the latter. Functionally, nothing changed. Vampires didn't notice an odd taste around that transition. Disease rates didn't fluctuate in some ridiculous way. Existing diseases didn't become defunct and existing medical practises didn't change in efficacy. Bleeding by leeches was just as useless before this change as it was after.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER you could argue that the diseases, Vampires, leeches and everything else changed with the Four Humours. In that case you're agreeing with the latter and using the aesthetic of disagreement. If it looks like a duck, sounds like a duck, moves like a duck and has the genetic code of a duck, it's a duck.<br /> <br /> Techno-based Magick/Sorcery are prevalent in modern times because it is a very logical way of understanding the way reality ACTUALLY IS. The Four Humours were a flawed understanding of the reality of human biochemistry and illness, and they are just about functional for a Mage; a Hermetic can Heal just as effectively by focusing on removing the &quot;imbalanced humours&quot;, but that's a crutch he uses to Focus his power, it isn't reality. A Virtual Adept who uses Life to heal others via medical equipment (with a good dose of reality hacking if you want to go vulgar) is doing the same thing but the Medical and Scientific knowledge involved are much closer to what the world actually is. The world was always round, people always were made of organs made up of tissues made up of cells made up of organelles made up of biological molecules made up of chemical molecules made up of atoms.<br /> <br /> That's part of what makes the Technocracy, Virtual Adepts and similar so powerful. A rational, logical society with good education will train children to believe in their paradigm from day one. The Technocracy doesn't need to mess with the curriculum (though they can if they want consensus on their side, teasing the idea of jetpacks/cyborgs being &quot;right around the corner&quot;), they can simply let people devote themselves to reason as it's a natural process of a developing society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:52:05-08:00","id":1045725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045697#post1045697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I go with the latter. Functionally, nothing changed. Vampires didn't notice an odd taste around that transition. Disease rates didn't fluctuate in some ridiculous way. Existing diseases didn't become defunct and existing medical practises didn't change in efficacy. Bleeding by leeches was just as useless before this change as it was after.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't be likely to see any obvious overnight changes anyways. People don't think they are changing reality, so any new theory has to explain what they already see. If disease patterns changed it was slowly over time, with the occasional sudden outbreak, both of which were normal anyways. Possibly Vampires did notice a change, although blood was one of the humours so maybe things stayed the same as far as they were concerned.<br /> <br /> However, when it comes to stuff like bloodletting and leeches, that stuff did work if enough people believed it did. Consensual reality is still a thing, regardless of whether it defines reality or only influences it. Hence Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Techno-based Magick/Sorcery are prevalent in modern times because it is a very logical way of understanding the way reality ACTUALLY IS. The Four Humours were a flawed understanding of the reality of human biochemistry and illness, and they are just about functional for a Mage; a Hermetic can Heal just as effectively by focusing on removing the &quot;imbalanced humours&quot;, but that's a crutch he uses to Focus his power, it isn't reality. A Virtual Adept who uses Life to heal others via medical equipment (with a good dose of reality hacking if you want to go vulgar) is doing the same thing but the Medical and Scientific knowledge involved are much closer to what the world actually is. The world was always round, people always were made of organs made up of tissues made up of cells made up of organelles made up of biological molecules made up of chemical molecules made up of atoms.<br /> <br /> That's part of what makes the Technocracy, Virtual Adepts and similar so powerful. A rational, logical society with good education will train children to believe in their paradigm from day one. The Technocracy doesn't need to mess with the curriculum (though they can if they want consensus on their side, teasing the idea of jetpacks/cyborgs being &quot;right around the corner&quot;), they can simply let people devote themselves to reason as it's a natural process of a developing society. </div> </div> </div>I've never been comfortable with this line of thinking. Mage, to me, is a game where magic and technology are the same thing. The Technocracy, to me, is a group of Mages trying to force their views on reality, not a bunch of scientists trying to divest themselves of their own awakening. If there is a one true reality underneath all of the changes the Consensus puts on it, the Technocracy should be as far from it as the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Indeed, there is another possibility, which is that there is a well defined baseline reality and the Technocracy is pushing the Consensus further from it, which is why their explanations need to be more and more complicated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:14:25-08:00","id":1045737,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> But the proof is in the pudding. No other paradigm allows for mobile phones which can be manufactured by mundanes using mundane materials, and handed out to mundane people and allow them to speak to eachother from across continents. Science is objectively the way to go, as far as we can see. There wasn't a hermetic inscribed stone in the Dark Ages which let people chat to eachother effortlessly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:19:08-08:00","id":1045741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045737#post1045737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> But the proof is in the pudding. No other paradigm allows for mobile phones which can be manufactured by mundanes using mundane materials, and handed out to mundane people and allow them to speak to eachother from across continents. Science is objectively the way to go, as far as we can see. There wasn't a hermetic inscribed stone in the Dark Ages which let people chat to eachother effortlessly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's because the Technocracy specifically set out to spread their particular brands of doing things too the masses. The Hermetics, notably, were trying to do the same thing in the few years before the OoR started their campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:33:44-08:00","id":1045750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045741#post1045741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's because the Technocracy specifically set out to spread their particular brands of doing things too the masses. The Hermetics, notably, were trying to do the same thing in the few years before the OoR started their campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you see it as one paradigm simply having become dominant, and mundane science's efficacy is just an extension of that? Well that is perfectly reasonable, even if it's opposed to another perfectly reasonable view. Do the books ever fall on one or the other? Like &quot;yes, science is all made up and is just as much a meaningless (or meaningful) paradigm as that of any random Mage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:43:40-08:00","id":1045789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045750#post1045750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you see it as one paradigm simply having become dominant, and mundane science's efficacy is just an extension of that? Well that is perfectly reasonable, even if it's opposed to another perfectly reasonable view. Do the books ever fall on one or the other? Like &quot;yes, science is all made up and is just as much a meaningless (or meaningful) paradigm as that of any random Mage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I'd say there's plenty of evidence for it. Or, well, it depends. Let me split that into three questions:<br /> <br /> <b>1) Does the modern world look and act like it does because of what modern people believe?</b><br /> <br /> This one is pretty certain. Between the descriptions of Consensual Realty, the descriptions of Reality Zones, and the rules for determining vulgarity, it's pretty well established. There are also numerous other nods throughout the books too, such as Traditions claim credit for getting the sleepers to accept certain ideas and technologies (Sons of Ether claim the EMP and Uncertainty), and Technocratic principles forever rejected by the Consensus and Paradox after the Czar Vargo event.<br /> <br /> I'd go so far as to say this is one of the core ideas of Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2) Does the Consensus make things real?</b><br /> <br /> This on the other hand...<br /> <br /> This one has been asked in a lot of forms. Is anything real? Is everything real? Is reality fully under the control of the Consensus? Is there a baseline reality that the Consensus overrides but doesn't erase?<br /> <br /> It's been asked a lot because the books are considerably less certain. While I could certainly mine up some quotes about the bulk of reality being defined by the Consensus, there are also references to Cosmological Constants and things that are remarkably hard to change. I do think Mage 2nd was written with the idea that the Consensus makes things real, but it does not say so definitively and M20 certainly doesn't invalidate anything it doesn't have to.<br /> <br /> So in this case the Consensus could make things happen but still be dead wrong. There could be a strong, well-defined baseline <i>reality</i> behind Consensual Reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3) If there is a baseline reality, is it the one defined by our modern scientific understanding?</b><br /> <br /> It could be, but probably not. There are references, even in M20, of modern technology not working in the distant, unpopulated areas of the world. Technocratic Reality is considered to be different than Primal Reality. Mythic threads keep mostly forgotten magic alive. So there's good reason to believe that the Technocrats are not right*.<br /> <br /> However, gravity is often cited as one of the Earthly Foundations and the need for Prime 2 to create things out of whole cloth implies a kind of Conservation of Matter and Energy. So if there is a strong baseline reality, I'd say it isn't our reality but it isn't completely alien to it either.<br /> <br /> *Or, to paraphrase Douglas Adams, they are definitively right. In cases of major discrepancy it is reality that has it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-08-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:55:38-08:00","id":1046070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045671#post1045671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how I understand it from my limited reading.<br /> <br /> The Consensus is made up of a few things. Basic Reality as determined by the laws of nature. Then you can add to that the viewpoints of Sleepers to get a more local consensus.<br /> <br /> The Earth IS round. However, if everyone in the world believed it was flat, and every Mage worked together to try and make it flat, that could work. Never happened however.<br /> <br /> The viewpoints of sleepers don't shape the world or &quot;cast&quot; magic. They are effectively like counter-magic for the big constants. Sleepers know that the moon doesn't just fall out of the sky, the sea doesn't boil with a click of your fingers, and so their views shape how a Mage can alter reality. They don't, however, shape reality.<br /> <br /> For example, around the time the theory of the 4 Humours was abandoned and modern medical science was becoming more and more accepted, the bile, pus and blood in every human in the relevant Reality Zones didn't transmute into something else. Gay people existed in times where the consensus was that they didn't, as another example.<br /> <br /> Simply put, you have a basal reality which can be explained multiple ways. Maybe it's all code, maybe it's all one big machine, maybe it's all one big Spiritual Entity or a creation of Allah/The Seven Heavens/God/Your Pantheon. Maybe none of that matters. But at the end of the day what goes up must come down, basic Newtonian Physics, celestial bodies etc. etc. are not up for debate. A Mage can play with these things (using Forces to stop Newtonian Physics, with some excuse about magnets or some made-up-effect (a surname followed by Effect or Law usually works)) but they cannot rewrite these things. Sleepers can be wrong about these things (and their being wrong can help a Mage; people with a sloppy grasp of physics can help a Forces user to remain Coincidental) but they cannot change these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That basically sums up my take on it. Your next example about the four humors too.<br /> <br /> <br /> What parts of modern technology is based on the Foundations and which are possible only because of the Consensus is an interesting debate, just as ultimately the &quot;what are the Foundations, really?&quot;. It's hard, because we essentially don't know how things would work without the consensus, the closes thing is how things were described in the DA books and historical parts of Mage books. We know as much as the most sophisticated technologies might work less in the remote places, so they might be based on the Consensus, or the Consensus could make them work more efficiently. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T17:40:32-08:00","id":1046083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045737#post1045737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> But the proof is in the pudding. No other paradigm allows for mobile phones which can be manufactured by mundanes using mundane materials, and handed out to mundane people and allow them to speak to eachother from across continents. Science is objectively the way to go, as far as we can see. There wasn't a hermetic inscribed stone in the Dark Ages which let people chat to eachother effortlessly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because no other paradigm is embraced by litterally billions of people. Every person on Earth has at least a few technocratic ideas kicking around their head. Even the traditions seem to have caved to some of their paradigm.<br /> <br /> Also yes. There totally could be a hermetic inscribed stone that worked like a phone. One that works in the hands of mortals even!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:53:25-08:00","id":1046140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1046083#post1046083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also yes. There totally could be a hermetic inscribed stone that worked like a phone. One that works in the hands of mortals even!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm imagining a magic mirror in each home, carved and enchanted by members of a guild of expert craftsmen. As the magi-technology improves, they'll figure out how to shrink them to pocket-size, so every make-up compact doubles as a portable communication tool. It would be that reality's version of the jump from land-line to cellular phones. Posters and public service announcements would crop up, warning common people to keep their Wards up to date, lest unscrupulous Sorcerers use the consumer's mirror to scry on them.<br /> <br /> Armies of alchemists would prepare and sell common remedies for aches and fevers, or bags of Floo Powder for teleportation like in Harry Potter. There wouldn't be airports, but Gate Stations, with portals being opened and closed on the hour to shuffle commuters, tourists, and immigrants across the world. Instead of vacuum cleaners, you'd buy enchanted brooms that sweep themselves, and buildings would be assembled by teams of super-strong Golems, with human foremen directing their efforts like they would construction equipment.<br /> <br /> If any of these works of High Wizardry were accepted by the masses, they would become Coincidental. If they become accepted enough, even Sorcerers would be able to build and maintain them. They would fall under the purview of mundane Ability before long, just as Computer, Technology, and Drive have in the Technocracy-dominated reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:08:04-08:00","id":1047802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1045697#post1045697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I go with the latter. Functionally, nothing changed. Vampires didn't notice an odd taste around that transition. Disease rates didn't fluctuate in some ridiculous way. Existing diseases didn't become defunct and existing medical practises didn't change in efficacy. Bleeding by leeches was just as useless before this change as it was after.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER you could argue that the diseases, Vampires, leeches and everything else changed with the Four Humours. In that case you're agreeing with the latter and using the aesthetic of disagreement. If it looks like a duck, sounds like a duck, moves like a duck and has the genetic code of a duck, it's a duck.<br /> <br /> Techno-based Magick/Sorcery are prevalent in modern times because it is a very logical way of understanding the way reality ACTUALLY IS. The Four Humours were a flawed understanding of the reality of human biochemistry and illness, and they are just about functional for a Mage; a Hermetic can Heal just as effectively by focusing on removing the &amp;quot;imbalanced humours&amp;quot;, but that's a crutch he uses to Focus his power, it isn't reality. A Virtual Adept who uses Life to heal others via medical equipment (with a good dose of reality hacking if you want to go vulgar) is doing the same thing but the Medical and Scientific knowledge involved are much closer to what the world actually is. The world was always round, people always were made of organs made up of tissues made up of cells made up of organelles made up of biological molecules made up of chemical molecules made up of atoms.<br /> <br /> That's part of what makes the Technocracy, Virtual Adepts and similar so powerful. A rational, logical society with good education will train children to believe in their paradigm from day one. The Technocracy doesn't need to mess with the curriculum (though they can if they want consensus on their side, teasing the idea of jetpacks/cyborgs being &amp;quot;right around the corner&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, they can simply let people devote themselves to reason as it's a natural process of a developing society.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, by that reasoning, you are completely failing to grasp the mood of Mage, plus, you're completely <i>destroying</i> all of the scenario.<br /> <br /> If the germ-theory for diseases is the basic background for how reality works instead of being due to bad eye curses, if we fall because of gravity and not because of the spirits of mother-Earth, if individuals are coded by their DNA and not by humurous fluids, if we are made of Carbon, Oxigen, Hidrogen and Nitrogen instead of water, air, fire and Earth...<br /> <br /> Why the hell are the Traditions fighting for? If that's truly is the case, guess what... The Traditions are a bunch of lunatics idiots! Congratulations, you just turned the Ascension War into the BS War...<br /> <br /> You can't do that without RUINING the game of Mage.<br /> <br /> So, no, in Mage, DNA <i>isn't really a thing</i>. It is no more <i>real</i> than using the eye of Horus to keep the bad spirits away.<br /> <br /> What you're failing to realize is that the world of Mage <u>is not the real world</u>.<br /> <br /> And no, the technocratic stuff works because they kidnapped people's beliefs, and not because they know the stuff better.<br /> <br /> And, once again, if that were the case, oppose the Technocracy would be retardic, the Traditions would be a bunch of delusional idiots, which would make the game of Mage a total nonsense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:25:42-08:00","id":1047810,"title":"","content":"But the <i>possibility</i> to be on the delusional idiots side is worthwhile...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:33:05-08:00","id":1047814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047802#post1047802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, by that reasoning, you are completely failing to grasp the mood of Mage, plus, you're completely <i>destroying</i> all of the scenario.<br /> <br /> If the germ-theory for diseases is the basic background for how reality works instead of being due to bad eye curses, if we fall because of gravity and not because of the spirits of mother-Earth, if individuals are coded by their DNA and not by humurous fluids, if we are made of Carbon, Oxigen, Hidrogen and Nitrogen instead of water, air, fire and Earth...<br /> <br /> Why the hell are the Traditions fighting for? If that's truly is the case, guess what... The Traditions are a bunch of lunatics idiots! Congratulations, you just turned the Ascension War into the BS War...<br /> <br /> You can't do that without RUINING the game of Mage.<br /> <br /> So, no, in Mage, DNA <i>isn't really a thing</i>. It is no more <i>real</i> than using the eye of Horus to keep the bad spirits away.<br /> <br /> What you're failing to realize is that the world of Mage <u>is not the real world</u>.<br /> <br /> And no, the technocratic stuff works because they kidnapped people's beliefs, and not because they know the stuff better.<br /> <br /> And, once again, if that were the case, oppose the Technocracy would be retardic, the Traditions would be a bunch of delusional idiots, which would make the game of Mage a total nonsense</div> </div> </div> </div>Does something have to be true to matter? The Traditions are fighting for culture, freedom of expression, against authoritarianism. &quot;Ooh, what if you're all right?!?!&quot; isn't by default the more mature approach to Mage. Eventually, there needs to be some fundamental force determining what can or can't be. And no, The Traditions aren't a bunch of idiots. Their explanations for the way reality is make perfect sense, they just happen to be incorrect. My question is why that matters. The Paradigms can't all be true. The Universe could be a Machine and Code at the same time, and possibly an Illusion, and possibly One Being, but can such a Unified Codified Mechanistic Illusionary universe also be both Chaotic and Fundamentally Good? Can it be both Gnostic and Monotheistic?<br /> <br /> Mage is cool and unique because people with strongly different beliefs can shape the world with them. Whether their beliefs are true isn't the issue.<br /> <br /> And seriously? You can't think of a SINGLE reason to oppose the Technocracy if they're right about science? Firstly, they aren't the only Technomages. You're ignoring two Traditions and a bunch of unaffiliated Mages, along with lots of members of the different Traditions and Dispirates. Secondly, they're PRETTY FUCKING EVIL. The Progenitors are genetic darwinists whose manifesto is straight up &quot;hey, humanity replaced the neanderthals, it's kind of our duty to push humanity to the next level of evolution&quot;. The Syndicate are Pentex on steroids. There are 10,001 reasons to fight the Technocracy even if you agree with them, ESPECIALLY if you agree with them. Just look at the Stereotypes of the Technocracy among the Etherites and the Adepts. The Technocracy is also kind of secretly controlled by a group of Nephandi... that is if you follow that Future Fate. And their Win-State, according to some setting options, is a world where people only want pop music and burgers, where creativity is dead, where no one believes in anything apart from the cold march of progress, where Awakening into anything other than Technomagick is impossible.<br /> <br /> &quot;My thoughts are one with everything&quot; doesn't have to be RIGHT to be cool. And if it works, if it's magickal, that's cool enough for me.<br /> <br /> With all of that said, I'm aware that the Mage lore is officially on the side of &quot;everyone is right/wrong&quot;, that just doesn't jam with me. And no, I'm not missing the whole point of the game. Oddly enough Noddist players are okay with the Book of Nod being a sham faked by Saulot to control the Jyhad, True Brujah players are okay with their Antedeluvian actually despising them... you can happily play a belief without immaturely demanding that it must be correct, or that no other belief can be more correct in a meta sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-12-2017, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:41:28-08:00","id":1047820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047802#post1047802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, by that reasoning, you are completely failing to grasp the mood of Mage, plus, you're completely <i>destroying</i> all of the scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, now, are we in one true way-ism territory?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the germ-theory for diseases is the basic background for how reality works instead of being due to bad eye curses, if we fall because of gravity and not because of the spirits of mother-Earth, if individuals are coded by their DNA and not by humurous fluids, if we are made of Carbon, Oxigen, Hidrogen and Nitrogen instead of water, air, fire and Earth...<br /> <br /> Why the hell are the Traditions fighting for? If that's truly is the case, guess what... The Traditions are a bunch of lunatics idiots! Congratulations, you just turned the Ascension War into the BS War...<br /> <br /> You can't do that without RUINING the game of Mage.<br /> <br /> So, no, in Mage, DNA <i>isn't really a thing</i>. It is no more <i>real</i> than using the eye of Horus to keep the bad spirits away.<br /> <br /> What you're failing to realize is that the world of Mage <u>is not the real world</u>.<br /> <br /> And no, the technocratic stuff works because they kidnapped people's beliefs, and not because they know the stuff better.<br /> <br /> And, once again, if that were the case, oppose the Technocracy would be retardic, the Traditions would be a bunch of delusional idiots, which would make the game of Mage a total nonsense </div> </div> </div>For one, let's not forget that a lot of sub-groups and individuals in the Traditions which embraced various modern sciences. The Traditions are just not anti-science and anti-technology. Certain ultra-conservative groups and persons could be that, but not the whole.<br /> <br /> For two, and that's the thing I feel several people just don't grasp, or don't like as a concept: magic and science could work side-by-side. The four humors theory could work, while being completely wrong from an objective reality standpoint, because mages could bend reality and the four humors were a paradigm, a focus for doing that. It could even work to some extent in the hands of sleepers, if enough of them believing in it.<br /> <br /> Why does it have to be either/or? Why the concept of baseline reality (based on science) superimposed by magic and/or consensus/reality zones are destroying Mage? Because i don1t think it does that, it was always how I interpreted the game.<br /> <br /> You just don't need to throw out every law of nature the window to have magic. It's indeed a game, a fantasy world, it could have both.<br /> <br /> Why the Traditions are fighting if reality is not entirely based on the beliefs of humanity? Because magic is still a thing and it's dangerous, but it's wonderful and the Union want to eradicate it, or monopolize it at best, because it's a wild card. That's why. Oh, and as 11twiggins wrote, for thousands of different cultural/political/philosophical/ethical reasons.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-12-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:52:45-08:00","id":1047829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1046140#post1046140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm imagining a magic mirror in each home, carved and enchanted by members of a guild of expert craftsmen. As the magi-technology improves, they'll figure out how to shrink them to pocket-size, so every make-up compact doubles as a portable communication tool. It would be that reality's version of the jump from land-line to cellular phones. Posters and public service announcements would crop up, warning common people to keep their Wards up to date, lest unscrupulous Sorcerers use the consumer's mirror to scry on them.<br /> <br /> Armies of alchemists would prepare and sell common remedies for aches and fevers, or bags of Floo Powder for teleportation like in Harry Potter. There wouldn't be airports, but Gate Stations, with portals being opened and closed on the hour to shuffle commuters, tourists, and immigrants across the world. Instead of vacuum cleaners, you'd buy enchanted brooms that sweep themselves, and buildings would be assembled by teams of super-strong Golems, with human foremen directing their efforts like they would construction equipment.<br /> <br /> If any of these works of High Wizardry were accepted by the masses, they would become Coincidental. If they become accepted enough, even Sorcerers would be able to build and maintain them. They would fall under the purview of mundane Ability before long, just as Computer, Technology, and Drive have in the Technocracy-dominated reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The sleepler society would look a lot like the magical society of Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> Or like a D&amp;D scenario, were magical objects are just common place on every people's lives.<br /> <br /> How much pervasive would that kind of magical influence be in society? That would depend a lot.<br /> <br /> For example, in our real world, we have billions of cellphones.<br /> <br /> But that's due to massive producing.<br /> <br /> Without the industrial production, we COULD have the technology, but not the massive production.<br /> <br /> Lets take the example of PCs for example (personal computers). They are common place for us now, but without Steve Jobs, perhaps we would never see that.<br /> <br /> Why would a regular person want a computer after all heh? Computers are useful for companies, for scientific purposes, for maths in industries, to keep data for administration... Why the hell would a regular Joe wanna a computer?<br /> <br /> Well... Need I go further on that?<br /> <br /> It is worth noticing that we have many technologies that simply aren't &quot;popular&quot; (or useful) amongst the masses, despite the fact that they could be.<br /> <br /> A society were the Hermetic Paradigm became dominant, for example, could range from the overly Magic society of Harry Potter (where Magic is as common as modern world tech), to the subtle Magic background of Lord of the Rings (there are half a dozen Rings of power, a few Crystal Balls - the Palintiri, which by the way any mundanes can use, like the Steward of Gondor, a few elfic itens and that's it, whit regular people living mostly mundane lives using iron age technologies and keeping as far away as possible from the business of the Mages or the servants of the enemy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:57:43-08:00","id":1047833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047820#post1047820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, now, are we in one true way-ism territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that he's as devoted to his Paradigm for playing Mage as the characters of Mage are to their Paradigms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:12:35-08:00","id":1047839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047814#post1047814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does something have to be true to matter? The Traditions are fighting for culture, freedom of expression, against authoritarianism. &amp;quot;Ooh, what if you're all right?!?!&amp;quot; isn't by default the more mature approach to Mage. Eventually, there needs to be some fundamental force determining what can or can't be. And no, The Traditions aren't a bunch of idiots. Their explanations for the way reality is make perfect sense, they just happen to be incorrect. My question is why that matters. The Paradigms can't all be true. The Universe could be a Machine and Code at the same time, and possibly an Illusion, and possibly One Being, but can such a Unified Codified Mechanistic Illusionary universe also be both Chaotic and Fundamentally Good? Can it be both Gnostic and Monotheistic?<br /> <br /> Mage is cool and unique because people with strongly different beliefs can shape the world with them. Whether their beliefs are true isn't the issue.<br /> <br /> And seriously? You can't think of a SINGLE reason to oppose the Technocracy if they're right about science? Firstly, they aren't the only Technomages. You're ignoring two Traditions and a bunch of unaffiliated Mages, along with lots of members of the different Traditions and Dispirates. Secondly, they're PRETTY FUCKING EVIL. The Progenitors are genetic darwinists whose manifesto is straight up &amp;quot;hey, humanity replaced the neanderthals, it's kind of our duty to push humanity to the next level of evolution&amp;quot;. The Syndicate are Pentex on steroids. There are 10,001 reasons to fight the Technocracy even if you agree with them, ESPECIALLY if you agree with them. Just look at the Stereotypes of the Technocracy among the Etherites and the Adepts. The Technocracy is also kind of secretly controlled by a group of Nephandi... that is if you follow that Future Fate. And their Win-State, according to some setting options, is a world where people only want pop music and burgers, where creativity is dead, where no one believes in anything apart from the cold march of progress, where Awakening into anything other than Technomagick is impossible.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;My thoughts are one with everything&amp;quot; doesn't have to be RIGHT to be cool. And if it works, if it's magickal, that's cool enough for me.<br /> <br /> With all of that said, I'm aware that the Mage lore is officially on the side of &amp;quot;everyone is right/wrong&amp;quot;, that just doesn't jam with me. And no, I'm not missing the whole point of the game. Oddly enough Noddist players are okay with the Book of Nod being a sham faked by Saulot to control the Jyhad, True Brujah players are okay with their Antedeluvian actually despising them... you can happily play a belief without immaturely demanding that it must be correct, or that no other belief can be more correct in a meta sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. If the Traditions are wrong... They are wrong. Period.<br /> <br /> If they fight for freedom, for a world of love and filled of rainbows... Why the hell does the idiotic Hermetic is still using cavemen runes?<br /> <br /> If Science! Really is a thing... The Dreamspeakers are just a laughble bunch of barbaric idiots living as cavemen!<br /> <br /> The political reasons to fight against the Union DOES NOT MATTER when you consider the existence of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The Traditions exist to preserve <i>their way of life </i>.<br /> <br /> Really, you'd have to be the most stupid person on Earth to keep praying for the spirits for a heal after a Technocrat show to you the germs infecting someone using his life 1.<br /> <br /> That's simply is nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Ramnses also showed already that THIS IS NOT HOW THE SCENARIO IS SHOWED.<br /> <br /> It is firmly implyed throughout all the line that science is no where more right (or more wrong) than the belief of the One, or the animistic world view of Dreamspeakers, or the notion that the world is a simulational matrix by the VA's, or the solipsistic view of Ecstatics. <br /> <br /> In fact, it is much more likely that Science is the more WRONG idea about the world. If I had to guess, I'd say that science is the biggest BS there is, and probably the animistic view of the universe is the closest to truth.<br /> <br /> You guys may, of course, state that Science is the real reality foundation for the scenario for Mage.<br /> <br /> But that's strictly headcannon, and in fact, it goes against the cannon of Mage.<br /> <br /> Check the post of Ramnses again, he just put it Crystal clear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:33:42-08:00","id":1047857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047839#post1047839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't matter. If the Traditions are wrong... They are wrong. Period. (1)<br /> <br /> If they fight for freedom, for a world of love and filled of rainbows... Why the hell does the idiotic Hermetic is still using cavemen runes? (2)<br /> <br /> If Science! Really is a thing... The Dreamspeakers are just a laughble bunch of barbaric idiots living as cavemen! (3)<br /> <br /> The political reasons to fight against the Union DOES NOT MATTER when you consider the existence of the Traditions. (4)<br /> <br /> The Traditions exist to preserve <i>their way of life </i>. (5)<br /> <br /> Really, you'd have to be the most stupid person on Earth to keep praying for the spirits for a heal after a Technocrat show to you the germs infecting someone using his life 1. (6)<br /> <br /> That's simply is nonsensical. (7)<br /> <br /> Ramnses also showed already that THIS IS NOT HOW THE SCENARIO IS SHOWED. (8)<br /> <br /> It is firmly implyed throughout all the line that science is no where more right (or more wrong) than the belief of the One, or the animistic world view of Dreamspeakers, or the notion that the world is a simulational matrix by the VA's, or the solipsistic view of Ecstatics. (9)<br /> <br /> In fact, it is much more likely that Science is the more WRONG idea about the world. If I had to guess, I'd say that science is the biggest BS there is, and probably the animistic view of the universe is the closest to truth. (10)<br /> <br /> You guys may, of course, state that Science is the real reality foundation for the scenario for Mage. (11)<br /> <br /> But that's strictly headcannon, and in fact, it goes against the cannon of Mage. (12)<br /> <br /> Check the post of Ramnses again, he just put it Crystal clear (13)</div> </div> </div> </div>1: And? I've stated that being right/wrong is irrelevant here, so if you could actually develop the argument.<br /> <br /> 2: Because that's how he shapes reality. He can't just decide to Unawaken and Reawaken as a Chemical Engineer or a Hacker when he sees the power of Science! in action. And who's the real idiot? The Hermetic can shape reality just as well as the Virtual Adept, and the Hermetic doesn't even need to learn Calculus. Lucky bastard.<br /> <br /> 3: Not... really. Again, does God have to exist for Nuns to matter? If you say yes, then you're simply wrong. There is value in meditation (prayer) even if there is no answer. There is value in helping those who need help, even if there isn't a God watching. The Dreamspeakers don't need to be correct to be worthwhile. And again, they're STILL FUCKING MAGES which is AWESOME, Science! or no Science!.<br /> <br /> 4: Yes, they kind of definitely do. The Tradition's major reasons for fighting the Technocracy are all political. The Technocracy is an antagonist because it does not accept other paradigms at all, and seeks to eradicate them, simple as that.<br /> <br /> 5: Great! I agree. And does a 'way of life' need to actually be correct to be worthwhile? I'd argue that the Pyramids were worthwhile, even if there isn't some Egyptian afterlife where that old King can have orgies for eternity, they're still quite neat. Imagine if Art and Culture in the real world were held to this standard. &quot;Oh, your painting is pretty, but is it correct about the reason for existence and mass enlightenment? HUH?!?!?!!?&quot; STOP OBSESSING OVER BEING RIGHT.<br /> <br /> 6: No, you absolutely wouldn't. That arrogance, seriously. People in Mage who hold onto deeply held beliefs despite Science! telling them they are wrong aren't morons. They've seen the proof of their powers in action. All I'm seeing is a bigger and bigger window into your world-view of actual culture, actual religion and actual philosophy, and it's a bit terrifying.<br /> <br /> 7: No comment, but Edit is your friend.<br /> <br /> 8: Well no, it's not a closed book. We don't know what the Earthly Foundations really are, and for all we know the Earthly Foundations are something which Scientific Paradigms are closer to than any other. Acting like it's a closed book is disingenuous; &quot;Science is the most accurate reflection of the Earthly Foundations&quot; isn't a head-canon, it's an opinion which fits within canon.<br /> <br /> 9: Yeah, cool, but define Wrong. Right/Wrong could mean &quot;can do magic&quot; or &quot;is actually a true reflection of the way reality is&quot;. The Mage lore is, yes, that there are merits to each Paradigm and that all of them let you alter reality, but the Mage lore isn't &quot;ooh, all of these contradictory ideas are 100% true reflections of the way this world works&quot;.<br /> <br /> 10: That's your headcanon, and it's a bad one. If Science is the most BS paradigm, then it's doing very well in spite of that.<br /> <br /> 11: Oh, THANK YOU. I was getting scared for a second. I'll gladly take my Mage ST License back, thank you sir.<br /> <br /> 12: Well, no, it doesn't. Thinking that the Earthly Foundations are most accurately reflected by science isn't a head-canon, it's an opinion which fits within the canon. You could say the same for any paradigm, but my money is on science since it has less hand-waving. Oh... Spirits. It's all Spirits! Why do we fall?! Spirits! Why does food go off when you leave it?! Spirits! And yes, Science! can be used in the same way, and sometimes is in Mage, but Science actually seeks to explain every phenomena with a theory which works in multiple test conditions, even the Science! of Mage. It is by far the best candidate for being the closest to the Earthly Foundations.<br /> <br /> 13: Yes, his posts were very insightful. No, you may not borrow cachet from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-12-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:34:59-08:00","id":1047859,"title":"","content":"One last thing: you are wrong. All paradigms CAN be true.<br /> <br /> If the universe is the Matrix, and that Matrix is weaved by those experiencing it... Well, I think you got the point.<br /> <br /> It is not necessarily thou, mind you, that's not what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> But, speaking of &quot;true way-ism&quot;, to quote Pmark, or to note how deeply delved into &quot;your own&quot; Paradigm, to quote 11twigg, it is interesting to notice that, I'm not the one saying &quot;this is how the world is&quot;...<br /> <br /> ...You guys are.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying what <i>it isn't </i>. So, it is NOT Cannon that Science really is a thing. It is you guys who are insisting on that - which is fine if you wanna that, but this is STRICTLY headcannon, so stop pushing it as the ultimate truth. That's basically what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, note that it's YOU who are so enclosured by your ownviews that can't accept anything beyond it. It's you guys saying that &quot;science is (more) right&quot;. Even thou that's not the game's assumption - at all.<br /> <br /> Like it has been said here a million times before - that's an open-ended subject, with no objective final truth - and that aspect of the scenario were delivered <i>on purpose</i>. And that's the thing - you guys have your absolute ultimate truth, and don't accept others - to the point of accusing those that do not share your viewpoints of been &quot;narrow minded&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, the thing is: can you be right? Sure you can.<br /> <br /> But you must also admit that this is <i><b>just a possibility</b></i>.<br /> <br /> That means that, if another group considers the bad eye as valid as the germ-theory... Well, that's how it is. Just because you think the germ-theory better (or more right) or more akin to the real world, that doesn't make you any where closer to been right. If you're the ST of your group, and the group goes by it, fine, good for you. But, if you tell that in a table were the players and ST actually abide with the &quot;Consensus is all&quot;, you'll have to suck it up and deal with the fact that, in Mage games, science &quot;is just another bullshit like curses&quot; - and in fact, science may be a BIGGER bullshit than saying that everything is made of fire, air, water and earth, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:45:02-08:00","id":1047864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047857#post1047857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 8: Well no, it's not a closed book. We don't know what the Earthly Foundations really are, and for all we know the Earthly Foundations are something which Scientific Paradigms are closer to than any other. Acting like it's a closed book is disingenuous; &amp;quot;Science is the most accurate reflection of the Earthly Foundations&amp;quot; isn't a head-canon, it's an opinion which fits within canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is getting tiresome. And since I'm tired of being accused to be narrow minded <i>by people that can't accept different opinions and think that only their ideas are right, violently rejecting any others</i>, I'll have to do something that I hate to do: ask for references.<br /> <br /> Please, post all the <b>Cannon</b> material that <b>objectively says</b> that the scientific paradigms are <b>the closer to the Earthly Foundations</b>.<br /> <br /> Book and page, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:47:58-08:00","id":1047866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047864#post1047864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is getting tiresome. And since I'm tired of being accused to be narrow minded <i>by people that can't accept different opinions and think that only their ideas are right, violently rejecting any others</i>, I'll have to do something that I hate to do: ask for references.<br /> <br /> Please, post all the <b>Cannon</b> material that <b>objectively says</b> that the scientific paradigms are <b>the closer to the Earthly Foundations</b>.<br /> <br /> Book and page, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please give a reference to me stating that my opinion IS the canon, rather than being something which fits in the canon very neatly? I'll wait <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, and saying &quot;I hate doing this&quot; while doing something doesn't let you keep any of the cachet doing it costs you. &quot;I hate doing [obnoxious behaviour], but you MADE me you monster!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:48:34-08:00","id":1047867,"title":"","content":"Basically, Karlgust is trying to make an argument that cWoD is a virtual world where the rules can be rewritten at any time, but it really isn't. Mages get to bend the rules and, if they get enough people to believe in the bending of the rules, they get to make their Magick easier and other Magick harder, but it has minimal effect on other supernatural creatures or other supernatural powers, so there are underlying rules that Mages cannot break. And let us see his arguments supported by book and page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:49:14-08:00","id":1047868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047859#post1047859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That means that, if another group considers the bad eye as valid as the germ-theory... Well, that's how it is. Just because you think the germ-theory better (or more right) or more akin to the real world, that doesn't make you any where closer to been right. If you're the ST of your group, and the group goes by it, fine, good for you. But, if you tell that in a table were the players and ST actually abide with the &quot;Consensus is all&quot;, you'll have to suck it up and deal with the fact that, in Mage games, science &quot;is just another bullshit like curses&quot; - and in fact, science may be a BIGGER bullshit than saying that everything is made of fire, air, water and earth, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not either/or. Why the bad eye and germ theory should be mutually exclusive? What if germ theory is how things go naturally, by default? Spells, spirits and such like could still cause diseases, because they could influence the building blocks of reality and mess with patterns? <br /> <br /> That magic is working doesn't have to be meaning that natural laws are nonexistent, or just the product of human beliefs. You could add, without substituting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:55:40-08:00","id":1047871,"title":"","content":"One last thing 11twiggins: if you play in a table were &quot;The One&quot; is the ultimate truth, you may angry and protest as much as you like, but science will be the hughest load of BS on the universe... And THAT'S IT.<br /> <br /> Once again, MAGE IS A SUBJECTIVE GAME.<br /> <br /> If you wanna make the techies views right, that's ABSOLUTELY ON YOU.<br /> <br /> But nobody else has the same obligation to follow up to that. <br /> <br /> Any interpretation you may wanna is STRICTLY HEADCANNON, because there is NO Cannon, period. Those questions were left open <i>on purpose</i>.<br /> <br /> So no, science is no way better than curses. It may be at your tables, at your own discretion, but that's not a Cannon rule AT ALL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:10:25-08:00","id":1047879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047868#post1047868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, it's not either/or. Why the bad eye and germ theory should be mutually exclusive? What if germ theory is how things go naturally, by default? Spells, spirits and such like could still cause diseases, because they could influence the building blocks of reality and mess with patterns? <br /> <br /> That magic is working doesn't have to be meaning that natural laws are nonexistent, or just the product of human beliefs. You could add, without substituting. </div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But that's also a flaw in THAT very argument. That's what you're failing to see, to grasp. And here, you're trying to fit things into your view, instead of accepting that <b><i>other views are just equaly possible </i></b>.<br /> <br /> Why should the germ theory and the bad eye be mutually exclusive?<br /> Answer: they shouldn't, or they haven't.<br /> <br /> But here is another, more interesting question<br /> <br /> Why should they BE COMPATIBLE?<br /> Answer: they could... But don't NEED to.<br /> <br /> Can you understand the difference?<br /> <br /> Can you understand that Mage is not set on stone?<br /> <br /> Can you understand that, yes, science may be the ultimate truth, and in fact does not goes against other mystical explanations, but in fact expands and goes beyond them<br /> <br /> Is just as valid as<br /> <br /> Science the ultimate bullshit.<br /> <br /> Both are just as valid!<br /> <br /> And the same goes for the idea of the One for the Chorus, the animistic view of Dreamspeakers and any other.<br /> <br /> That's what you're failing to understand - all the answer don't have to lead towards &quot;Science is right&quot;. They don't! The game doesn't even imply that - at all.<br /> <br /> Could it be? Yes... But... Does it HAVE to be? Absolutely not!<br /> <br /> So, when you say &quot;you know, its not necessary that Science is either absolutely right/wrong&quot;. Yes, you're right. But you are failing to understand that, the possibility that Science is a total bullshit, is a totally valid position too. You can't,simply put that one out to fit into your worldview..<br /> <br /> And in fact, it is a very rich game indeed when you turn science into just an illusory conspiracy, instead of the ultimate truth... It's a very interesting game and concept to play too, you should try it some day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:13:25-08:00","id":1047881,"title":"","content":"There are objective realities in Mage though, as the powers if other supernatural creatures work regardless of the Consensus. Heck, Mages aren't even the best things at True Magick because Demon Lords can make normal mortals Archmages if the mortal is willing to gamble their souls.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Technocrats are con artists because they take credit for Fundamental Reality. They aligned their practices just close enough to Fundamental Reality and moved the Consensus close enough to Fundamental Reality that they could make some of their Magick coincidental. Whenever they could without endangering their power, they pushed technology so they could use technology instead of Magick, but they are parasites not innovators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:34:29-08:00","id":1047892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047867#post1047867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, Karlgust is trying to make an argument that cWoD is a virtual world where the rules can be rewritten at any time, but it really isn't. Mages get to bend the rules and, if they get enough people to believe in the bending of the rules, they get to make their Magick easier and other Magick harder, but it has minimal effect on other supernatural creatures or other supernatural powers, so there are underlying rules that Mages cannot break. And let us see his arguments supported by book and page.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I haven't. Or, rather, I said that as <i>my personal view</i> - which is the definition of headcannon. That's why I don't need quotes, because there arent any.<br /> <br /> But that's the thing - your opinion is YOUR headcannon too - because there is no Cannon ultimate answer. Im not saying you're wrong - but you're saying that I AM. Beyond any doubt.<br /> <br /> Now, since you think my view is TOTALLY impossible, since YOUR ultimate truth is supremme and beyond any doubt, and my views are utterly nonsense, now, that's something I would like for YOU to prove.<br /> <br /> Book and page please. I'm sure that will be no problem for you, since my idea is so ridiculously nonsensical, after all, your answer is the ONE and ONLY possible one, and anything beyond that is completely garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:46:09-08:00","id":1047900,"title":"","content":"Well, I can point you to the existence of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Possessed, Sorcerers, Spirits, Wraiths, etc as evidence of a Fundamental Reality that Mages cannot change through changing the Consensus. In the case of Sorcerers, you have magical practitioners that can shut down Mages because they have superior forms of countermagic, which suggests that Numina aligns better with Fundamental Reality than Spheres (plus the complete lack of Paradox). And the Paradigm of the Mage or Sorcerer does not matter, Sorcerers still get to say 'no' to Mages better than Mages get to say 'no' to Sorcerers (Sorcerers get to say 'no' to a lot of things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:46:52-08:00","id":1047901,"title":"","content":"Primal reality is NOT technocratic reality.<br /> <br /> Which one is closer to the &quot;real&quot; reality?<br /> <br /> By the way, that thing about &quot;objective reality&quot; isnt set in stone either. Thre is no ultimate answer for the supernatural powers of the nightfolk - the idea that they work on some static principle or are based on some &quot;reality Foundation&quot; are <i><b>theories</b></i> about the subject, not ultimate laws. In fact, you'll find 2 conflicting theories as the main ones - the &quot;based on reality foundation&quot; would say, for example, something like &quot;vampirism is the will of God&quot;, therefore works on a higher principle. That's close to the &quot;cosmological constants&quot;. But the &quot;static principle&quot; would oppose that, and those creatures would work <i>within the Consensus</i> based on static principles, in a way that ressambles the sorcerors powers. Therefore, no, that's not set in Stone.<br /> <br /> Once again, it can be that if you wanna, but it is not the Absolut ultimate truth that everybody should adhere for in order to not commit the heresy of deviating from the Cannon.<br /> <br /> The view of absolute Consensus remains still valid, THATS MY ONLY POINT","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:53:01-08:00","id":1047904,"title":"","content":"The only point I see is a lot of shouting. Shouting does not make a point any more valid, it just makes it louder. If there is an absolute Consensus, it does not effect anything but Mages because the rest of the Nightfolk do not seem to care. In fact, Mages might not want to advertise that weakness because Kindred and KJ might figure out how to manipulate humanity in such a way that the Consensus turns so against Mages that the lot of them find themselves banished beyond the Horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:58:03-08:00","id":1047908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047900#post1047900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can point you to the existence of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Possessed, Sorcerers, Spirits, Wraiths, etc as evidence of a Fundamental Reality that Mages cannot change through changing the Consensus. In the case of Sorcerers, you have magical practitioners that can shut down Mages because they have superior forms of countermagic, which suggests that Numina aligns better with Fundamental Reality than Spheres (plus the complete lack of Paradox). And the Paradigm of the Mage or Sorcerer does not matter, Sorcerers still get to say 'no' to Mages better than Mages get to say 'no' to Sorcerers (Sorcerers get to say 'no' to a lot of things).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a strong headcannon, but it's funny that you would use CHANGELLINGS as &quot;proof&quot; of supernaturals that <i>can't be changed by Consensus</i>.<br /> <br /> If anything, Changellings are LIVING PROOF of the POWER OF CONSENSUS.<br /> <br /> Changellings are what remains of the true fae of old, that had to parasite human souls to remain on Earth... That's basically the changelling way. And why? Yep, that's right... Because of the change of the Consensus, that doesn't believe in fairies any more.<br /> <br /> Spirits? Oh please... Spirits have become all but bygones... When once it were simple for them to cause trouble, now... Unable to remain in the material world - Consensus courtesy.<br /> <br /> So, no, once again, things don't add up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:02:11-08:00","id":1047911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047904#post1047904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only point I see is a lot of shouting. Shouting does not make a point any more valid, it just makes it louder. If there is an absolute Consensus, it does not effect anything but Mages because the rest of the Nightfolk do not seem to care. In fact, Mages might not want to advertise that weakness because Kindred and KJ might figure out how to manipulate humanity in such a way that the Consensus turns so against Mages that the lot of them find themselves banished beyond the Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're wrong. Changellings, spirits, even wraiths, all of them seem to be not just affected by Consensus - but HEAVILY affected.<br /> <br /> That's also valid for Demons - they are FAITH dependent after all, aren't they?<br /> <br /> And for others - again, there is no ultimate truth. Just your headcannon, which you are Absolutely incapable of admiting that is just your own personal view, and not the ultimate Cannon truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:05:41-08:00","id":1047914,"title":"","content":"In fact, you can find a few hints of Consensus working on the other nightfolk now that I came to think about it... Other than Changellings, spirits and wraiths (which are BLATANTLY affected), you have flaws like &quot;alergic to garlic&quot; or &quot;alergic to crosses&quot; that are a clear sign of being &quot;affected by Consensus&quot; of sorts (again, I'm not putting it on stone, I'm simply stating those facts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:23:24-08:00","id":1047920,"title":"","content":"Once again, more shouting, less evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:34:18-08:00","id":1047933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047908#post1047908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a strong headcannon, but it's funny that you would use CHANGELLINGS as &quot;proof&quot; of supernaturals that <i>can't be changed by Consensus</i>.<br /> <br /> If anything, Changellings are LIVING PROOF of the POWER OF CONSENSUS.<br /> <br /> Changellings are what remains of the true fae of old, that had to parasite human souls to remain on Earth... That's basically the changelling way. And why? Yep, that's right... Because of the change of the Consensus, that doesn't believe in fairies any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the consensus. Banality, a cold force of unmaking and bleakness. Mage's consensus isn't the same thing as Banality, notably because one of the reasons that fae had to do this, according to Darkening Sky, I think, was because they basically started dropping Banality bombs on each other via use of religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits? Oh please... Spirits have become all but bygones... When once it were simple for them to cause trouble, now... Unable to remain in the material world - Consensus courtesy. </div> </div> </div>Spirits and Bygones aren't the same, either. Spirits can give the gauntlet - which is maintained by the Weavers via Pattern Spiders, and not humans - the finger if their Gnosis is high enough, and they don't have to worry about this &quot;thaumivory&quot; thing, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:55:45-08:00","id":1047956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047933#post1047933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not the consensus. Banality, a cold force of unmaking and bleakness. Mage's consensus isn't the same thing as Banality, notably because one of the reasons that fae had to do this, according to Darkening Sky, I think, was because they basically started dropping Banality bombs on each other via use of religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what is banality?<br /> <br /> About religion... What is religion on the Mage setting?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047933#post1047933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits and Bygones aren't the same, either. Spirits can give the gauntlet - which is maintained by the Weavers via Pattern Spiders, and not humans - the finger if their Gnosis is high enough, and they don't have to worry about this &amp;quot;thaumivory&amp;quot; thing, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>In WtA perhaps.<br /> But this is a discussion about Mage.<br /> In Mage (as it is in WtA), the Gauntlet is stronger in urban areas. And, in a Tecnocratic lab, it can be about 9-10.<br /> That's almost taboo for the majority of spirits to affect the material world.<br /> The same goes for wraiths - the stronger is the the &quot;technocratic Consensus&quot;, the harder is the shroud, so, the harder it is for wraiths to do their stuff.<br /> <br /> Once again, that's not explicit said in Wraith the Oblivion for example, but it is said that the shroud is &quot;stronger on science labs&quot; (guess what a techie's construct is?). The same for spirits.<br /> <br /> So, the actual fact remains - the stronger the tech Consensus, the less supernaturals.<br /> <br /> About changellings, the technocratic Consensus has always been a major force of banality. That's the <i>byproduct</i> of it.<br /> <br /> About your pattern spiders - WtA does NOT concern itself about Consensus. The pattern spiders are spirits - and usually, spirits don't just &quot;appear&quot; out of the blue. They are context-wise. So, if I have a bunch of pattern spiders around that Technocratic amalgam... Hum... I wonder why....<br /> <br /> So no, in a Mage view, the spiders are the symptons, not the causes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:57:21-08:00","id":1047960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047956#post1047956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what is banality?<br /> <br /> About religion... What is religion on the Mage setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something different to what it is in Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In WtA perhaps.<br /> But this is a discussion about Mage. </div> </div> </div>Guess which game introduced it and had it as an actual integral part of it rather than an add on &quot;I guess we can go there&quot; optional part of the game? That's right, it was Werewolf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:00:15-08:00","id":1047961,"title":"","content":"Weaver-related spirits invert the Gauntlet. So an Ananassi or Pattern Spider can cross the Shroud far more easily thanks to the Technocracy. Just sayin'. Consensus doesn't consistently matter to other Supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:00:23-08:00","id":1047962,"title":"","content":"One more thing: spirits are subjected to disbelief. At least in Mage. Your WtA view is not for MtA however. Weird, paradoxical spirits, will lose essence over time, until being forced away back to Umbra. So... Yes, the power of Consensus stands still","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:07:13-08:00","id":1047967,"title":"","content":"Wraiths love Union labs, they gives them so many toys to inhabit and to destroy to bring over to the other side and they just love to possess Mages with Puppetry because they get to follow them to other Umbra Realms (Wraith Player's Guide, p. 147).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T18:33:40-08:00","id":1048016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047900#post1047900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can point you to the existence of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Possessed, Sorcerers, Spirits, Wraiths, etc as evidence of a Fundamental Reality that Mages cannot change through changing the Consensus. In the case of Sorcerers, you have magical practitioners that can shut down Mages because they have superior forms of countermagic, which suggests that Numina aligns better with Fundamental Reality than Spheres (plus the complete lack of Paradox). And the Paradigm of the Mage or Sorcerer does not matter, Sorcerers still get to say 'no' to Mages better than Mages get to say 'no' to Sorcerers (Sorcerers get to say 'no' to a lot of things).</div> </div> </div> </div>While not an entirely sensible interpretation, one could interpret Format Space's wording as effecting ALL magic outside of Hypertech.<br /> <br /> Meaning Vampire powers and their ilk would count as vulgar True Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T05:32:45-08:00","id":1048198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1047904#post1047904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only point I see is a lot of shouting. Shouting does not make a point any more valid, it just makes it louder. If there is an absolute Consensus, it does not effect anything but Mages because the rest of the Nightfolk do not seem to care. In fact, Mages might not want to advertise that weakness because Kindred and KJ might figure out how to manipulate humanity in such a way that the Consensus turns so against Mages that the lot of them find themselves banished beyond the Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other game lines do not get to dictate rules to Mage, nor does Mage get to dictate terms to them. If Wraith says something that conflicts with Mage's setting or theme, Mage wins (for Mage games anyways). That's common sense. It's also stated explicitly.<br /> <br /> Subjective Reality, however it actually works, is one of the themes of Mage; it goes to the very heart of Mage's postmodernist bent. It does not play very well with other game lines or histories. Often those games have to contradict Mage just to maintain their own themes but that makes no difference to Mage. Cite Changeling or Werewolf all you want, they may even be informative, but if there is a contradiction, Mage wins.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Mage has to be 100% Subjective Reality*, but it does mean that we can reject anything from other lines that say it can't be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T08:23:49-08:00","id":1048252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can point you to the existence of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Possessed, Sorcerers, Spirits, Wraiths, etc as evidence of a Fundamental Reality that Mages cannot change through changing the Consensus. In the case of Sorcerers, you have magical practitioners that can shut down Mages because they have superior forms of countermagic, which suggests that Numina aligns better with Fundamental Reality than Spheres (plus the complete lack of Paradox). And the Paradigm of the Mage or Sorcerer does not matter, Sorcerers still get to say 'no' to Mages better than Mages get to say 'no' to Sorcerers (Sorcerers get to say 'no' to a lot of things).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth to point out that, while you can do that, and that's a valid interpretation of the lore (and my perspective on WoD it's similar, albeit I don't put the Sorcerers in the same bag), in the canon lore of Mage there are plenty of perfectly reasonable explanations about why and how all these phenomena are, in fact, created by the Consensus. Like saying that the supernatural creatures/powers work because humans have a subconscious belief in them, and/or that the supernaturals pay their Paradox in the form of their Banes (and Sorcerers by being unable to use magic in front of unbelievers, which it's optional but canon, and goes well with this approach).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other game lines do not get to dictate rules to Mage, nor does Mage get to dictate terms to them. If Wraith says something that conflicts with Mage's setting or theme, Mage wins (for Mage games anyways). That's common sense. It's also stated explicitly.<br /> <br /> Subjective Reality, however it actually works, is one of the themes of Mage; it goes to the very heart of Mage's postmodernist bent. It does not play very well with other game lines or histories. Often those games have to contradict Mage just to maintain their own themes but that makes no difference to Mage. Cite Changeling or Werewolf all you want, they may even be informative, but if there is a contradiction, Mage wins.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Mage has to be 100% Subjective Reality*, but it does mean that we can reject anything from other lines that say it can't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. While I don't believe in a 100% Subjective Reality, I do agree in that the door for that interpretation of the canon material it's open, it's just that it doesn't mix well with the canon of other gamelines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-13-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T17:16:12-08:00","id":1048489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048198#post1048198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other game lines do not get to dictate rules to Mage, nor does Mage get to dictate terms to them. If Wraith says something that conflicts with Mage's setting or theme, Mage wins (for Mage games anyways). That's common sense. It's also stated explicitly.<br /> <br /> Subjective Reality, however it actually works, is one of the themes of Mage; it goes to the very heart of Mage's postmodernist bent. It does not play very well with other game lines or histories. Often those games have to contradict Mage just to maintain their own themes but that makes no difference to Mage. Cite Changeling or Werewolf all you want, they may even be informative, but if there is a contradiction, Mage wins.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that Mage has to be 100% Subjective Reality*, but it does mean that we can reject anything from other lines that say it can't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although (and I'm writing this as a shamelessly pro-crossover fan), when I have an explanation which doesn't contradict the other lines and one which does, I choose the former, because, well, Occam's razor. An explanation which have to ignore too much things from the wider WoD is less likely in my eyes than one that enables more things.<br /> <br /> Yes that approach comes from the viewpoint that the gamelines aren't existing in their own exclusive universe, but parts of the larger communal setting instead. I know, the preferences of authors on this was different, but I think the official approach to the setting was closer to mine, with the exclamation that you always exclude things if you want, or rather you don't <i>have</i> to use the other lines' books. Nevertheless, the majority books of every line were written with the other lines in mind and referred again and again, I think. For example, Wraith is being referred in the Euthanatos tradbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T19:17:19-08:00","id":1048537,"title":"","content":"Heck, everything is mentioned in KotE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T01:56:06-08:00","id":1048632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048489#post1048489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although (and I'm writing this as a shamelessly pro-crossover fan), when I have an explanation which doesn't contradict the other lines and one which does, I choose the former, because, well, Occam's razor. An explanation which have to ignore too much things from the wider WoD is less likely in my eyes than one that enables more things.<br /> <br /> Yes that approach comes from the viewpoint that the gamelines aren't existing in their own exclusive universe, but parts of the larger communal setting instead. I know, the preferences of authors on this was different, but I think the official approach to the setting was closer to mine, with the exclamation that you always exclude things if you want, or rather you don't <i>have</i> to use the other lines' books. Nevertheless, the majority books of every line were written with the other lines in mind and referred again and again, I think. For example, Wraith is being referred in the Euthanatos tradbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Euthanatos have zero to say about Stygia, the Technocracy is largely close to non existent in EVERY other games, and the only game where technology is Magik! and Science is just a mamboo jamboo, just as valid as astrology, only in Mage. So, no, each line is its own; those few hints about the others are not to make it a single, coherent and organic integrated world, but rather to allow for the connection, in case it is desired. However, you WON'T see a super Camarilla waging gang wars against the Sabbat everywhere in a Mage game, and even if you do, the Technocracy will be there on many times (in a Vampire game, the Technocracy will NEVER interfere). Also, the role of Consensus is also a Mage only thing. Subjective reality too.<br /> <br /> When playing werewolf, you'll use THEIR Umbra. And with Mage, it's Umbra. And so on. So no, it doesn't matter what other splats say about any one splat actually.<br /> <br /> In truth, Mage wouldn't exist at all if the other splats were to be taken with more authority than Mage itself. There would be no Technocracy, no Consensus reality shaped, no Horizon Realms, no technology as magik, and so, no ascension war","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T03:44:41-08:00","id":1048654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048632#post1048632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In truth, Mage wouldn't exist at all if the other splats were to be taken with more authority than Mage itself. There would be no Technocracy, no Consensus reality shaped, no Horizon Realms, no technology as magik, and so, no ascension war </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in your reasoning behind this point.<br /> Would you mind to elaborate on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:35:49-08:00","id":1048693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048489#post1048489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although (and I'm writing this as a shamelessly pro-crossover fan), when I have an explanation which doesn't contradict the other lines and one which does, I choose the former, because, well, Occam's razor. An explanation which have to ignore too much things from the wider WoD is less likely in my eyes than one that enables more things.<br /> <br /> Yes that approach comes from the viewpoint that the gamelines aren't existing in their own exclusive universe, but parts of the larger communal setting instead. I know, the preferences of authors on this was different, but I think the official approach to the setting was closer to mine, with the exclamation that you always exclude things if you want, or rather you don't <i>have</i> to use the other lines' books. Nevertheless, the majority books of every line were written with the other lines in mind and referred again and again, I think. For example, Wraith is being referred in the Euthanatos tradbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's fair, and an intuitive path to take if you do a lot of crossovers. Other game lines can be great inspiration for what Mage can be, they just have no say at all on what it can't be. Hence why when the authors mine other lines for ideas they pass them through a filter so that Werewolf doesn't have accept the existence of God and Caine, nor Vampire Gaea, nor Mage Objective Reality. One of Mage's filters, for example, is the Mythic Threads.<br /> <br /> From that angle, I don't find there is much I have to throw out. It's not the existence of Wraiths, nor the powers of Wraiths, nor the history of Wraiths that is a problem for Mage. The only problem is that Wraith was written with the assumption of an objective reality, and that's not a hard element to strip out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:09:48-08:00","id":1048958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048654#post1048654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested in your reasoning behind this point.<br /> Would you mind to elaborate on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy is an overwhelming presence in Mage; they've literaly built the modern world. Yet, in the other splats they are nonexistent; the presence of such an organization would have a <i>massive</i> impact on those scenarios. In VtM and even WtA, at tops, outside the regular foes (Sabbat, Independent clans, anarchists, Camarilla, rivals inside the sect, or the Wyrm paws for Werewolf, and the eventual Weaver or spirit foe beside rival Garou or Fera), the most you could expect would be a mortal Hunter, or some Hunter organization like the inquisition. There is no vast conspiracy of Mages with vast resources on top of it's supernatural capacities hunting kindred or Garou in those games. Tipically at least. You can make it, of course, but that's not how the scenario truly works for those lines.<br /> <br /> There is no such a thing as &quot;Consensus&quot; for the other lines either. Nor do they have subjective realities. In fact, there isn't even the effort about it. Werewolf has an Umbral landscape with an objective reality; no Horizon Realms on those. The Umbra for Mage can't even be the same, otherwise the game won't function too well.<br /> <br /> The other splats don't present technology as inherently magic either; that's a Mage exclusively thing too. On contrary, technologies on many occasions are presented as anti-magic, as a &quot;weaver-thing&quot; that supress all the wonders of magic.<br /> <br /> The other splats pay no concern about humans beliefs; it isn't important at all. To Mage, it is the most important thing.<br /> <br /> To truly mix all splats... Well, first of all, you'd have to take many of the MAGE and put it above the rest. Meaning: yes, Hit Marks hunt down those sabbat cotteries when they find them. Yes, technology is magik. And yes, belief shapes reality. Without that overriding of the other splats, you're not really making crossovers with Mages, you're just putting humans with spheres as interesting NPCs or PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:19:51-08:00","id":1048993,"title":"","content":"Or you can just rule that Mages are uniquely vulnerable to the effects of the Consensus and their perceptions of everything are subjective because of the filters of their Avatars and their Paradigms. The contradictions go away at that point because the other supernatural creatures do not suffer the same limitations and can exploit the weaknesses of the subjective perceptions of Mages. Other supernatural creatures just shrug when Technocrats claim that technology is 'magick' and shoot the Mages with the 'magickal' firearms that the Mages claim to have created through manipulating the Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:53:35-08:00","id":1049011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048993#post1048993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can just rule that Mages are uniquely vulnerable to the effects of the Consensus and their perceptions of everything are subjective because of the filters of their Avatars and their Paradigms. The contradictions go away at that point because the other supernatural creatures do not suffer the same limitations and can exploit the weaknesses of the subjective perceptions of Mages. Other supernatural creatures just shrug when Technocrats claim that technology is 'magick' and shoot the Mages with the 'magickal' firearms that the Mages claim to have created through manipulating the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's kind of dumb and makes no sense whatsoever in ANY setting. &quot;Oh, these Avatars which every human has, for some reason allows these particular humans to warp reality with their perceptions, but not these other humans and oh we vampires don't have them, and they're kind of like souls but not really and if they really ARE the corpses of angels like that infernalist said, We did kill him by the way yes? Good. Anyway, if they ARE the corpses of angels where did all the extra ones come from? I mean, the existence of Barrabi, kind of means these 'avatars' are re-used, but the earths population is several times over what it used to be, if they were just being re-used, there wouldn't be enough for everyone. But everyone has one, which implies there were more coming from somewhere. But if there were just more around waiting their turn, why would Barrabi exist? The chances of that particular Avatar coming back would be tiny.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it really doesn't get any better if you try to involve werewolf cosmology because werewolf cosmology is stupidly objective.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the idea that the other creatures were simply slipped into the consensus in a past age by someone or another making them as 'mundane' as guns or cars.... I mean noone uses swords anymore, but if someone stabs you with one they don't garner paradox. Just because something has fallen out of common thought or active belief doesn't mean it's not there.....<br /> <br /> Well, reality is consensual. And Reality has inertia. It will mostly stay the same unless someone makes a deliberate effort to sway the consensus. It used to be that noone really bothered with this. And so, pretty much anything could happen because there was no unified consensus. People believed all kinds of crazy shit.<br /> <br /> Besides, if, as is implied by certain things, Kinfolk, ghouls, and Kithain have Avatars.... well then. They strongly believe in Vampires, Werewolves and Fae. And most people don't actively believe much of anything about them, but they don't DISBELIEVE either. They just.... don't think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:56:03-08:00","id":1049013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048632#post1048632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Euthanatos have zero to say about Stygia, the Technocracy is largely close to non existent in EVERY other games, and the only game where technology is Magik! and Science is just a mamboo jamboo, just as valid as astrology, only in Mage. So, no, each line is its own; those few hints about the others are not to make it a single, coherent and organic integrated world, but rather to allow for the connection, in case it is desired. However, you WON'T see a super Camarilla waging gang wars against the Sabbat everywhere in a Mage game, and even if you do, the Technocracy will be there on many times (in a Vampire game, the Technocracy will NEVER interfere). Also, the role of Consensus is also a Mage only thing. Subjective reality too.<br /> <br /> When playing werewolf, you'll use THEIR Umbra. And with Mage, it's Umbra. And so on. So no, it doesn't matter what other splats say about any one splat actually.<br /> <br /> In truth, Mage wouldn't exist at all if the other splats were to be taken with more authority than Mage itself. There would be no Technocracy, no Consensus reality shaped, no Horizon Realms, no technology as magik, and so, no ascension war</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say, I disagree with every point of this and leave it at there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I see it as the exact opposite. Every game of the World of Darkness is a part of the WoD. Every one of them have the stamp on the books, the lines are cross-referenced, crossover plots, novels, chronicles and plot books were written, etc. You'll only have irresolvable contradictions between the lines if you handle any of the big conspiracies as much more omniscient and omnipresent as they were written. But we had this argument not so long ago and I don't have the inclination to going through it again.<br /> <br /> Go, read the Euthanatos book. It mentions the dual nature of wraiths, even mechanics. It mentions soul-forging, the Tempest, Ferrymen, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-14-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:27:54-08:00","id":1049068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1048993#post1048993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can just rule that Mages are uniquely vulnerable to the effects of the Consensus and their perceptions of everything are subjective because of the filters of their Avatars and their Paradigms. The contradictions go away at that point because the other supernatural creatures do not suffer the same limitations and can exploit the weaknesses of the subjective perceptions of Mages. Other supernatural creatures just shrug when Technocrats claim that technology is 'magick' and shoot the Mages with the 'magickal' firearms that the Mages claim to have created through manipulating the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, your &quot;solution&quot; basically is:<br /> <br /> What others think about - Mages:<br /> <br /> Vampires: &quot;Mages? You see, I know of many malkavians that make more sense them those lunatics. Can you believe that they think my tablet is actually &quot;Magic&quot;? Really, I can't be that insane even with setite drugs&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolves: &quot;Those guys are Wyld encarnated. The kind of nonsense that they'll tell you about the Umbra is staggering - really, even a Vortex makes more sense than a Mage<br /> <br /> Changellings: &quot;Mages? Honey, Bedlam makes more sense than a Mage. You see, we are affected by banality, but they are affected by ANY bullshit that you could think of! Really, the Far Dream is more coherent than a Mage, I swear to you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your solution just turned Mages, from the enlightened ones of the WoD, to the most fringe lunatic group of critters, that believe in ridiculous stuff (without any good reason), have a deep level of schizofreniac psychotic perception of reality, and yet hold a huge amount of power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:45:42-08:00","id":1049076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049013#post1049013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say, I disagree with every point of this and leave it at there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I see it as the exact opposite. Every game of the World of Darkness is a part of the WoD. Every one of them have the stamp on the books, the lines are cross-referenced, crossover plots, novels, chronicles and plot books were written, etc. You'll only have irresolvable contradictions between the lines if you handle any of the big conspiracies as much more omniscient and omnipresent as they were written. But we had this argument not so long ago and I don't have the inclination to going through it again.<br /> <br /> Go, read the Euthanatos book. It mentions the dual nature of wraiths, even mechanics. It mentions soul-forging, the Tempest, Ferrymen, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum... Ok, where was the Technocracy, or even better, were was the bloodthirst Order of Reason during the anarchist revolt that led to the rise of the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Where was the Garou nation when a group of Mages started strenghtening the Gauntlet, and started hunting down to extinction several bygones and spirits all over the world?<br /> <br /> How the hell haven't the Garou nation noticed all those Mages filling the world with their magikal Weaver creations? (Not to mention the Wyrm taint that followed).<br /> <br /> How haven't the Tremere noticed the incredible magical potential of all those new magical toys that humans were producing without even realizing? (By the way, auspex should suffice to few the Magic on the mundane technologies).<br /> <br /> How the hell haven't werewolves notice that the changes on Consensus would affect the spirits connection to the material world? How the hell haven't the Tremere noticed any change in magic that the change of Consensus brought?<br /> <br /> And... Changellings? They should be swore enemies of the technocrats! Those guys more than any other should now how the Consensus affects reality... However, they don't. They don't see banality as the passive desbelief, but rather as a sort of active force of dulness, of lack of imagination. <br /> <br /> About wraiths... This is a game without too much impact on others, wraith actually is probably the easist to do crossover with. The fact it is an entire other world alltogether may help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T19:00:20-08:00","id":1049083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049068#post1049068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, your &quot;solution&quot; basically is:<br /> <br /> What others think about - Mages:<br /> <br /> Vampires: &quot;Mages? You see, I know of many malkavians that make more sense them those lunatics. Can you believe that they think my tablet is actually &quot;Magic&quot;? Really, I can't be that insane even with setite drugs&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolves: &quot;Those guys are Wyld encarnated. The kind of nonsense that they'll tell you about the Umbra is staggering - really, even a Vortex makes more sense than a Mage<br /> <br /> Changellings: &quot;Mages? Honey, Bedlam makes more sense than a Mage. You see, we are affected by banality, but they are affected by ANY bullshit that you could think of! Really, the Far Dream is more coherent than a Mage, I swear to you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Your solution just turned Mages, from the enlightened ones of the WoD, to the most fringe lunatic group of critters, that believe in ridiculous stuff (without any good reason), have a deep level of schizofreniac psychotic perception of reality, and yet hold a huge amount of power</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. you understand my position on Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T19:04:53-08:00","id":1049087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049083#post1049083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. you understand my position on Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must then, understand why I view your position on mages to be objectively terrible. Since positing Mage as the 'oververse' to the rest allows the others to come through unharmed and un-diluted, you have instead decided to deliberately maim the MAGE version of the WoD because reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T20:03:15-08:00","id":1049105,"title":"","content":"It is not maimed, it is clarified. Subjective viewpoints can exist within an objective reality but objective perspectives cannot exist within a subjective reality. The nature of the subjective perspectives of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Mage, Wraiths, etc can exist in an objective reality (much like the subjective perceptions of individual humans can exist within an objective world) because there are common foundations to reality. In a subjective reality, however, the powerful groups are more correct than the powerless groups because their perceptions are dominant.<br /> <br /> In an objective reality, slavery is wrong and has always been wrong, regardless of the opinions of the powerful groups, because slavery oppresses human being with innate rights. In a subjective reality , however, slavery is right when the powerful groups say it is right and wrong when the powerful groups say it is wrong, and when the powerful groups say slavery is right, slaves are subhumans that have no rights. The objective reality just makes more sense, from an ethical (and a scientific viewpoint), than a subjective reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T20:18:21-08:00","id":1049110,"title":"","content":"Except objective ethics are nonsense. There are subjective ethics to be sure. But it's not written into the base laws of reality that murder is wrong and you will be punished for it. Noone has innate rights. We have whatever rights we, or others on our behalf, can enforce.<br /> <br /> And Objective perspectives can TOTALLY exist within a subjective reality. That's the whole point. You simply have many perspectives alongside one another rather than a single universal perspective that all see from different angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T21:37:47-08:00","id":1049138,"title":"","content":"You cannot have objective perceptions within a subjective reality because a subjective reality cannot support anything that is objective. Objectivity requires a foundamental framework from which everyyhing can be measuered, which is logically impossible within a subjective reality. Subjective realities can only support subjective perceptions and, because of the subjective nature of reality, the powerful groups are right and the powerless groups are wrong.<br /> <br /> Perceptions are always subjective because of the inherent limitations of biology and cognition. Objective perceptions require infinite cognition in order to properly understand everything. Subjective perceptions can be supported by an objective reality but objective perceptions cannot be supported by a subjective reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:55:54-08:00","id":1049232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049110#post1049110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except objective ethics are nonsense. There are subjective ethics to be sure. But it's not written into the base laws of reality that murder is wrong and you will be punished for it. Noone has innate rights. We have whatever rights we, or others on our behalf, can enforce.<br /> <br /> And Objective perspectives can TOTALLY exist within a subjective reality. That's the whole point. You simply have many perspectives alongside one another rather than a single universal perspective that all see from different angles.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049138#post1049138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot have objective perceptions within a subjective reality because a subjective reality cannot support anything that is objective. Objectivity requires a foundamental framework from which everyyhing can be measuered, which is logically impossible within a subjective reality. Subjective realities can only support subjective perceptions and, because of the subjective nature of reality, the powerful groups are right and the powerless groups are wrong.<br /> <br /> Perceptions are always subjective because of the inherent limitations of biology and cognition. Objective perceptions require infinite cognition in order to properly understand everything. Subjective perceptions can be supported by an objective reality but objective perceptions cannot be supported by a subjective reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, hold up here a second. I'm almost certain you aren't using the same definitions. Even if you are, I suggest you define your terms before you go on. It can't hurt and it will probably help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:16:12-08:00","id":1049242,"title":"","content":"Objective reality is a reality based on consistent (if unknown) principles that can be approximately described through a scientific method. It does not matter if the scientific method is animist or materialist in perspective as long as the results are reasonably accurate and reasonably valid. Subjective reality is reality without consistent principles.<br /> <br /> Objective perceptions are a hypothetical omniscient and omnipresent state where everything is known and understood (the perception of 'God'). While it is a useful hypothetical construct for explaining an objective reality, it does not exist at the human-level. Subjective perceptions are perceptions that are bounded by innate limitations. Humans have subjective perceptions because our sensory organs evolved to sense specific forms of information and each of our brains have finite capabilities related to analyzing, extrapolating, forecasting, interpreting, and storing sensory information. <br /> <br /> In effect, humans have two major limitations when it comes to perception. We use instruments to attempt to attempt to circumvent our biological limitations (with a limited amount of success) and the scientific method to attempt to circumvent our cognitive limitations (once again, with a limited amount of success). <br /> <br /> Mages gain an extra nine senses with their Avatars (the Nine Spheres) but do not gain improved cognition, which is why they suffer from the same subjective perceptions as normal humans. While they have circumvented some of their biological limitations, they have overwhelmed their cognitive limitations, and the Spheres also make them vulnerable to the Consensus. In effect, Mages gain more information, which allows them to manipulate reality, but they do not gain better information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:35:50-08:00","id":1049531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049105#post1049105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not maimed, it is clarified. Subjective viewpoints can exist within an objective reality but objective perspectives cannot exist within a subjective reality. The nature of the subjective perspectives of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Mage, Wraiths, etc can exist in an objective reality (much like the subjective perceptions of individual humans can exist within an objective world) because there are common foundations to reality. In a subjective reality, however, the powerful groups are more correct than the powerless groups because their perceptions are dominant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly agreeing with that. The following discussion is interesting too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In an objective reality, slavery is wrong and has always been wrong, regardless of the opinions of the powerful groups, because slavery oppresses human being with innate rights. In a subjective reality , however, slavery is right when the powerful groups say it is right and wrong when the powerful groups say it is wrong, and when the powerful groups say slavery is right, slaves are subhumans that have no rights. The objective reality just makes more sense, from an ethical (and a scientific viewpoint), than a subjective reality. </div> </div> </div>I won't take any ethical sensibility as objectively right or wrong. I understand your anti-oppression viewpoint and in general I agree, slavery is wrong, from a modern moral standpoint. However, you can't go back, for example to the Roman Empire and say &quot;you're wrong&quot;, when there wasn't a notion of Human Rights and the whole question of slavery was much more nuanced than most people usually imagine.<br /> <br /> Ethics aren't rules of the universe (or objective reality) I think. They are something we collectively <i>decide. </i>Taking <i>any </i>ethics as objectively true is the same thought process as, well, religions, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:38:25-08:00","id":1049532,"title":"","content":"Plato wrote about the evils of slavery, so it is not like the Romans did not understand the abuses of the system, they just did not care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:42:05-08:00","id":1049570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049532#post1049532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plato wrote about the evils of slavery, so it is not like the Romans did not understand the abuses of the system, they just did not care.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no objective morality. Unless you're a theist and believe that some cosmic etherial intelligence that created the universe out of a bucket filled with nothing just delivered to us all the random stuff that he likes/dislikes in a clay stone for us to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:44:33-08:00","id":1049571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049532#post1049532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plato wrote about the evils of slavery, so it is not like the Romans did not understand the abuses of the system, they just did not care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firs off, every system is prone to abuse (and will be abused, but that's my inner cynicism speaking).<br /> <br /> Secondly, here are some links on the topic:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/2180538?seq=1#page_scan_tab_contents\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.jstor.org/stable/2180538...n_tab_contents</a><br /> <a href=\"http://philosophy.stackexchange.com/questions/468/what-were-platos-view-on-slavery-in-particular-with-respect-to-his-proposed-ut\" target=\"_blank\">http://philosophy.stackexchange.com/...is-proposed-ut</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/ethics/slavery/ethics/philosophers_1.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/staticarchive/2e00d1d53e9c3bd91993196aa19a1d88589969f0.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/ethics/slavery/ethics/philosophers_1.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"> BBC - Ethics - Slavery: Philosophers justifying slavery </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/ethics/slavery/ethics/philosophers_1.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.bbc.co.uk/ethics/slavery/ethics/philosophers_1.shtml </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Some historical philosophers sought to justify slavery, not necessarily from selfish intentions. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I want to stress that I'm not saying slavery is okay, I'm just saying modern ethics, worldviews and expectations aren't applicable backward in time and that topics like slavery were far more nuanced than we tend to think today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:49:05-08:00","id":1049575,"title":"","content":"You can be an atheist and believe in an objective human-specific ethical system based on the fact that all humans belong to the same species. In fact, you can be a spiritual atheist (as opposed to a material atheist) who believes that the hundreds of billions to trillions of human dead judge the souls of the newly dead based on such an objective ethical system. If you believe in a spiritual atheist afterlife, where the ancient dead judge the recent dead on their action by such an objective ethics, then religion does not matter because no diety will ever judge the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:00:48-08:00","id":1049585,"title":"","content":"However, that is, as I wrote above, the same <i>thought process</i> as a religious person's, because it basically says there IS an objective ethical and judging system, which we have zero proof of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:01:55-08:00","id":1049586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049571#post1049571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firs off, every system is prone to abuse (and will be abused, but that's my inner cynicism speaking).<br /> <br /> Secondly, here are some links on the topic:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/2180538?seq=1#page_scan_tab_contents\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.jstor.org/stable/2180538...n_tab_contents</a><br /> <a href=\"http://philosophy.stackexchange.com/questions/468/what-were-platos-view-on-slavery-in-particular-with-respect-to-his-proposed-ut\" target=\"_blank\">http://philosophy.stackexchange.com/...is-proposed-ut</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/ethics/slavery/ethics/philosophers_1.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bbc.co.uk/ethics/slavery/...ophers_1.shtml</a><br /> <br /> I want to stress that I'm not saying slavery is okay, I'm just saying modern ethics, worldviews and expectations aren't applicable backward in time and that topics like slavery were far more nuanced than we tend to think today.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first is ignoring the example of the Meno, where Socrates shows the inherent equality of the slave to the master in intellect, as well as the examples throughout the rest of Plato's works where Socrates illustrates the corruption of the soul that occurs from people becoming dependent on slaves. The second one is an incorrect interpretation of the Republic, which is analogy of the soul, not an outline for a government. The third is a quote taken out of context from a discussion of the morality of rhetoric, where Socrates is using the analogy of physical force to show the immorality of rhetorical force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-15-2017, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:57:03-08:00","id":1049620,"title":"","content":"Now, I'd have to do extensive reading (since classical philosophy is not my field of study, apart from a cursory interest) to go further with this conversation, so I leave the discussion of Plato's works to those with applicable knowledge. I hope something will come out of it, because it (I mean the view on slavery by contemporary authors) is indeed a very interesting topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T18:17:08-08:00","id":1049628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049575#post1049575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be an atheist and believe in an objective human-specific ethical system based on the fact that all humans belong to the same species. In fact, you can be a spiritual atheist (as opposed to a material atheist) who believes that the hundreds of billions to trillions of human dead judge the souls of the newly dead based on such an objective ethical system. If you believe in a spiritual atheist afterlife, where the ancient dead judge the recent dead on their action by such an objective ethics, then religion does not matter because no diety will ever judge the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have superstitious beliefs without believing in deities, sure. There is, however, zero evidences of such. And there are a few atheist religions - buddhism being the most know of them, but not the only one. They are still religions however, based on the same kind of magical thinking. <br /> <br /> By a skeptical rational view of the world (as opposed to the emotional magical thinking of religions and superstitions), there is no objective morality or ethics.<br /> <br /> Hell, you can try to find any kind of morality in the natural world. It's nonexistant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T18:40:17-08:00","id":1049639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049628#post1049628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can have superstitious beliefs without believing in deities, sure. There is, however, zero evidences of such. And there are a few atheist religions - buddhism being the most know of them, but not the only one. They are still religions however, based on the same kind of magical thinking.<br /> <br /> By a skeptical rational view of the world (as opposed to the emotional magical thinking of religions and superstitions), there is no objective morality or ethics.<br /> <br /> Hell, you can try to find any kind of morality in the natural world. It's nonexistant</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on the religion part.<br /> <br /> As for nature and ethics, weeeeeel, I'd agree nature doesn't have objective ethics, but animals could do things which need empathy and compassion and such without real positive effects on their lives. However, I think, for ethics, you'd need sentience so, for as long as we haven't figured out how to converse with dolphins... yes, it seems ethics is a purely human thing.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I think Pratchett is applicable here: <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/583655-hogfather\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/583655-hogfather</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:21:19-08:00","id":1049817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049575#post1049575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be an atheist and believe in an objective human-specific ethical system based on the fact that all humans belong to the same species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you please elaborate on this point without references to the supernatural?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:04:21-08:00","id":1049829,"title":"","content":"Human beings belong to one species (with limited genetic diversity), which means that every individual basically shares 99.9% of their genes with every other person. We evolved to create societies, to support each other and to take care of each other, and violations against other human beings are violations against our nature. We have adaptability and exploratory behavior, they are the biological principles that create free will, so we can choose to act against our nature, but we pervert and pollute what we are when we do.<br /> <br /> Societies exist to regulate human behavior in groups larger than our evolution makes us comfortable with, but societies can twist and wrap humans because humans can rationalize exploitative behavior for their own benefit because not enough people recognize their behavior as wrong (evenyually, an entire society can go wrong). Societies that do not stamp down on exploitative behavior rot from the inside becomes the exploitative behavior becomes a cancer where every human being rationalized inhuman actions because every other human being is acting in an inhuman fashion.<br /> <br /> Thus, humans are biological evolved towards compassion and equality, but socialization shapes us from the beginning away from our innocent natures. Humans learn to be human from other humans, so exposure to 'good' humans will likely result in growing up to be 'good' humans and exposure to 'bad' humans will likely result in growing up to be a 'bad' human. Of course, we socialize with many people when we are children, either directly through communication and proximity or indirectly through books, internet, radio, tv, etc. Free will, which is a biological phenomenon, not a spiritual phenomenon, allows us to either return to the goodness of human evolution or devolve to the wickedness of exploitative behavior.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is a skeleton explanation because we have limited space. The basic concepts expressed are grounded in biological evolution and human psychology. We have evolved with one universal ethics, which free will and socialization can pervert, which is based on our evolution and which is dependent on the groups that we were evolved to encounter and on us deciding to do the right thing. Deviation from the universal ethics may benefit the individual but it harms the group, so groups have the right and responsibility to correct the exploitative behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:42:17-08:00","id":1049842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049531#post1049531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ethics aren't rules of the universe (or objective reality) I think. They are something we collectively <i>decide. </i>Taking <i>any </i>ethics as objectively true is the same thought process as, well, religions, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is one of those little ironies of life that the statement &quot;No moral stance is objectively better than another&quot; is itself a moral stance. As is any attempt to judge a moral stance by non moral standards. It is pretty much impossible to choose a normative code of ethics without assuming some moral stance is superior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:26:49-08:00","id":1049864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049829#post1049829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human beings belong to one species (with limited genetic diversity), which means that every individual basically shares 99.9% of their genes with every other person. We evolved to create societies, to support each other and to take care of each other, and violations against other human beings are violations against our nature.</div> </div> </div> </div> Apologies to anyone if I'm incorrect, way off. I'm by no means an expert on these topics. Just going off my rather uneducated view on it. It seems like a lot of your following statements go off this point. That because we evolved as social creatures to create societies, that violations against other humans is against our nature. I'm just not sure that's necessarily true. I'd probably agree if perhaps you were trying to relate this on a very local level. But it seems like an overly reaching statement to apply it to all violations against all other humans (outside of societal punishment) as against our nature. I mean, wolves naturally work in packs, but still fight other wolves and packs. Is that inherently against their nature? Not to give another animal as an example, but it seems the most clear of 'creature that evolved to work in a group that still naturally has conflict in and outside of groups.' I might just be missing the point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:09:40-08:00","id":1049881,"title":"","content":"There's also the chimps, who are viciously violent and would explore the woods in gangs and gleefully dismember any other chimp or group of chimps (if they have the numeric superiority) that they find in their path. T<br /> <br /> Saying that *evil* comes from society ignores how violent it's nature, and how some animals enjoy killing, even members of their own race.<br /> <br /> But this in no way prooves that morality it's relative, just that humans inherently wanting the better for their race, and then being trajically corrupted by society it's an ingenuous proposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:25:03-08:00","id":1049888,"title":"","content":"Recorded chimp behavior is not 'natural' because it is the result of tremendous stress put on the chimps due to human behavior (chimp hunting and habitat loss has reduced the chimp population by over 90% since 1900). We are not witnessing a healthy species, we are witnessing the traumatized survivors of a ongoing genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:50:55-08:00","id":1049903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049888#post1049888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recorded chimp behavior is not 'natural' because it is the result of tremendous stress put on the chimps due to human behavior (chimp hunting and habitat loss has reduced the chimp population by over 90% since 1900). We are not witnessing a healthy species, we are witnessing the traumatized survivors of a ongoing genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just from a quick read, that seems a contentious issue.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20150811-do-animals-fight-wars\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cms.bbcearth.com/sites/default/files/2021-02/Homepage_search.jpeg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20150811-do-animals-fight-wars\" target=\"_blank\"> BBC Earth | Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20150811-do-animals-fight-wars\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20150811-do-animals-fight-wars </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Welcome to BBC Earth, a place to explore the natural world through awe-inspiring documentaries, podcasts, stories and more. </div> </div> </div><br /> But I must say, it certainly is an interesting topic. If a bit outside the bounds of this thread and forum. I appreciate the insight regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:59:18-08:00","id":1049907,"title":"","content":"We are an aggressive species, we are predators, but there is little evidence of widespread human-on-human predation until the Neolithic. Even then, the evidence is limited until the Late Neolithic. Climate change and population growth changed human society from a symbiotic relationship with human beings to a parasitic relationship with human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:52:24-08:00","id":1049933,"title":"","content":"I don't think that &quot;there is little evidence of widespread human-on-human predation until the Neolithic&quot; it's enough to proove human innately moral nature. Among other things because there's little evidence of anything before that. It's know that Paleolithic humans had knives. It's speculated that the Neanderthal population went extinct, in part, because because the violent predation of our natural ancestors (that probably shared more in comon with the neanderthal than with us). Of course, evidence it's unconclusive<br /> <br /> And since we've prooved that beings in *natural state* doesn't need to be inherently moral, you should find a strongger evidence than an hipotetical lack of human-to-human violence on our ancestors to proove that there's a &quot;psychological constant&quot; about morality.<br /> <br /> Well, this forum it's not best the medium for this kind of demonstrations (nor to argue agains't them).<br /> <br /> It seems that what was considered moral did changed over the ages. For instance, according to Homeric lore &quot;Killer of Men&quot; was a great praise for ancient Greeks<br /> <br /> Nowdays society abhor killing in greater (and less natural) ways than any other. To the point that many people even condemn the cruelty to other animals (which it's a very common behaviour among hunters of various species). We condemn slavery ( even when we use sweat factories and other kinds of laboral abuse that are quite resemblant to what slavery was) and all of the like. We don't do so because we're closer to *nature* than ancient romans, but because we follow a moral rationale that took centuries in the making, with the toughts of hundreds of phylosophers (and adopting religious practices, too).<br /> <br /> But then, do we relly need to proove that there's an universal underlying morality in order to justify the application of a given methaphysic at our game table?, isn't enough that a given subject it's inmoral to our own society to say that it's inmoral?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-16-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:29:31-08:00","id":1050026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049907#post1049907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are an aggressive species, we are predators, but there is little evidence of widespread human-on-human predation until the Neolithic. Even then, the evidence is limited until the Late Neolithic. Climate change and population growth changed human society from a symbiotic relationship with human beings to a parasitic relationship with human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because before the advent of the agriculture, human populations were too few and too far. That's the only reason.<br /> <br /> Any biology studant however, learns that the WORSE enemy of ANY organism on Earth is another of the same species.<br /> <br /> Just think about it:<br /> <br /> Lions need to struggle for the same territories;<br /> Wolves will eat the same food;<br /> Sea elephants will dispute the same sexual partners.<br /> <br /> There is no fiercer competition than that with your kin. That holds true for any being on earth, from fungi to whales.<br /> <br /> Evolution made humans emphatic towards their equals. We depend on our kin for our survival.<br /> <br /> But that's the key word. EQUALS.<br /> <br /> That means, my tribesmen, my clan, my group.<br /> <br /> The OTHERS however, are dangerous. The outsiders, those are the enemies.<br /> <br /> The other group will kill you for your women, for your food, for your land.<br /> <br /> At the same time that evolution made us empathetic towards those in our group, it also made us xenophobics towards outsiders.<br /> <br /> So, no, all that New Age talk about how the hippie life of the cavemen were harmonious, is just romantic New Age bullshit.<br /> <br /> Do you have any doubts? Well, the precolombian tribal natives of the Americas had genocided several minor groups way before the europeans get here.<br /> <br /> The truth is: the natives were just as brutal, and as bloodthirst, violent and barbaric as the europeans. Or as the paleolitic cavemen.<br /> <br /> Nature is brutal. Period. Any one can paint a heavenly picture of a divine Garden, but that is a fairy tale, no more childish them believing in the cosmic Santa Claus beyond the clouds watching over all the good people. Nature is a nightmarish hell, of pain, and fear and rage, and worse of all, absolute apathy.<br /> <br /> So, no, civilization wasn't the force of corruption of the purity of the human kind. On contrary, we are beggining to try to move away from the barbarism that is the natural condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:03:12-08:00","id":1050045,"title":"","content":"Please, take a look at Hitler, Mao, or Stalin and tell me that they (and a hundred other despots during the 20th century) are not the products of over five thousand years of civilization? Civilization demands despots, genicide, slavery, and war. It is the inevitable result of any human civilization not chained by the focus on human rights, and it is only by chaining civilization with the focus on human rights that we can attempt to avoid despots, genocide, slavery, and war. Otherwise, we just repeat history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:41:32-08:00","id":1050078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050045#post1050045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, take a look at Hitler, Mao, or Stalin and tell me that they (and a hundred other despots during the 20th century) are not the products of over five thousand years of civilization? Civilization demands despots, genicide, slavery, and war. It is the inevitable result of any human civilization not chained by the focus on human rights, and it is only by chaining civilization with the focus on human rights that we can attempt to avoid despots, genocide, slavery, and war. Otherwise, we just repeat history.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are NOT products of the civilization, but of the human nature - the same natural evolutionary force that made us violently xenophobics.<br /> <br /> The only difference between Hitler and Stalin and a cavemen or a medieval men is that Hitler and Stalin had the technological means to kill millions, something the cavemen lacked, but the core motivations remain the same. The scale is a technical matter, not moral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:57:52-08:00","id":1050095,"title":"","content":"No, there is no scientific evidence of your claim that evolution is responsible for xenophobia (if you have any evidence from peer-reviewed academic journals, please share). Hitler, Mao, and Stalin were products of centuries, if not tens of centuries, of civilization, and are the perfect avatars of civilization. The 'murderous' motivation that you talk about seems to be a product of civilization, not a product of human nature, as there is no archeological evidence to support your claims (once again, if you have peer-reviewed journals that support your claims, please share).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T15:39:25-08:00","id":1050117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050095#post1050095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, there is no scientific evidence of your claim that evolution is responsible for xenophobia (if you have any evidence from peer-reviewed academic journals, please share). Hitler, Mao, and Stalin were products of centuries, if not tens of centuries, of civilization, and are the perfect avatars of civilization. The 'murderous' motivation that you talk about seems to be a product of civilization, not a product of human nature, as there is no archeological evidence to support your claims (once again, if you have peer-reviewed journals that support your claims, please share).</div> </div> </div> </div>What Im saying here, actually is very, very old knews. There are extensive studies about that subject on evolutionary psychology. Just type &quot;xenophobia evolution&quot; on Google and you'll see a ton on material about it, I'm not just saying random stuff here, this is well sedimented on the academics.<br /> <br /> If you're curious, here (<a href=\"https://evolution-institute.org/article/xenophobia-in-the-light-of-evolution-on-the-origins-of-anti-immigration-sentiment/\" target=\"_blank\">https://evolution-institute.org/arti...ion-sentiment/</a>) is just a little article about the subject that I found on a quick search, it has a few sources of the studies done around the subject (those are around since the 80's, so it's really old knews), check it out if you wish, or look for others, literature about this subject is abundant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:04:41-08:00","id":1050126,"title":"","content":"I said peer-reviewed academic journals, not a rubber science website. If I want to look at blogs, I will look at blogs, and a blog that cherry picks outdated economic and psychology articles to support an argument that is about anthropology and biology is hardly credible. Yes, chimps raised by civilized human are probably going to emulate the humans who raised them, that is hardly odd. You have not yet provided anthropological (or archeological) or biological evidence to support your positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:00:17-08:00","id":1050153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050126#post1050126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said peer-reviewed academic journals, not a rubber science website. If I want to look at blogs, I will look at blogs, and a blog that cherry picks outdated economic and psychology articles to support an argument that is about anthropology and biology is hardly credible. Yes, chimps raised by civilized human are probably going to emulate the humans who raised them, that is hardly odd. You have not yet provided anthropological (or archeological) or biological evidence to support your positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're gonna make me expose my inner traditionalist... but quite frankly, peer reviewed academic journals are just as capable of being full of shit as anything else. ESPECIALLY in a soft field like sociology and psychology.<br /> <br /> People have waged war for as long as people have had the ability to do so. I say that's pretty strong evidence that war is inherent to our species given the ability to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:03:35-08:00","id":1050158,"title":"","content":"People have waged wars as long as there have been civilizations. Please provide evidence of warfare that occurred in a hunter-gatherer society without contamination from civilized societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:07:23-08:00","id":1050161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050158#post1050158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have waged wars as long as there have been civilizations. Please provide evidence of warfare that occurred in a hunter-gatherer society without contamination from civilized societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Native Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:13:45-08:00","id":1050164,"title":"","content":"Native American possessed extensive agrarian civilization. The Eastern Woodlands civilization maintained extensive trading networks that covered over one million square miles of land and possessed nations with populations equal to that of many of their European compatriots before the European plagues killed 90% of the population. Further south, the Aztec and Maya each possessed scientifically advanced agrarian civilizations, and the Inca and the Amazon civilization were complex agrarian civilizations before European plagues killed 90% of the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:16:52-08:00","id":1050167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050164#post1050164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Native American possessed extensive agrarian civilization. The Eastern Woodlands civilization maintained extensive trading networks that covered over one million square miles of land and possessed nations with populations equal to that of many of their European compatriots before the European plagues killed 90% of the population. Further south, the Aztec and Maya each possessed scientifically advanced agrarian civilizations, and the Inca and the Amazon civilization were complex agrarian civilizations before European plagues killed 90% of the population.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, plenty of them were still hunter gatherers who waged war.<br /> <br /> This isn't even going into the point that your question is inherently biased because in order to KNOW about these things, there had to be some civilized contamination. There is no record of an 'uncontaminated' hunter gatherer society that was utterly peaceful either. There's just a lack of records entirely.<br /> <br /> War is just a thing people do. It's not something that happens because we decided to build our own caves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:21:36-08:00","id":1050169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1049842#post1049842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is one of those little ironies of life that the statement &quot;No moral stance is objectively better than another&quot; is itself a moral stance. As is any attempt to judge a moral stance by non moral standards. It is pretty much impossible to choose a normative code of ethics without assuming some moral stance is superior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, who decides which is objectively better? What external force? IMO that's one of the big selling points of religions, you get an external arbiter of morals and thus, stability.<br /> <br /> If we're the ones deciding, our thought processes are products of our age and civilization just as past ones were products of theirs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:31:25-08:00","id":1050171,"title":"","content":"I'd agree that the &quot;humans are evolved to be non-agressive&quot; is a very biased standpoint. I could understand the appeal of this modern version of &quot;humans are inherently good&quot;, but I don't see any hard evidence. <br /> <br /> That we don't have evidence prior to the neolithic, that could be for a lot of reasons, for example:<br /> <br /> - scarcity of remains<br /> - the low number of human population<br /> - abundance of resources in comparison to the size of the population<br /> <br /> Every example we know from the natural world and from our history tells that no, humans (and animals) are not inherently good, or bad as species. Need and opportunity bring aggression, not the Evil Society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:40:44-08:00","id":1050175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050126#post1050126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said peer-reviewed academic journals, not a rubber science website. If I want to look at blogs, I will look at blogs, and a blog that cherry picks outdated economic and psychology articles to support an argument that is about anthropology and biology is hardly credible. Yes, chimps raised by civilized human are probably going to emulate the humans who raised them, that is hardly odd. You have not yet provided anthropological (or archeological) or biological evidence to support your positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL, sure, I'm sorry for trying to spoil your divine revelations with common scientific knowledge that has been around for decades and yet it haven't reached you, what was I thinking<br /> <br /> Sure, civilization is inherently evil, that's a &quot;scientific&quot; idea uphold by NO ONE. Plus you. Sure.<br /> <br /> How about YOU, from the top of your supremme truth, show ME some peer-reviewed academic jornals supporting your fantastic (and fantasy) idea that chimps raised by &quot;civilized&quot; humans will EMULATE those humans?<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> Show me the peer-reviewed academic jornals that DISQUALIFIES THE DISCIPLINE OF BEHAVIORISM AS A VALID SCIENCE?<br /> <br /> And please, wait a minute because I have to tell my teachers of behaviorism and of ecology and evolution that they should burn their away their PhDs, since their disciplines are a hoax","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:42:58-08:00","id":1050177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050161#post1050161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Native Americans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, africans in tribal stage, polineseans, the australian aborigenous... And EVERY SINGLE group of hunter-gatherers groups.<br /> <br /> Jeez man... I cannot believe Im seeing this being said with all that arrogance...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:58:40-08:00","id":1050186,"title":"","content":"And what's even more ridiculous, that territorial behavior of apes, viciously attacking other groups, is a perfectly regular thing all over the nature. Nothing strange in that. That kind of thing is widely documented, both by observation of groups, as from fossil evidences. And that's not something exclusive to just apes, that's a norm on nature. And yet you'll tell me that it's a human induced behavior LOL LMAO that's rich, I can only laugh at the idea. Tell you what, show me the peer-reviewed paper that says &quot;chimps gangs attacking others are human-induced&quot; LOL<br /> <br /> Really Aya, I don't wanna do this, but you hold your ideas with too much arrogance. You may believe what your saying, and you can believe what you will, and you can stand for what you believe, but you are absolutely wrong about that subject, which by the way is fine, no one is the keeper of thruth, but when you make such statements with not confidence, but arrogance, specially when you're so deeply wrong, you make a fool of yourself. So, there's no need to be so condescending, just relax a bit, ask for sources if you like and debate up to exaustion, but try to recognize when you've done too much.<br /> <br /> You're wrong in this one pal. Give it a little search and you'll see that. There is no shame in that, so just relax bro","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:47:30-08:00","id":1050222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050167#post1050167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, plenty of them were still hunter gatherers who waged war.<br /> <br /> This isn't even going into the point that your question is inherently biased because in order to KNOW about these things, there had to be some civilized contamination. There is no record of an 'uncontaminated' hunter gatherer society that was utterly peaceful either. There's just a lack of records entirely.<br /> <br /> War is just a thing people do. It's not something that happens because we decided to build our own caves.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of them were hunter-gatherer societies without extended contact with civilizations. The majority were agrarian societies, some of which had been practicing agriculture longer than the Europeans, so they were no more hunter-gatherer societies that the 'civilized' nations of Asian or Europe. A minority were hunter-gatherer societies that had prolonged contact with Native American agrarian societies. Since my statement was 'please provide evidence of warfare that occurred in a hunter-gatherer society without contamination from civilized societies', I can only assume that you are willfully ignoring to statement and are just pursuing some other agenda. Oh, if you want evidence of war before historical records, you look at the archeological evidence, since violence leaves fairly consist evidence on the skeletons of the victims regardless of which century the events occurred.<br /> <br /> Let us define hunter-gatherer societies. We will use the common anthropological definition. Hunter-gatherer societies derive their nutrition purely from fishing, gathering, and hunting. Any society that practices horticulture (small scale plant cultivation), pastoralism (animal husbandry of large animals), or agriculture (large scale plant cultivation) is not a hunter-gatherer society. So, no, the vast majority of Native Americans, Tribal Africans, etc were not hunter-gatherer societies. We really do not have any archeological evidence of Australian Aborigine inter-tribal warfare (though I am sure there was interpersonal violence) until the nineteenth century, a century after British colonization of Australia, so they had already been contaminated by contact with a civilization.<br /> <br /> The perspective that war is in innate part of being human is not supported by the anthropological or archaeological evidence. War comes from civilization, that seems to be a rather widespread conclusion from the anthropological and archeological literature. Of course, not every civilization practices war (look at the Amish) but even pacifistic civilizations will hire other civilizations to commit war (look at the Amish hiring Scottish and Irish mercenaries in the 18th century to commit genocide against the Native Americans of Pennsylvania).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:53:28-08:00","id":1050225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1050222#post1050222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The perspective that war is in innate part of being human is not supported by the anthropological or archaeological evidence. War comes from civilization, that seems to be a rather widespread conclusion from the anthropological and archeological literature. Of course, not every civilization practices war (look at the Amish) but even pacifistic civilizations will hire other civilizations to commit war (look at the Amish hiring Scottish and Irish mercenaries in the 18th century to commit genocide against the Native Americans of Pennsylvania).</div> </div> </div> </div>Competition, even violent competition for resources (food, shelter, mating, safety) is part of nature in general, especially in times of scarcity. War is only the institutionalized extension of that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:12:53-08:00","id":1050235,"title":"","content":"No enemy of a Lion will be as terrible as another of it's kind.<br /> <br /> That's one of the most basic lessons from ecology. The worst competitor is another of the same species, always. Thats nature.<br /> <br /> You are confusing things. You seem to think that before agriculture, humans were flower smellers and pacifist hippies. That's a nonsense like I never saw equal before. There are MANY records of violence before agriculture, it just wasn't so common. But the reason is very simple<br /> <br /> - Tiny population - until the agriculture revolution, the global human population was less than a million.<br /> <br /> - Tiny groups - it were impossible to have groups with more than a few hundreds of individuals.<br /> <br /> - Harsher enviroment - it were far easier to die out of accidents, killed by predators or out of thirst/hunger/cold/heat before agricultural age. Agriculture made life safer - which means that, the natural dangers lost some of its importance when compared to the Danger posed by other humans.<br /> <br /> That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:22:07-08:00","id":1050240,"title":"","content":"Yes, lions are much more dangerous to other lions than humans are...wait, how does that make any sense? Let us see your many records of violence before agrarian civilizations. Please do not use Native Americans, Tribal Africans, etc as your examples because I have already outlined how they were agrarian civilizations and not hunter-gatherer societies for thousands of years before European contact. And human populations were much higher before agriculture than one million, that is an old myth based on Victorian archeology, more modern estimates using genetics place the population at around 60 million or so before the beginning of agriculture (the 1,000 fold increase in population having started 70,000 years ago instead of 10,000 years ago [<a href=\"http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0006366]\" target=\"_blank\">http://journals.plos.org/plosone/art....pone.0006366]</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-16-2017, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:40:43-08:00","id":1050519,"title":"","content":"Your link says &quot;page not found&quot;...<br /> <br /> And, as I already stated, you're arguing from a point of negative evidence. There's <a href=\"http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0126589\" target=\"_blank\">evidence of predatory violence among homids far before agrarian civilizations</a> that you want to portray, somehow, as <i>&quot;not evil violence&quot;</i>. Only because the scale, because it was &quot;less&quot;, or because it wasn't &quot;organized&quot;. But that's a very long shot, because you want to prove that evil comes from civilization, not that evil was increased by it (as all human potential was).<br /> One could say that things like cannibalism, fighting for food, or for woman show the kind of violent instincts and lack of emphaty, that, when maximized by the scale and power of a big group of people (hunter-gatherer groups were rather small) could cause all the issues with humanity that you seem to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-17-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}